// Sort My Sites: full research modules with sources. Not legal advice.
export default {"clients":{"title":"Building and hosting client websites, apps and email","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Fact to establish","u":""},{"t":"Why it changes the answer","u":""},{"t":"Question","u":""}],[{"t":"Whose account holds each service: domain, DNS, hosting, database, form backend, mail, analytics","u":""},{"t":"It decides who the vendor's customer is, whose DPA applies and how hard handover is","u":""},{"t":"Q-083, Q-086","u":""}],[{"t":"Whether you can see or change personal data in the client's systems, such as form submissions, mailboxes, databases or logs","u":""},{"t":"If you never touch personal data, you may not be a processor for that client at all","u":""},{"t":"Q-083, Q-085","u":""}],[{"t":"Whether you use any client data for your own purposes, such as a case study, a cross-client dashboard or your own marketing","u":""},{"t":"For that purpose you become a controller, not a processor","u":""},{"t":"Q-084","u":""}],[{"t":"Which plan each vendor account is on, and whether the vendor's DPA binds that exact plan","u":""},{"t":"Some public DPAs cover paid plans only, and some free plans bar commercial use","u":""},{"t":"Q-086","u":""}],[{"t":"Which entities and countries can reach the data, including vendor support and backups","u":""},{"t":"Access from a third country by a separate entity can be a transfer","u":""},{"t":"Q-085, Q-106","u":""}],[{"t":"For each US vendor, whether the exact legal entity is active on the DPF List","u":""},{"t":"DPF adequacy covers only listed organisations","u":""},{"t":"Q-108","u":""}],[{"t":"Whether you can audit, object to a new sub-processor and leave the service in practice","u":""},{"t":"Your DPA promises to the client depend on what your vendors let you do","u":""},{"t":"Q-087","u":""}],[{"t":"Who the client names as controller, and which recipients and transfers its privacy notice lists","u":""},{"t":"The client's notice needs your vendor list to be accurate","u":""},{"t":"Q-071, Q-075","u":""}],[{"t":"Whether you register domains for clients, run DNS for others, or resell either","u":""},{"t":"Some NIS2 categories apply regardless of size","u":""},{"t":"Q-123","u":""}]]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"1. Roles are decided per activity, not per business","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A controller decides why and how personal data is processed. A processor handles it on the controller's behalf. You assess each activity separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The activity involves personal data within GDPR Articles 2 and 3. You identify who decides the purpose, the data types, the recipients and the retention.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A vendor's product category or DPA label does not settle its role. A hosting service that follows instructions is not automatically a joint controller. Roles are functional, so a contract label cannot override what the parties actually decide.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8) and 28(10). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part I, paragraphs 12-13 and 39-41.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"A typical split for a small studio looks like this. It is an inference from the rule above, to test against your own facts.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Activity","u":""},{"t":"Likely role","u":""},{"t":"Why","u":""}],[{"t":"Your own enquiries, client contacts, quotes, invoices and newsletter","u":""},{"t":"Controller","u":""},{"t":"You decide the purpose","u":""}],[{"t":"Building a site with no access to real personal data","u":""},{"t":"Often no processing for the client","u":""},{"t":"Code and design alone are not processing personal data","u":""}],[{"t":"Hosting a client site, form backend or database in your own account","u":""},{"t":"Processor for the client","u":""},{"t":"You hold the data on the client's behalf","u":""}],[{"t":"Maintaining a site, database or mailbox in the client's account with admin access","u":""},{"t":"Processor for the client","u":""},{"t":"Access to personal data is processing","u":""}],[{"t":"Setting up mail for a client and keeping admin rights afterwards","u":""},{"t":"Processor for the client while you keep access","u":""},{"t":"You can reach mailbox content","u":""}],[{"t":"Reusing client leads, visitor data or mail for your own purpose","u":""},{"t":"Controller for that purpose","u":""},{"t":"GDPR Article 28(10) treats a processor that decides purposes as a controller","u":""}],[{"t":"Deciding with the client how a shared tool uses data for both of you","u":""},{"t":"Possibly joint controllers","u":""},{"t":"Joint decisions need an Article 26 arrangement (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-03)","u":""}]]}]},{"h":"2. Processing for a client needs a binding written contract","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Processing for a client must be governed by a contract or other binding legal act. It must be in writing, and electronic form counts. It states the subject, duration, nature and purpose of the processing, the data types, the people affected, and the client's rights and duties.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You process personal data on the client's behalf. The contract names the correct contracting entities and services, and its schedules match the plan and features actually in use. The instructions name the allowed purposes and transfers. Confidentiality and security measures match the processing risk.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What the contract must require.","t":"Documented instructions, including on international transfers. Confidentiality. Article 32 security. Rules for sub-processors. Help with individual rights and with Articles 32 to 36. Return or deletion at the end, at the client's choice. Audit cooperation, and an immediate warning if you think an instruction breaks the GDPR or other EU or national data protection law.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A general privacy notice is not this contract. Article 28 also accepts another binding legal act, though a contract is the usual route. The instruction duty has a statutory exception where law requires the processing, with advance notice unless law forbids it. Copying GDPR wording alone does not show how you implement it. Processor support does not move the client's controller duties onto you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 28(3), opening sentence, and 28(9). Article 28(3)(a)-(d), (e)-(f), (g) and (h) and final subparagraph. EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part II, paragraphs 95-99, 110-114, 125-127 and 130-145.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-06, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-08, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-10.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A starting template.","t":"The Commission adopted standard contractual clauses between controllers and processors under Article 28(7), Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2021/915 of 4 June 2021. Claim id: none in the pack yet (gap). Check the text on EUR-Lex before you use it.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"3. Your client authorises your sub-processors, and you stay liable for them","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"You may use a sub-processor only with the client's prior specific or general written authorisation. Under general authorisation you tell the client about intended additions or replacements and give it a chance to object. The same data protection obligations flow down to each sub-processor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"EDPB reads Article 28(2) as requiring you to actively flag changes. A web list that changes without a targeted notice does not meet that reading. The identities of every processor in the chain should stay available. How deeply you verify depends on risk.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"You stay fully liable to the client for your sub-processor's performance. Low risk does not remove the duty to verify. You do not automatically need a copy of every downstream contract.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 28(2) and 28(4). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, paragraph 128 and footnote 54. EDPB Opinion 22/2024, paragraphs 22-29, 34-41 and 69-71.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"4. Choosing a vendor is a continuing duty, not a one-time signature","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Use only processors that give sufficient guarantees. EDPB treats this as a continuing duty. Check guarantees at sensible intervals.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Weigh the processing risk, the vendor's expertise, reliability and resources, and current evidence and changes. Look at the whole data path. Hosting includes logs, backups and support access. Forms include submissions, attachments and spam filtering. Analytics includes identifiers, event payloads and vendor reuse. Email includes lists, message content and open or click tracking.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Practical method.","t":"Review service by service. Match the DPA, security annex, sub-processor list, transfer terms and exit process to the data that actually flows.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A signed DPA is not conclusive proof of adequate guarantees. This method is not a finding that any named service complies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 28(1)-(4) and 28(9). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, paragraphs 94-99, especially paragraph 99, and paragraphs 112-114 and 143-145.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"5. Remote access from a third country can be a transfer","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A transfer has three elements. The exporter is subject to GDPR for the processing. It makes personal data available to another entity. That entity is in a third country or is an international organisation. Chapter V then applies, on top of the rest of the GDPR. Adequacy, appropriate safeguards and derogations are separate routes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"For each flow, collect the exporter and importer identities, locations, roles, data categories, storage and remote-access routes. Match each flow to a covered mechanism and record its limits.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"EU hosting alone does not rule out third-country support or onward transfers. A lawful basis for processing does not supply a transfer mechanism.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paragraphs 9-13 and Examples 7 and 8.1. GDPR Articles 44, 45(1), 46(1) and 49(1). EDPB Recommendations 01/2020, Section 2.1, paragraphs 8-14.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-02, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"6. The DPF covers listed US entities only, and it never replaces the DPA","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"The EU-US Data Privacy Framework decision covers personal data sent to US organisations on the Department of Commerce DPF List. Check the official list for active certification, its scope and covered subsidiaries. Certifications renew yearly.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Even with DPF cover, you still need Article 28 processor terms with that vendor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Status on 2026-11-07.","t":"EUR-Lex marks Decision 2023/1795 in force. The appeal C-703/25 P shows \"Case in progress\" on the CURIA register. A pending appeal does not suspend the decision. This is a dated inference, not a forecast.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A US address, a vendor badge or a parent company's name is not enough. DPF cover does not create a lawful purpose, valid cookie consent or good security.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795, Article 1 and Annex I, Section I.3. EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses (2026), Question 3, page 4, Question 3.1, page 5, and Question 3.3, pages 5-6. EDPB information note of July 2023, Question 1.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"7. Standard Contractual Clauses: pick the right module and complete it","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Decision 2021/914 has four modules. When you act as the client's processor and pass data to a sub-processor outside the EEA, the processor-to-processor module (Module 3) is the usual fit (inference). Completed Modules 2 and 3 already include the Article 28 requirements for the processing they cover.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The parties must bind themselves, complete the annexes and describe the actual transfers and security measures.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A link to blank Commission clauses is not a completed contract. Do not use these clauses automatically for an importer already subject to GDPR for the same processing. Article 28-only clauses do not authorise a transfer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Decision 2021/914, Article 1(1)-(2), recitals 7 and 9, and Annex, Clauses 1 and 8 module headings and Modules 2 and 3. Commission SCC questions and answers, Questions 6-7, 29, 35 and 39.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-13, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-14, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"8. Breaches: you tell the client, the client tells the authority","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"As processor, you notify the client without undue delay after you become aware of a personal data breach. The client, as controller, notifies the competent supervisory authority without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours of becoming aware. That duty does not apply where the breach is unlikely to result in a risk to people's rights and freedoms. A late notice must give the reasons for the delay. In Croatia that authority is usually AZOP, the Agencija za zaštitu osobnih podataka.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"AZOP's breach page is the controller's entry point. The client first confirms AZOP is the competent authority for its processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not give yourself or a vendor an automatic 72-hour waiting period. Not every security incident is a personal data breach. A rights-complaint form is not the breach route.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 33(1)-(2), read with Article 28(3)(f). Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018, Article 4(1)-(3). AZOP page \"Izvješćivanje o povredi osobnih podataka\", heading and first substantive paragraph.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-11, N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-06.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"9. Rights requests that reach you go to the client","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Recognise a rights request even if it does not name the GDPR. Log it, identify the right asked for and route it to the controller responsible for that activity. Logging and routing are practical steps inferred from these duties. Your contract must say how you help.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Record the date and channel of receipt, what the person wants, the controller and processors involved, and any authorised representative.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A preferred form does not justify ignoring a clear request received through an appropriate channel.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 12(1)-(2), 5(2) and 28(3)(e). EDPB Guidelines 01/2022, paragraphs 47-57, section 3.1.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"10. The client's notice needs your vendor list","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"The client's privacy notice names recipients or meaningful categories of recipients. Where data goes to a third country, it says whether an adequacy decision exists or names the safeguard and how to get it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"This is the client's duty as controller. It needs the hosting, email, payment, analytics and support recipients, their roles, the destinations including overseas access, the actual transfer route and safeguard documents, and how a person can get a copy. It can only be accurate if you hand over the vendors, entities, locations and transfer routes you use for the client.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A disclosure does not make a transfer lawful. The notice cannot claim a safeguard that is not in place. EU hosting alone does not show that no overseas recipient can access data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1)(e)-(f) and 14(1)(e)-(f). EDPB DPF FAQ (2026), Question 3.2.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"11. Scripts you install on a client site fall under the Croatian device-access rule","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Storing information on, or reading it from, a visitor's device needs consent after clear and complete information. The exemptions are access only to transmit a communication, and access strictly necessary for a service the user explicitly asked for.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The Croatian provision applies to the activity, and storage or access happens through an electronic communications network. An exemption needs a specific purpose, a function the user requested, and real necessity for it. The duty likely sits with the site operator, usually your client (inference). You build and configure the scripts, so you shape whether the site meets it. UC-06 covers analytics in depth.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The rule is not limited to named cookie formats or to identifiable data. Small-business size and a vendor's \"essential\" label do not establish an exemption.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama (ZEK), NN 76/2022, Article 43(4), first and second sentence. Later amendments in NN 14/2024 and NN 45/2026 did not change Article 43(4), checked 2026-11-07. ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 5(3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"12. Each client site needs its own trader information","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A Croatian provider of an information society service shows its identity, seat, effective contact including email, and applicable registration, supervisory, professional and VAT details, directly and permanently. A d.o.o. client's website must also show the company name and seat, registry court and number, bank and account details, share capital and management board names.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The client provides an information society service. The fields depend on its legal form and establishment, registration, any supervision or regulated profession, and its VAT status. The d.o.o. fields apply to a Croatian d.o.o. and need its current registered data, bank accounts, capital payment status and management members. This is the client's duty. Your site template should leave room for it and never copy your own details into a client footer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The VAT-number field is conditional. Article 6 is not limited to consumer sales. The issued-share field in Article 21(5)(2) concerns a d.d., not a d.o.o.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, Article 6(1). Zakon o trgovačkim društvima, NN 152/2011, Article 21(4), (5)(1) and (3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-06.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"13. Processor records of processing","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A processor keeps a record of each category of processing it carries out for each controller.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions (inference).","t":"You act as a processor for at least one client. The record names each controller, the categories of processing, any third-country transfers, and a general description of security measures where possible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions (inference).","t":"Article 30(5) relieves organisations under 250 staff, but not where the processing is likely to be risky, is not occasional, or includes special categories or criminal data. Ongoing hosting or maintenance is unlikely to be occasional.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 30(2) and 30(5).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim id.","t":"None in the pack yet (gap).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"14. Hosting-plan terms (vendor terms, not law)","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"These are a vendor's own terms, checked on 2026-11-07. They show a pattern to look for on every plan you use.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Non-commercial plans.","t":"Vercel's terms say a Hobby plan is only \"for your personal or non-commercial use\" (vercel.com/legal/terms, section 4). Its fair-use page lists \"Receiving payment to create, update, or host the site\" and \"Advertising the sale of a product or service\" as commercial use (vercel.com/docs/limits/fair-use-guidelines, \"Commercial usage\").","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"DPA scope.","t":"Vercel's public DPA applies to customers \"on Enterprise and Pro plans\" (vercel.com/legal/dpa, sections 1 and 4.1). Section 4.1 also covers a customer acting as controller or processor, which fits client work on those plans. Section 13.1 says primary processing facilities are in the United States, and Schedule 3 holds the SCCs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Region is not residency.","t":"New Vercel projects run functions in iad1 (Washington, D.C.) by default. Choosing an EU function region moves those functions only. CDN, analytics, logs, support and sub-processors are separate paths.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"The wider pattern.","t":"Other free tiers vary. Some form relays publish no processor agreement. Some call themselves an independent controller. Some mail and office plans offer EU data regions only on higher editions. Some database free tiers include no automatic backups. Read the terms, DPA scope and region notes for the exact plan in each account.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"These terms matter when a studio-owned account on a free or hobby plan hosts paid client work, or holds personal data for a client.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A separately agreed contract with the vendor would need its own evidence. Public terms show what a vendor offers. They cannot show which plan or agreement your account actually accepted.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim id.","t":"None. These are vendor facts. Question Q-086 covers them.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"15. NIS2: usually out of scope by size, with exceptions worth one check","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A micro or small enterprise generally falls below the NIS2 size rule, after you check linked and partner enterprises. Some providers are covered regardless of size, including DNS service providers and entities that provide domain name registration services. A covered client's supply-chain security terms can reach you by contract without making you directly regulated.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Size depends on staff annual work units, turnover and balance sheet, and ownership links. The size-independent routes depend on whether you actually provide a DNS, trust or communications service, and whether you act as a registrar or reseller and who contracts for the registration. Contract reach depends on your client's own scope, its contract and any criticality designation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Owning a domain or using a third-party certificate is not providing these services. Editing records in someone else's DNS service is likely not providing one either (inference). Ordinary domain ownership alone is not a registration service. Being below 50 staff is not enough where financial or group facts change the size class. Do not call yourself directly regulated only because a client asks for NIS2 assurances.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555, Articles 2(1)-(4), 3, 2(2)(a)(i)-(iii), 6(22), 21(2)(d) and 27-28. Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC, Annex Articles 2-6.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-NIS2-02, F-NIS2-05, F-NIS2-07, F-NIS2-11.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Make one service inventory.","t":"One row per client per service: domain, DNS, hosting, database, form backend, mail, analytics, backups. Columns: account owner, plan, who pays, who has admin, personal data inside, vendor entity, DPA link and version, region, transfer route.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: every row has an owner and a plan, or says \"unknown\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: run it against each client domain you name. It observes hosting headers, every third-party request, form destinations, and MX and SPF records, which reveal the mail provider. It builds an observed vendor list. It cannot see account owners, plans, billing or DPA acceptance. Those stay \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Mark your role for each activity.","t":"Use the table in rule 1. Write controller, processor, none, or \"ask counsel\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no activity is left blank.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: nothing to observe. Needs your answer (Q-083, Q-084).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Check the plan behind every paid client project in your own accounts.","t":"Move it to a plan that allows commercial use and whose DPA covers you as a processor, or move the service into the client's own account.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the vendor billing page shows the plan. Record the DPA version and date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: response headers usually name the host. The plan itself needs your answer (Q-086).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Accept the vendor DPAs in each account you own.","t":"Many are accepted in the dashboard or by accepting the terms. Record the version and date. For each US vendor, search the exact legal entity on the DPF List in a browser and save the date and status.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a dated record per vendor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: shows which vendors load. Their DPA links and transfer routes come from each vendor's own pages. Mark what you cannot find as unknown (Q-108).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Sign a DPA with each client you process for.","t":"Cover every point in Article 28(3). Annex your sub-processors with entity, location and transfer route, copied from step 1.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: one signed copy per client, and its annex matches the inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Give each client its notice inputs.","t":"Send the recipient list and transfer routes for its site.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the client's notice lists those recipients or their categories.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: look for whether a privacy notice link and trader information appear on each site. Compare the observed third parties with the notice by hand (Q-075).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Remove what nobody uses.","t":"Take out dead tags, scripts pointing to hostnames you no longer run, and analytics no one reads on client sites.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: repeat the outside check and confirm the requests are gone.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: the network log shows the before and after.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Write a one-page breach and rights routine.","t":"Who you call at each client, within what time, and what you send. Note that the AZOP report is the client's step.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: one contact per client is on file and dated.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Set a sub-processor change routine.","t":"Subscribe to each vendor's change notices. Forward relevant changes to clients with an objection window.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: one test notice has gone out.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not observable (Q-087).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Plan each handover before you need it.","t":"The client should be the domain registrant. List the steps to move the hosting project, repository, DNS, mail tenant admin and analytics property. Rotate secrets, revoke your access, and return or delete your copies at the client's choice. Confirm it in writing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: dry-run the handover on one small client.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: repeat it after handover. Unchanged MX and hosting results show the site and mail still work.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Keep your processor record.","t":"One entry per client under Article 30(2), built from the inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the record matches the inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Paid client work on a free or hobby plan.","t":"Some plans bar commercial use, and their public DPA may not cover them at all.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A badge treated as a contract.","t":"\"GDPR compliant\" or a DPF claim on a vendor page is not an Article 28 agreement.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"An EU region treated as EU only.","t":"A function region does not move logs, CDN, analytics, support or sub-processors.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Client leads through your own free form relay.","t":"That usually makes the relay your sub-processor, often with no processor terms and no client authorisation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Domains registered in your name.","t":"The client cannot leave cleanly, and you may look like a reseller.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A one-time setup price that implies recurring duties.","t":"Hosting renewals, mail renewals, maintenance and support then have no named owner and no funding. Say in the offer what stops at launch.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"One shared team for every client.","t":"A budget cap that pauses the team takes every client site offline at once.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Your card on client renewals.","t":"If it lapses, the client's site or mail stops.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Client data in a consumer AI account.","t":"Consumer terms usually come with no DPA. UC-08 covers AI helpers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A cross-client dashboard.","t":"Combining visitor data across clients for your own insight likely makes you a controller for that purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A copied notice template.","t":"It names tools the site does not use, or misses ones it does.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A free mail plan sold as \"EU\".","t":"Data-region options often depend on the edition. Check the exact plan before you promise EU storage.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work only in repositories and domains the owner names. Plan changes, terms acceptance, domain transfers and DPA signatures are owner actions. Prepare them, never do them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Create a service inventory file per client from step 1. Verify: every third party the outside check shows for that domain appears in the file.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add SUBPROCESSORS.md to each client repository with vendor, legal entity, region, transfer route, DPA link and checked date. Verify: it matches the vendors the outside check shows, with unknowns marked unknown.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] List every form endpoint and confirm each posts to a backend in the inventory. Verify: no form posts to a destination missing from the inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove unused third-party scripts, fonts and pixels. Verify: repeat the outside check and the requests are gone.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Load any non-essential analytics only after consent, or remove it. Verify: the consent-order check shows no analytics request before a choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Set the function region where the host supports it, and record that it covers functions only. Verify: the deployment settings show the region.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Keep secrets in environment variables, never in the repository. Verify: a secret scan of the repository finds none.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Use synthetic data in fixtures, seeds and prompts. Verify: a search of fixtures finds no real email addresses or phone numbers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Write a handover checklist: transfer repository and project, rotate keys, revoke studio access, export data, confirm deletion. Verify: after a dry run, the studio account no longer appears in the client's team and a deploy still succeeds.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Do you agree with my role for each activity, especially build-only work with a staging copy, and mail setup where I keep admin access?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Does my client DPA meet Article 28(3)? What liability limit, governing law and audit terms suit a one-person studio?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"If I host clients in my own accounts and re-bill them, what must my client contract say about renewals, suspension, service levels and exit?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Past processing ran on a plan whose public DPA did not cover it. What is the right fix, and do I tell the client?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"Do I register or manage domains in a way that makes me a domain registration service or reseller under NIS2 and the Croatian Cybersecurity Act (Q-123)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"A client sends NIS2 supply-chain terms. Which duties are contractual only, and which can I accept?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant or tax adviser","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"When I pay for hosting, domains or mail and re-bill the client, is that my own supply? How do I invoice it, with or without a margin?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Which foreign subscriptions require a PDV ID and self-assessed Croatian VAT for me (F-TAX-05, F-TAX-12)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"From which date do I issue or receive eRačun for domestic business clients, given my VAT status (F-TAX-08, F-TAX-09)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Should setup and recurring maintenance or hosting go on separate invoices? UC-11 covers obrt invoicing in depth.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Checked","u":""}],[{"t":"GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 4(7), 4(8), 12, 13(1)(e)-(f), 14(1)(e)-(f), 26, 28, 30(2), 30(5), 33, 44-49","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Part I paragraphs 12-13, 39-41. Part II paragraphs 94-99, 110-114, 125-128, 130-145","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Opinion 22/2024 on processors and sub-processors","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2024-10/edpb_opinion_202422_relianceonprocessors-sub-processors_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 22-29, 34-41, 69-71","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021 on Article 3 and Chapter V","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 9-13, Examples 7 and 8.1","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Recommendations 01/2020 on supplementary measures","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2021-06/edpb_recommendations_202001vo.2.0_supplementarymeasurestransferstools_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Section 2.1, paragraphs 8-14","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-04/edpb_dpf_faq-for-businesses_v2_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Questions 3, 3.1, 3.2, 3.3","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB information note on transfers to the US","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-07/edpb_informationnoteadequacydecisionus_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Question 1","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 01/2022 on the right of access","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-04/edpb_guidelines_202201_data_subject_rights_access_v2_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 47-57, section 3.1","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2023/1795, EU-US Data Privacy Framework","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/1795/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Article 1, Annex I Section I.3, EUR-Lex status","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"C-703/25 P case register","u":"https://juris.curia.europa.eu/juris/liste.jsf?num=C-703/25&language=en"},{"t":"Court of Justice","u":""},{"t":"Displayed status \"Case in progress\"","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"DPF List","u":"https://www.dataprivacyframework.gov/list"},{"t":"US Department of Commerce","u":""},{"t":"Search by legal entity. Renders only in a browser","u":""},{"t":"Check per vendor","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2021/914, transfer SCCs","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Article 1(1)-(2), recital 7, Annex Clauses 1 and 8","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission SCC questions and answers","u":"https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/international-dimension-data-protection/new-standard-contractual-clauses-questions-and-answers-overview_en"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Questions 6-7, 29, 35, 39","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2021/915, Article 28(7) controller-processor SCCs","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/915/oj"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Whole Annex. No claim in the pack","u":""},{"t":"Not re-read. Verify","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2018_05_42_805.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 4(1)-(3)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP breach reporting page","u":"https://azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Heading and first substantive paragraph","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama, NN 76/2022","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 43(4)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2002/58/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Article 5(3)","u":""},{"t":"Cited through N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01 and 02. Not re-read","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2003_10_173_2504.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 6(1)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o trgovačkim društvima, NN 152/2011","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/full/2011_12_152_3144.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 21(4)-(5)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2022/2555/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 2-3, 6(22), 21(2)(d), 27-28","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reco/2003/361/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Annex Articles 2-6","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti, NN 14/2024","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Named in the counsel question on NIS2. Its NIS2 scope rules are not in the pack","u":""},{"t":"Not in the pack. Verify","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_06_89_1233.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Articles 2(1)(24) and (34), 38(1), 80","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC, consolidated","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02006L0112-20250414"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 196, 219a, 220, 226","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel terms","u":"https://vercel.com/legal/terms"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Section 4, Hobby plan","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel fair-use guidelines","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/limits/fair-use-guidelines"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"\"Commercial usage\"","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel DPA","u":"https://vercel.com/legal/dpa"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Sections 1, 4.1, 13.1, Schedule 3","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel function regions","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/configuring-functions/region"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Default region","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Note for kit maintainers: the F-NIS2 claims live in the master research pack. The kit's research/families/ folder does not hold F-NIS2 yet, so those ids will not resolve in the kit's rule pages until it is copied in.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-02","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: A yearly SaaS sold to holiday-rental hosts","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small Croatian business that sells a yearly guest-guide SaaS to rental hosts, some of them companies or sole traders and some private individuals","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-161, Q-163, Q-053, Q-165, Q-172, Q-220, Q-216, Q-191, Q-193, Q-083]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-CONSUMER-01, F-CONSUMER-02, F-CONSUMER-04, F-CONSUMER-05, F-CONSUMER-06, F-CONSUMER-07, F-CONSUMER-08, F-CONSUMER-09, F-CONSUMER-11, F-CONSUMER-14, F-CONSUMER-15, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-02, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-03, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-04, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-06, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-07, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-09, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-10, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-01, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-03, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-05, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-07, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-08, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-10, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-02, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-03, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-04, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-05, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-06, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-07, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-12, F-ECOMMERCE-02, F-ECOMMERCE-04, F-ECOMMERCE-08, F-EAA-02, F-EAA-03, F-EAA-06, F-EAA-10, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-02, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-03, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-04, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-07, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-09, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-10, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-TAX-02, F-TAX-09, F-TAX-11, F-TAX-15]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"saas":{"title":"A yearly SaaS sold to holiday-rental hosts","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Fact","u":""},{"t":"Why it matters","u":""},{"t":"Question","u":""}],[{"t":"Does each buyer act outside a trade, business, craft or profession?","u":""},{"t":"Only a natural person buying for private purposes is a consumer. That decides whether the consumer rules below apply to that sale.","u":""},{"t":"Q-161","u":""}],[{"t":"Is the product a digital service, digital content, a human-made guide, or a mix?","u":""},{"t":"Withdrawal exceptions differ. A digital service loses withdrawal only after full performance. Digital content can lose it when supply begins, under extra conditions.","u":""},{"t":"Q-163","u":""}],[{"t":"Do buyers order through a checkout, or only by individual email or phone?","u":""},{"t":"An online checkout brings in the order-flow duties and the online withdrawal function. Contracts made only by individual email are excluded from some order-flow duties, not all.","u":""},{"t":"Q-053","u":""}],[{"t":"Does the order step show the yearly price, duration, renewal and payment duty before the buyer commits?","u":""},{"t":"Subscription disclosures and the payment-acknowledgement rule depend on it.","u":""},{"t":"Q-165","u":""}],[{"t":"Did a consumer buyer expressly ask you to start within 14 days and acknowledge the effect on withdrawal?","u":""},{"t":"Without that request you cannot charge for the period used before withdrawal.","u":""},{"t":"Q-172","u":""}],[{"t":"Does the site show prices, and does it conclude consumer distance contracts?","u":""},{"t":"Price display rules apply when you show prices. The new price-list duty applies to traders with websites from 17 November 2026.","u":""},{"t":"Q-220","u":""}],[{"t":"Is the seller an obrt, a d.o.o., another legal entity or a foreign provider?","u":""},{"t":"The trader-information fields differ by legal form.","u":""},{"t":"Q-216","u":""}],[{"t":"Do consumers in Croatia conclude contracts through your website or app?","u":""},{"t":"If not, the accessibility act's e-commerce gate is not met.","u":""},{"t":"Q-191","u":""}],[{"t":"What were average staff numbers and prior-year revenue or assets?","u":""},{"t":"Fewer than 10 staff and at most EUR 2 million revenue or assets means the service exemption may apply.","u":""},{"t":"Q-193","u":""}],[{"t":"Who decides what guest data goes into a guide and why?","u":""},{"t":"That decides whether you are a processor for each host, or a controller in your own right.","u":""},{"t":"Q-083","u":""}]]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"1. Consumer or trader buyer","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A consumer is a natural person who concludes a contract or acts on the market outside their trade, business, craft or professional activity. The other party must be a trader.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Look at the purpose and circumstances of this purchase, not at a label. A d.o.o. is a legal person, so it is never a consumer. A sole trader who buys for the business acts within the activity. A private renter is an open case. It depends on the purpose of the purchase, how the guide is used and the scale of the rental.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Directive 2011/83/EU recital 17 says a dual-purpose buyer should also count as a consumer when the trade purpose is so limited that it does not predominate. A recital guides interpretation. It is not an operative rule. Registration status does not decide the question either way. The labels used for VAT, eRačun and consumer law do not replace each other. The same buyer can be a business for one and a consumer for another.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o zaštiti potrošača (ZZP), NN 19/2022, Art. 4 points 21 and 34. Directive 2011/83/EU, Art. 2(1) and (2), recital 17.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-CONSUMER-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"2. What you sell: digital service, digital content or a human service","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Digital content is data supplied in digital form. A digital service lets the consumer create, process, store or access data, or interact with it. A human service does not become a digital service only because it is delivered online.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A hosted guide that the host edits and that stays online all year looks like a digital service. A guide you build by hand for each property may be partly a human service. A downloadable file is digital content.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Bundles may need legal classification.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Directive (EU) 2019/770, Arts. 2(1) to (3) and 3(4) to (6). Directive (EU) 2019/2161, Art. 4(1)(c) to (e).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-CONSUMER-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"3. Pre-contract information for a consumer buyer","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Before a distance contract, give clear information about the product, your identity and contacts, the price, payment, duration and the withdrawal right. For subscriptions, include the cost per billing period, duration, termination and renewal conditions and any minimum commitment. For digital supply, include functionality, compatibility and conformity information.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Applies when the buyer is a consumer and the contract is a distance contract. ZZP Art. 60 was replaced by NN 59/2026 Art. 24. Do not rely on the 2022 item numbers. The information must be in Croatian in Latin script. Other languages may be added. The format must suit the distance medium and use simple, understandable language.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Distance financial services use their own chapter.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"NN 59/2026, Art. 24 (new ZZP Art. 60(1) points 1 to 13, 15, 18, 21 to 25, Art. 60(3) to (5) and 60(9)). ZZP NN 19/2022, Art. 72(1). Directive 2011/83/EU, Art. 6(1)(e), (o) and (p), Art. 8(2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-03, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-04, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-06, F-CONSUMER-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"4. Commencement dates of the 2026 consumer amendment","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"NN 59/2026 was published on 9 June 2026. Its Art. 66 sets these dates. The table names the provisions that matter here. It is not the full list, so read Art. 66 for any provision not shown.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"From","u":""},{"t":"What starts, including","u":""}],[{"t":"17 June 2026","u":""},{"t":"Every provision that Art. 66 does not assign to a later date","u":""}],[{"t":"19 June 2026","u":""},{"t":"The online withdrawal function (new Art. 81a), the withdrawal-function information in Art. 60 and the financial-services changes","u":""}],[{"t":"31 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"NN 59/2026 Arts. 45 to 48","u":""}],[{"t":"27 September 2026","u":""},{"t":"Further Art. 60 points, amended ZZP Art. 46(1) to (4) and the new ZZP Art. 74(1)","u":""}],[{"t":"17 November 2026","u":""},{"t":"Amended ZZP Art. 7(1) to (9), including the website price-list duty","u":""}]]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Check the date of the transaction you assess. Historic transactions use the version in force on their own date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The 17 November phase is not a general delay of other consumer duties.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"NN 59/2026, Art. 66.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"5. Ordering and confirmation","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Before a consumer pays online, show the key information clearly and prominently. Get explicit acknowledgement of the payment obligation. Label the button \"order with obligation to pay\" or with equally clear wording. If you do not, the consumer is not bound. Send a confirmation on a durable medium in reasonable time, and at the latest before the service starts. An email can serve.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A consumer distance contract. The general electronic-order rules also apply to business buyers: explain the contract steps, let the buyer fix input errors, make the terms storable and reproducible, and acknowledge an order without delay.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Business buyers can agree to waive some order-flow steps, but not the storable-terms duty. Contracts concluded only by individual email or similar exchanges are excluded from the step-by-step information, the input-error correction and the acknowledgement duty. The storable-terms duty still applies. A link to editable website terms does not prove a durable confirmation was delivered.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZZP NN 19/2022, Art. 74(2) to (4), Arts. 75 and 76. NN 59/2026, Art. 27 (new Art. 74(1)). Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini (ZET), NN 173/2003, Arts. 12(1) to (4), 13 and 14(1) to (3). Directive 2011/83/EU, Art. 8(2), (3) and (7). Directive 2000/31/EC, Arts. 10 and 11.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-07, F-CONSUMER-14, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-12, F-ECOMMERCE-04, F-ECOMMERCE-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"6. Withdrawal for a yearly digital subscription","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A consumer can withdraw within 14 days without giving reasons. For services and for digital content not on a physical medium, the period runs from the day the contract is concluded.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"If you did not give the withdrawal information, the period runs until one year after the ordinary 14 days end. If you give the information during that year, the consumer has 14 days from receipt.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How the consumer withdraws.","t":"By the model form or any clear statement sent before expiry. You cannot make the model form the only route. The consumer must prove timely withdrawal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Online function.","t":"From 19 June 2026, a contract concluded through an online interface needs a prominent, accessible withdrawal function for the withdrawal period. The statutory labels are \"raskid ugovora\" and \"potvrditi raskid ugovora\", or equally clear wording. You must promptly acknowledge the content, date and time on a durable medium.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Model instructions.","t":"Pravilnik NN 105/2026 sets the current withdrawal instructions and model form. It came into force on 26 September 2026 and repealed Pravilnik NN 117/2022. It includes an instruction on where the online function sits. Pick only the options that fit your offer. Do not copy every option into one form. The Annex I part I.6 wording on a proportionate charge for digital content is unresolved, so leave it out until counsel checks it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"For a paid service, withdrawal ends only when the service is fully performed, after the consumer's prior express consent and acknowledgement. Activating a yearly subscription is not full performance. The paid digital-content exception is different. Performance must begin with prior express consent, acknowledged loss of withdrawal, and a contract confirmation. Under NN 59/2026 Art. 29 (new Art. 84(10)), no charge is due for that digital content if a listed consent, acknowledgement or confirmation condition fails. It is not a general exception for digital services. The online function does not create a cancellation right after the withdrawal period ends.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Early start.","t":"A consumer who expressly asks you to start a service within 14 days and then withdraws owes a proportionate amount for the time used. Use the contract price, or market value if the price is excessive. Nothing is owed if you did not give the required withdrawal and cost information, or if there was no express request.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Renewals.","t":"For a free trial followed by paid automatic extension, the CJEU held in Sofatutor that withdrawal is available once, if the consumer was clearly told about the later payment at conclusion. Do not stretch this to a materially changed or new contract.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZZP NN 19/2022, Arts. 77(1) and (2), 79(1) to (5), 80(1) and (2), 81(1) to (5), 84(8) and (9), 86(1) points 1 and 13. NN 59/2026, Arts. 28 (new Art. 81a) and 29. Pravilnik NN 105/2026, Arts. 1 and 3 to 5, Annex I. Directive 2011/83/EU, Arts. 9, 10, 11a, 14(3) and (4), 16(a) and 16(m). Directive (EU) 2023/2673, Art. 1(2) and (3). CJEU C-565/22, Sofatutor, paras. 45 to 51.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-01, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-03, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-05, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-07, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-08, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-10, F-CONSUMER-04, F-CONSUMER-05, F-CONSUMER-06, F-CONSUMER-08, F-CONSUMER-09, F-CONSUMER-15.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"7. Conformity remedies are separate","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Losing the withdrawal right does not remove remedies for a digital service that fails or does not conform.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A consumer contract for digital content or a digital service.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The Croatian transposition of Directive (EU) 2019/770 was not identified in this research. Ask counsel.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Directive (EU) 2019/770, Arts. 1, 13, 14 and 22. Commission Notice 2021/C 525/01, section 5.4.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-CONSUMER-11.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"8. Price display","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Displayed prices must be clear. They must say whether tax, delivery and other price-affecting costs are included. For consumer contracts, the new Art. 60 adds its own price and recurring-cost rules.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"New from 17 November 2026.","t":"New ZZP Art. 7(9) requires traders to publish current price lists on their websites. Art. 7(12) leaves the publication method to a ministerial rule. That rule was not located in this research. Do not invent a format, update frequency or exemption.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You show prices on a website. ZET Art. 6(2) is not limited to consumer sales.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Price display does not replace tax or invoice rules. A business that is exempt from VAT as a small taxpayer may not show VAT on invoices. Your accountant confirms the exact VAT note.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZET NN 173/2003, Art. 6(2). NN 59/2026, Art. 4 (new ZZP Art. 7(9) and (12)), Art. 24 (new Art. 60(1) point 5 and 60(3) to (6)), Art. 66. Directive 2000/31/EC, Art. 5(2). VAT Act amendments NN 152/2024, Art. 18 (new Arts. 90f to 90h).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-02, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-10, F-ECOMMERCE-02, F-TAX-15.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"9. Trader identification","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"An information society service provider makes these details directly and permanently available: name or business name, seat, contact details including an email address, register details and number, the supervisory authority where approval is needed, details for regulated professions, and the tax number where the provider is a VAT payer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Consumer layer.","t":"For consumer distance contracts, the new Art. 60 adds phone, email, any representative and a complaints address. ZET disclosures do not replace it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Complaints.","t":"Keep written complaint channels at your business premises, by post and by email, display a clear complaints notice on your website, acknowledge receipt without delay, reply in writing within 15 days, and keep records for one year.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"By legal form.","t":"An obrt business name includes the owner's name and the seat (Obrt Act Art. 19). That article's physical-display rule is not a full website checklist. Art. 19(6) applies company-name rules correspondingly, but its effect on an obrt website is unresolved. Do not copy d.o.o. capital and management fields onto a sole trader's site. A d.o.o. website must show the company name and seat, registry court and number, bank names, seats and account numbers, share capital, whether it is fully paid and any unpaid amount, and each management board member's surname and at least one given name.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The VAT-number field is conditional. The ZET provision is not limited to consumer sales. Croatian establishment rules differ from those for providers in another Member State.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"NN 67/2025 repealed ZET Arts. 16, 17, 18 and 21, not Art. 6. The Obrt Act amendment NN 114/2026 item 1370 adds registration fields from 1 January 2027. It does not itself create a website list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZET NN 173/2003, Art. 6(1). NN 67/2025, Arts. 25(1) and 26. Zakon o obrtu NN 143/2013, Art. 19. NN 114/2026 item 1370, Arts. 4 and 44. Zakon o trgovačkim društvima, NN 152/2011, Art. 21(4) and (5). NN 59/2026, Art. 24 (new Art. 60(1) points 2 to 4). ZZP NN 19/2022, Art. 10. Directive 2000/31/EC, Art. 5(1).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-03, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-04, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-05, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-06, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-07, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-09, F-ECOMMERCE-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"10. European Accessibility Act: scope and microenterprise exemption","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"The Croatian act (NN 89/2025, item 1231) covers listed consumer services, including e-commerce. An e-commerce service is provided at a distance through a website or mobile service, at a consumer's request, to conclude a consumer contract.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Two gates.","t":"Either gate can take you out of scope.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Is it a covered service? Guests who read a guide conclude no contract through it. The question is how hosts buy. If only businesses buy, the consumer-contract definition is not met. If private renters who count as consumers buy through your site, it may be.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Are you a microenterprise? Art. 4(2) exempts microenterprises that provide services. Current Art. 5 point 22 requires an average of fewer than 10 workers a year and, per prior-year financial statements, revenue or assets of at most EUR 2 million.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Numbering.","t":"NN 114/2026 item 1371 came into force on 15 October 2026. It renumbered the definitions: old point 18 is now point 22, and old point 25 is now point 29. It did not replace the e-commerce scope or the service exemption.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"If you are in scope.","t":"Make the website, service information, support, identification, security and payment functions accessible. Publish Annex V compliance information in written and oral forms that disabled people can use, and keep it while the service runs. Correct non-conformity and inform the authorities.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Exactly 10 average workers fails the \"fewer than 10\" test. Product duties are not covered by the service exemption. An accessibility widget or statement alone does not prove compliance. Art. 17 separately governs fundamental alteration and disproportionate burden. A business in its first year has no prior-year statements, so ask counsel how the test applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Supervisor.","t":"Market inspectors of the State Inspectorate (Državni inspektorat) supervise e-commerce services. Under the October 2026 amendment, the operator pays examination costs if the service does not comply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"NN 89/2025 item 1231, Arts. 3(2), 4(2), 5 points 22 and 29 (current numbering), 15(2) to (5), 25(9), Annexes I and V. NN 114/2026 item 1371, Arts. 1, 4 and 13. Directive (EU) 2019/882, Arts. 3(23), 3(30), 4(5), 13, Annexes I and V.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-02, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-03, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-04, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-07, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-09, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-10, F-EAA-02, F-EAA-03, F-EAA-06, F-EAA-10.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"11. The host as controller of guest data","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A controller decides the purposes and means of processing. A processor handles personal data on the controller's behalf. Roles are functional. A contract label cannot override who actually decides.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"When a host puts guest names, arrival details or house rules with personal data into a guide, the host decides why. You host it on the host's behalf. You are then likely the host's processor. You are usually the controller of your own data about hosts as customers, and of any analytics you run on guide pages for your own purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What the contract needs.","t":"A processing agreement, or another binding legal act, in writing, which may be electronic. It sets out subject, duration, nature and purpose, data types, the people affected, and the controller's rights. It binds you to documented instructions, confidentiality, security and lawful sub-processing. Vendors that process the host's guest data for you, such as hosting or email, are usually your sub-processors. They need the host's prior general or specific written authorisation, with notice of changes and a chance to object. At the end of the service, the host chooses return or deletion.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Your own privacy notice.","t":"Name the recipients or their categories. Say whether data goes to a third country and, where it does, on what safeguard. Do not claim a safeguard you have not put in place.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"If you use guest data for your own purposes, such as product analytics across all hosts, you may become a controller for that use. Assess each activity separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679), Arts. 4(7), 4(8), 13(1)(e) and (f), 28(2), 28(3)(a) to (h), 28(4), 28(9), 28(10). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part I paras. 12 and 13, 39 to 41.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"12. Tax and invoicing pointers","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"These points route to your accountant. UC-11 covers them in depth.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Whether a hosted guide is an electronically supplied service depends on how automated it is. A guide built by hand may not qualify. Email contact alone does not decide it (Implementing Regulation 282/2011, Art. 7. VAT Directive, Art. 58(1)). Claim F-TAX-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Croatia's small-taxpayer exemption uses a EUR 60,000 domestic annual-turnover threshold (VAT Act Art. 90 as amended by NN 152/2024, from 1 January 2025). Claims F-TAX-11, F-TAX-15.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"eRačun phases: VAT-registered issuers issue and receive from 1 January 2026. Covered non-VAT recipients receive from 2026 and start issuing on 1 January 2027 (Zakon o fiskalizaciji NN 89/2025, Arts. 38(1) and 80). Claim F-TAX-09.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Record each buyer's status at order time.","t":"Add one required field: \"buying for a company or registered business\" or \"buying as a private person\". Store the answer with the order.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: open the last order record and confirm the field is there.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-161 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Put the trader details on every site that sells.","t":"Use the ZET Art. 6(1) fields and the fields for your legal form. Add phone, email and a complaints address for consumer buyers. Add a complaints notice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: from the home page, reach the trader page in one click. Compare its fields with section 9.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: observes whether a trader-information or imprint page exists on each site, and its language.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Fix the price line.","t":"Say \"per year\". State whether VAT is included, or that VAT is not charged, in the words your accountant confirms. State renewal terms next to the price.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: read the pricing section aloud. A buyer should know the full yearly cost and what happens at renewal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: does not cover price wording. Answer Q-220 and Q-165 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Prepare for 17 November 2026.","t":"Publish a current price list on your website. Watch for the Art. 7(12) ministerial rule and adjust when it appears.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the price list page exists, is dated, and matches what you invoice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: cannot judge this duty. Mark it \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Give consumer buyers the pre-contract pack in Croatian.","t":"Cover the Art. 60 items: identity, price per year, duration, renewal and cancellation, functionality and compatibility, and the withdrawal information. Use the NN 105/2026 model instructions and form, with only the options that fit your offer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a private buyer receives this before they pay. Keep a copy of what was sent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: observes page language only.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Send a durable confirmation.","t":"Email a confirmation with the terms, the withdrawal information and the model form, before access starts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: place a test order and check the email arrives with every item.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: never submit a form, so this is not visible. Answer Q-053 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Add an early-start request for consumers.","t":"If a private buyer wants access at once, ask them to request it expressly and to acknowledge the effect on withdrawal. Record the request.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the order record holds the request text and a timestamp.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-172 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"If you add an online checkout, build the withdrawal function.","t":"Label it \"raskid ugovora\", add a \"potvrditi raskid ugovora\" step, and send an acknowledgement with date and time. Add the payment-acknowledgement button.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run the function on a test account and check the acknowledgement email.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: does not log in, so it cannot reach the function. It can observe a form's destination on a public page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Sign a processing agreement with each host.","t":"Use an electronic agreement that covers the Art. 28(3) items. List your sub-processors and give notice of changes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each active host account shows an accepted agreement version and date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: shows which vendors load. It cannot see your host agreements. Answer Q-083 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Check the accessibility act gates.","t":"Record average headcount and the prior-year figure. If you are not a microenterprise and consumers buy online, plan the Annex I work and the Annex V statement.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a one-page note with the figures, the date and the result of both gates.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-191 and Q-193 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Keep guest-facing guide pages clean.","t":"Run no analytics on guide pages unless you have assessed it. See UC-06.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: load a guide page in a fresh browser and list every outbound request.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: logs third-party scripts and whether analytics fires before a choice.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating every host as a business.","t":"A private renter may be a consumer. Registration with the tourist board or the tax office does not settle it either way.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating a subscription start as full performance.","t":"For a digital service, withdrawal ends only after the whole service is performed. A yearly plan is not performed on day one.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Using the digital-content exception for a hosted service.","t":"Art. 86(1) point 13 concerns paid digital content. It is not a general exception for digital services.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Relying on old item numbers.","t":"ZZP Art. 60 was replaced and Art. 46(1) to (4) amended in 2026. Cite the NN 59/2026 text.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Waiting until 17 November for everything.","t":"The online withdrawal function started on 19 June 2026, and further information duties on 27 September 2026.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Copying the old withdrawal form.","t":"Pravilnik NN 117/2022 was repealed. Use NN 105/2026, with only the options that fit your offer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"An English-only pre-contract page.","t":"Where Croatian consumer law applies, the information must be in Croatian.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Calling an accessibility widget compliance.","t":"It proves nothing on its own.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Using old EAA point numbers.","t":"After NN 114/2026, the microenterprise definition is point 22 and e-commerce is point 29.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Assuming no processor role.","t":"Hosting a guide that holds guest data for a host usually makes you a processor, whatever your terms say.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A link to editable terms as the confirmation.","t":"The consumer needs a copy on a durable medium.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work through these in order. Stop and ask the owner where a step needs a fact you do not have.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a required buyerCapacity field (business or private) to the order form and the order record.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: create a test order and read the stored record.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Build a trader-information page with the fields for the owner's legal form. Link it from the footer on every page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: crawl every page and confirm the footer link resolves with HTTP 200.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Change the price text to show \"per year\", the VAT note the owner supplies, and the renewal terms beside the price.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: grep the built pages for each price and confirm the VAT note sits beside it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a dated price-list page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the page returns HTTP 200 and its date and prices match the owner's source file.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a Croatian pre-contract information page and the NN 105/2026 model form as a download. Include only the options the owner confirms. Leave out the Annex I part I.6 digital-content charge wording.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the page lang attribute is hr and the form link returns HTTP 200.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Make the order confirmation email include the terms, the withdrawal information and the form.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: send a test order to a test inbox and check each item.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For private buyers who want immediate access, add an unticked early-start request with its acknowledgement text. Store the text shown and a timestamp.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: submit a test order with and without the box and compare the records.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] If the site has an online checkout, add the \"raskid ugovora\" function with a \"potvrditi raskid ugovora\" step and an emailed acknowledgement with date and time.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run it on a test account and check the email.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add an in-app processing-agreement acceptance for hosts. Store the version and date. Publish the sub-processor list and a change-notice step.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: query the accounts table for any active host without an accepted version.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove analytics from guest-facing guide pages unless the owner has an assessment.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run the outside check on a guide page and confirm no analytics request fires before a choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Do not write legal conclusions into the site. Leave every counsel question below open.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"How should a private renter who buys a yearly guide subscription be classified under ZZP Art. 4 point 21, given the purpose of the purchase?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Is a yearly hosted guide a digital service, digital content or both? What follows for early start, the Art. 86 exceptions and conformity duties? Which Croatian act transposes Directive (EU) 2019/770?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"Does our current sales channel count as an online interface for Art. 81a?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Does \"price list\" in the new Art. 7(9) cover a subscription service, and has the Art. 7(12) rule been issued?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"How does the accessibility act's microenterprise test apply in a business's first year, with no prior-year statements?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"Which trader-information fields must our site show for our legal form, including any tax-number line?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"","t":"Is a private host who uses our guide a controller under the GDPR, and does our host agreement meet Art. 28(3)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"","t":"Which NN 105/2026 Annex I options fit our offer, and does the part I.6 digital-content charge wording apply to us at all?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Is our guide an electronically supplied service for VAT, given how much human work goes into each one?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Are we inside the EUR 60,000 small-taxpayer threshold, and what exact VAT note should our prices and invoices carry?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"Which document does each buyer type get (eRačun, B2C receipt or other invoice) from 2026 and from 1 January 2027?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Is a private renter a business or a consumer for VAT, and what evidence of status and location should we keep?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"When do we invoice a yearly plan: at signup, at renewal, or prorated?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Checked","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o zaštiti potrošača, NN 19/2022, item 203","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_02_19_203.html"},{"t":"Arts. 4 points 21 and 34, 10, 72(1), 74 to 77, 79 to 81, 84(8) and (9), 86(1) points 1 and 13","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o izmjenama i dopunama Zakona o zaštiti potrošača, NN 59/2026, item 728","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_06_59_728.html"},{"t":"Arts. 4 (Art. 7(9) and (12)), 21, 24 (Art. 60), 27, 28 (Art. 81a), 29, 66","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Pravilnik on withdrawal information and form, NN 105/2026, item 1272","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/full/2026_09_105_1272.html"},{"t":"Arts. 1, 3 to 5, Annex I","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, item 2504","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2003_10_173_2504.html"},{"t":"Arts. 6(1), 6(2), 12 to 14","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"NN 67/2025, item 857","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_04_67_857.html"},{"t":"Arts. 25(1), 26","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o obrtu, NN 143/2013, item 3065, and amendment NN 114/2026, item 1370","u":""},{"t":"Art. 19, amendment Arts. 4 and 44","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o trgovačkim društvima, NN 152/2011, item 3144","u":""},{"t":"Art. 21(4) and (5)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o zahtjevima za pristupačnost proizvoda i usluga, NN 89/2025, item 1231","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_06_89_1231.html"},{"t":"Arts. 3(2), 4(2), 5, 15, 25(9), Annexes I and V","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"NN 114/2026, item 1371","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_10_114_1371.html"},{"t":"Arts. 1, 4, 12, 13","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2011/83/EU, consolidation of 27 September 2026","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02011L0083-20260927"},{"t":"Arts. 2, 3, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11a, 14, 16, recital 17","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive (EU) 2023/2673","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2023/2673/oj/eng"},{"t":"Art. 1(2) and (3), Art. 2(1)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive (EU) 2019/770","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/770/oj/eng"},{"t":"Arts. 1 to 3, 13, 14, 22","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive (EU) 2019/2161","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/2161/oj/eng"},{"t":"Art. 4","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Notice 2021/C 525/01)","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52021XC1229(04"},{"t":"Sections 5.4, 5.6, 5.7","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU C-565/22, Sofatutor, ECLI:EU:C:2023:735","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62022CJ0565"},{"t":"Paras. 45 to 51","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2000/31/EC, consolidation of 17 February 2024","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 5, 10, 11","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive (EU) 2019/882","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 3(23), 3(30), 4(5), 13, Annexes I and V","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679"},{"t":"Arts. 4(7), 4(8), 13(1)(e) and (f), 28","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":""},{"t":"Part I paras. 12, 13, 39 to 41","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC and Implementing Regulation 282/2011","u":""},{"t":"Directive Art. 58(1), Regulation Art. 7","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Act amendments, NN 152/2024","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 16 to 18, 28","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, item 1233","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_06_89_1233.html"},{"t":"Arts. 38(1), 80","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Gaps: the Art. 7(12) price-list rule was not located. The Croatian transposition of Directive (EU) 2019/770 was not identified. The ZZP Art. 80 cross-reference to the replaced Art. 60 needs a consolidated text. CJEU case law on consumer status for accommodation renters was not checked. The NN 105/2026 Annex I part I.6 digital-content charge wording is not reconciled with new Art. 84(10) and Art. 86(1) point 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-03","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Signups for a free online workshop or event","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small business in Croatia that runs a free online workshop, webinar or live session and collects email addresses to send the joining link.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-073, Q-080, Q-213, Q-214, Q-209, Q-061, Q-062, Q-075, Q-077, Q-083]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-05, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-NOTICE-M03, F-GDPR-BASIS-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-03, F-GDPR-BASIS-05, F-GDPR-BASIS-M01, F-GDPR-BASIS-M02, F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-04, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-07, F-EMAIL-08, F-EMAIL-10, F-EMAIL-11, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-02, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-03, F-DEVICE-04, F-DEVICE-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-03, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M03, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-ECOMMERCE-03, F-CONSUMER-03, F-SECTOR-01, F-SECTOR-02, N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-03]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"signups":{"title":"Signups for a free online workshop or event","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Answer these first. Each one moves the result.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What the form collects, and which tools touch it","t":"(Q-073). An email field alone is a small notice. A form that also asks for a name, a company or free-text questions, or a page that runs analytics or embeds a video player, needs more lines in the notice and may raise device-access questions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"When the person sees the notice","t":"(Q-080). Next to the form, before submit, is on time. A notice that first appears in the confirmation email is late.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What each message is: service, promotion, or a mix","t":"(Q-213). A joining link is a service message. A confirmation email that also pitches a paid course is a mix, and the promotional part brings in the marketing rules.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether you have valid consent before you send any promotion, or whether every customer-exception condition applies","t":"(Q-214). For a free workshop list, the default answer is consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How close your free workshop is to the free service in the Inteligo case","t":"(Q-209). That judgment treated one specific free account, tied to paid content, as a sale context. A plain free event signup may be a different fact pattern.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What else happens to the address","t":"(Q-061). Open tracking, click tracking, segmentation, sharing with a co-host and suppression are separate operations with their own rules.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How an unsubscribe reaches every list and automation","t":"(Q-062). A stop request must also reach imported copies, reminder sequences and any second tool.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who receives the data, and from which countries they can access it","t":"(Q-075). This includes the form backend, the database, the sending provider and the video-meeting platform.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How long you keep each data set, and what starts the clock","t":"(Q-077). The event list, the marketing list and the suppression record need separate periods.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who decides purposes and means for each vendor feature","t":"(Q-083). Your sending provider is usually your processor. A co-host who reuses the list for its own purposes may be a separate or joint controller.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"1. Notice at collection","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"When you collect data directly from a person, give them the GDPR Art. 13 information at that moment. That covers who you are and how to reach you, each purpose and its legal basis, recipients or categories of recipients, any third-country transfer and its safeguard, the retention period or the criteria for it, and the rights, including withdrawal of consent and the right to complain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"GDPR applies to your processing, and the data come from the person.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Art. 13(4) removes the duty only where and insofar as the person already has the information.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How to present it [Guidance].","t":"A layered notice is recommended: key facts at the form, with a direct link to the full notice. Keep the layers consistent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Before you use data for a new purpose,","t":"give the information about that purpose first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 13(1)(a)-(d), 13(1)(e)-(f), 13(2)(a)-(d), 13(1)-(3), 13(4). WP260 rev.01, paragraphs 35-36, printed p. 19, endorsed by EDPB Endorsement 1/2018, Item 2.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-05, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"2. Legal basis for running the event","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"Each purpose needs its own basis. Article 6(1)(b) can cover data objectively needed to perform a contract with the person or to take steps they request. Answering a request and adding the person to a marketing list are separate purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Article 6(1)(b) fits a free event only if the processing is objectively needed to perform a contract with the person, or to take steps they asked for before one. If that is unclear, Art. 6(1)(f) may fit, but only after you record a legitimate purpose, necessity and a balancing result.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Extra tracking or marketing does not become \"necessary\" because your terms mention it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Art. 6(1)(b), 6(1)(f). EDPB Guidelines 2/2019, paragraphs 22-30 and 45-47, printed pp. 8-9 and 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-BASIS-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"3. Service messages versus marketing messages","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"ZEK Art. 50(1) covers direct promotion and sales by email, and also by SMS and MMS.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How to classify [Inference].","t":"Classify each message by its actual purpose and wording, not by its label.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Usually service: the signup confirmation, the joining link, a reminder for the session the person booked, a notice that the time changed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Can be marketing: an invitation to a later workshop, a pitch for a paid offer, a \"join our newsletter\" request, or any service message with an upsell added.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"An email that only asks for marketing consent can itself count as marketing. Assess its wording before you send it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK, NN 76/2022, Art. 50(1),(2),(4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"4. Prior consent for marketing email","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"In Croatia, email direct promotion needs the recipient's consent, obtained in advance. The EU starting rule for natural-person subscribers is the same. HAKOM's consumer guidance repeats that promotion by email needs prior consent and a free way to stop further messages.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Croatian law governs the campaign or recipient. The recipient is an individual, including a professional individual.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The customer exception in Art. 50(2) (see rule 5). Art. 50(4) removes paragraphs 1 and 2 for communications to legal persons. People who sign up for a workshop usually do so as individuals, so Art. 50(4) rarely helps here.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Current text.","t":"NN 76/2022 took effect on 12 July 2022. NN 14/2024 (in force 15 February 2024) repeals Art. 41, and NN 45/2026 (in force 7 May 2026) renumbers definitions. Neither changes Art. 50.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Art. 50(1),(2),(4). NN 14/2024, Arts. 115(1), 116. NN 45/2026, Arts. 3, 10-13, 38. HAKOM, \"Neželjene elektroničke komunikacije\", first two paragraphs. Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 13(1),(2),(5).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-02, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, F-EMAIL-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"5. The customer exception and free signups","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"A trader may email its own consumers about its own similar products or services, using addresses it obtained from them for a sale. The person needs a clear, easy and free way to object at collection and in every message, and must not have refused at the start.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Croatian wording [Law].","t":"ZEK Art. 50(2) says \"potrošača\" (consumers) and \"u svrhu prodaje\" (for the purpose of selling). The Directive says \"customers\" and \"in the context of the sale\". The Croatian consumer definition excludes business, craft and professional purposes. It moved from Art. 5(1)(54) to Art. 5(1)(56) in NN 45/2026.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"The Inteligo case [Law, case law].","t":"The CJEU (C-654/23, 13 November 2025) treated one specific free publishing account as a sale context. That account gave limited free articles, a daily newsletter and optional paid access, and the indirect payment through paid content mattered. The judgment does not make every free download or registration a customer relationship. A bare giveaway registration is not automatically equivalent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What this means here [Inference].","t":"Do not rely on the customer exception for a free workshop list. Treat promotion to that list as needing prior consent, unless counsel confirms otherwise for your facts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Art. 50(2), Art. 5(1)(54) in the base text. NN 45/2026, Art. 3. Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 13(2). Inteligo Media, C-654/23, paragraphs 38-39, 43-48, 53-69 and operative points 1-2.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-03, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-04, F-EMAIL-10, F-GDPR-BASIS-M01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"6. What valid consent looks like","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"Consent is freely given, specific, informed and unambiguous, by a statement or a clear affirmative action. You must be able to prove it. A written consent request must stand apart from other matters. Withdrawal must be as easy as giving consent. Making the workshop depend on marketing consent it does not need weighs against free choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Granularity [Guidance].","t":"Separate purposes need separate choices.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Example [Inference].","t":"\"Future workshops\" and \"general studio news\" are likely two purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Pre-ticked boxes [Law, case law].","t":"A pre-ticked box is not valid consent (Planet49, decided on cookies, applying the same GDPR consent standard).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Evidence [Guidance].","t":"Keep a proportionate record that links each consent to when and how it was given, the purposes, and the wording and interface version shown. Do not collect extra IP addresses or device data only to make the record look stronger.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Double opt-in [Inference].","t":"It helps as evidence and filters typos. The cited provisions do not require it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 4(11), 7(1)-(4), Recital 32. EDPB Guidelines 05/2020, paragraphs 43-45, 64-65 and 104-108, printed pp. 22-23. CJEU Planet49, paragraphs 52-65 and 74-81.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-EMAIL-05, F-GDPR-BASIS-05, F-DEVICE-04, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, F-EMAIL-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"7. What every promotional email must carry","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"A promotional email must not hide or misstate the sender. It must give a valid, free address or number for stop requests. It must not breach e-commerce rules or push people to sites that do. Its commercial nature and the person it represents must be identifiable. Art. 50(3) also applies to legal persons.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Right to object [Law].","t":"A person can object to direct marketing at any time, and you must then stop that use. There is no balancing test. Bring this right to their attention clearly and separately from other information, at the latest in the first communication.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Art. 50(3)-(4). Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 13(2),(4). Directive 2000/31/EC, Art. 6(a)-(d). GDPR Art. 21(2)-(5), read with Art. 21(1)-(2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-11, F-ECOMMERCE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-M03, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"8. Open and click tracking in event emails","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law and Guidance].","t":"Storing or reading information on a person's device needs consent after clear information, unless access is only to transmit the communication or is strictly necessary for a service the person expressly asked for. The EDPB treats tracking pixels and tracked links, including in email, as storage and access mechanisms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What this means here [Inference].","t":"Knowing who opened the joining-link email is not needed to deliver it. The simplest path is to turn open and click tracking off for event mail.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Art. 43(4), first and second sentences. Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 5(3). EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 v2.0, Section 3.1, paragraphs 46-51.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-DEVICE-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"9. Retention and the suppression record","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"State how long you keep each data set, or the criteria that decide it. \"As long as necessary\" needs enough detail for a person to understand what decides the period.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Suppression [Inference].","t":"A minimal record of refused addresses can stop them being re-imported. No provision names this list. Give it a lawful purpose, access controls and a review period, and never reuse it for marketing. It is not kept forever by default.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 13(2)(a), 5(1)(b),(c),(e),(f), 21(3). WP260 rev.01, Annex, storage-period row, printed pp. 38-39.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-EMAIL-08, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"10. The provider that stores the list and sends the mail","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"Assess each activity separately. A provider that processes the list on your behalf is your processor. You need a written contract or other binding legal act that covers the subject, duration, nature, purpose, data types, people affected and your rights. Sub-processors need your prior specific or general written authorisation, and general authorisation needs change notices and a chance to object.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Co-hosts [Law].","t":"If you and a co-host jointly decide what happens to the list, you need an Art. 26 arrangement and must make its essence available to people.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"US providers [Law and Guidance].","t":"The EU-US Data Privacy Framework covers only US organisations on the official DPF List, within the scope of their certification. Check the list entry. DPF transfers need no extra transfer tool, but you still need Art. 28 terms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Notice [Law].","t":"Say whether data go to a third country, whether an adequacy decision exists, and for other routes which safeguard applies and how to get a copy. Do not claim a safeguard you have not established.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Practice [Inference].","t":"Some sending providers keep account data and logs in the United States whatever sending region you pick. Read the provider's region and DPA pages for your plan before you write the transfer line.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 4(7), 4(8), 26(1)-(3), 28(1)-(4), 28(9), 28(10), 13(1)(f). Decision 2023/1795, Art. 1 and Annex I, Section I.3. EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses, Question 3, page 4, Question 3.2, printed p. 5, and Question 3.3, pages 5-6. EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part II, paragraphs 112-114 and 143-145.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-03, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"11. Rights requests and complaints","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"Answer a rights request without undue delay and within one month. You can extend by two further months for complexity or volume if you explain why within the first month.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Croatia [Law].","t":"AZOP (Agencija za zaštitu osobnih podataka) is the supervisory authority under Art. 4 of the Croatian GDPR implementing act, NN 42/2018. Its contact page is https://azop.hr/kontakt/. Put the complaint route in the notice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Art. 12(3)-(4). Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018, Art. 4(1)-(3). AZOP, Kontakt page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02, N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"12. Reusing old signups","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"Further use for a new purpose, without consent or a qualifying law, needs a compatibility assessment and advance information. A new notice or a newly named basis does not establish compatibility on its own.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What this means here [Inference].","t":"New consent wording does not turn earlier workshop signups into marketing consent. Keep the original wording, source and date for each list. Do not send a blanket re-permission email to an old list, because that email can itself be marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 5(1)(b), 6(4)(a)-(e), 13(3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-BASIS-M02.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Put a short notice under the email field.","t":"One line says what you use the email for and links to the full notice. Example:","lk":[]},{"k":"q","t":"We use your email to send the workshop link and one reminder. See Privacy."},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: open the page in a private window and read the line before you submit anything.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: notice text next to the form before submit, a privacy link, and whether that link returns a real page. A 404, or a response identical to the homepage shell, counts as no notice found.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Collect only what the event needs.","t":"An email address is usually enough. Make a name optional, or drop it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: list the form fields and match each one to a purpose in the notice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: the number and names of input fields.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Add one separate, unticked box per marketing purpose.","t":"Example:","lk":[]},{"k":"q","t":"[ ] Email me about future workshops. Unsubscribe any time."},{"k":"q","t":"[ ] Email me studio news. Unsubscribe any time."},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"If you want only one box, it names one purpose, and you send nothing else under it. Do not add an \"I agree to the privacy policy\" box.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: submit the form with both boxes empty and confirm the signup still works.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: checkbox count, whether any box has the checked attribute on load, and whether each label names a single purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Record each choice.","t":"Store the address, each purpose chosen, the time in UTC, the page, and a version id for the exact wording shown.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: make a test signup with an address you control and read the stored row.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: nothing. This is an owner answer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Keep service emails clean.","t":"The confirmation, joining link and reminder carry no upsell and no request to join your news.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: read each template. Mark it service, promotion or mixed (Q-213).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: nothing on the site. The owner can forward a test message.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Turn off open and click tracking for event mail.","t":"If you want it later, put it behind consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: check the provider setting. In a test message, look for a 1x1 image and for links rewritten through a tracking domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: only a test message that the owner supplies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Choose and check the provider.","t":"Confirm the DPA applies to your account and plan, where account data and logs are stored, the sub-processor list, and the DPF List entry or the SCCs for any US path. Name the provider or its category in the notice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: save the DPA version and the date you accepted it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: the domain the form posts to, and public DNS records for the sending domain. These hint at the provider. They do not prove which terms you accepted.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Set retention.","t":"Pick a period for the event-only list that ends a short time after the event, and write it in the notice. Keep the marketing list only while consent stands. Give the suppression record a purpose and a review date. The exact numbers are your decision, not a rule from the sources.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a scheduled deletion job or a dated calendar task exists.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: whether the notice states a period or criteria.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Wire the unsubscribe.","t":"Every promotional email names the sender, gives a working stop link and a reply address, and states the right to object separately from other text. A stop request reaches every list, automation and second tool.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: unsubscribe a test address, then trigger a promotional send and confirm it does not arrive.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: nothing on the site. This is an owner test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Check what the signup page loads.","t":"Remove analytics you do not read. If you track signup steps, send only event names, never the email or form values.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: open the browser network panel, focus the field, submit, and search the request bodies for your test address.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: third-party requests that fire on page load, on field focus and on submit, and whether any payload carries the typed email.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Hold promotion to old lists.","t":"Before you promote anything to an existing list, find the wording people saw. If you cannot show it, send only service messages to that list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each list has a stored wording version and source.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: nothing. This is an owner answer.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"One box for everything.","t":"\"I agree to the privacy policy and to receive news\" bundles a notice with consent and joins two purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A pre-ticked box.","t":"It is not consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"The notice only in the confirmation email.","t":"It arrives after collection, which is too late.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating a free signup as a customer relationship.","t":"The Croatian text uses narrower wording than the Directive, and Inteligo turned on its own facts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Update\" emails that sell.","t":"A label does not change what a message is.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Asking for marketing consent inside the joining-link email.","t":"That request can itself be marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"SMS reminders with a promotion inside.","t":"Art. 50(1) covers SMS and MMS too.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Tracking on by default.","t":"The EDPB treats tracking pixels and tracked links as device storage and access, so open and click tracking in event mail can need consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Reading \"EU sending region\" as \"EU storage\".","t":"Check where the provider keeps account data and logs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A privacy link that goes nowhere.","t":"A 404, or an app that serves its homepage at every path, gives the person no notice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Keeping everything forever.","t":"That includes the suppression record.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Funnel events that carry the email.","t":"Analytics events should never include the address or form values.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A co-host who reuses the list.","t":"Sharing the list with a partner for its own marketing is a new purpose and a new recipient.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work through these in order. Stop and ask the owner where a step needs an owner answer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Find the signup form. Add a one-line notice and a privacy link directly above the submit button.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: render the page and confirm the notice is visible without scrolling past the button.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Confirm the privacy link resolves to a page with notice content.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: request the URL and confirm HTTP 200 and a body that differs from the homepage shell.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add one unticked checkbox per marketing purpose, with its own label.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no checked attribute on load, and the form submits with every box empty.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Send each box value to the server as its own field, and store it with a UTC timestamp and a wording version id.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test signup writes one row with the purposes, time and version.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Keep the email and form values out of analytics events.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: search the network log of a test signup for the test address. It appears only in the request to your own signup endpoint.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Turn off open and click tracking for event emails, or ask the owner to.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test message contains no 1x1 image and no rewritten links.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove promotional content from the confirmation, joining-link and reminder templates.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each template is marked service in a short comment or config entry.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a footer to promotional templates only: sender name, reply address, unsubscribe link, and a separate line on the right to object.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: render a promotional template and check all four elements.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Connect the provider's unsubscribe event to the consent record and to every other list or automation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: unsubscribe a test address and confirm the record changes and no promotional send reaches it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a scheduled job or a dated owner task that deletes the event-only list after the period in the notice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the job exists and its period matches the notice text.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Ask the owner for: the provider's DPA version and acceptance date, the storage region, and the wording used for any existing list. Do not guess these.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Can a free workshop signup ever count as an address obtained \"u svrhu prodaje\" from a \"potrošač\" under ZEK Art. 50(2)? How close would the facts need to be to the Inteligo account?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Is there a contract for a free online workshop, so that GDPR Art. 6(1)(b) fits? If not, does a recorded Art. 6(1)(f) assessment hold?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does consumer law apply where a free live online session is supplied and the person gives personal data used for other purposes? The EU rules can reach digital supply in exchange for personal data (F-CONSUMER-03).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Children may sign up. Which national age applies under GDPR Art. 8 if you rely on consent, and which country's rule governs a cross-border audience? (F-SECTOR-01, F-SECTOR-02)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Recipients outside Croatia: which country's marketing rules apply before a mixed-country campaign?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"A co-hosted event: are you and the co-host separate controllers, joint controllers, or controller and processor?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If a free workshop leads to paid sessions or products, which invoice and VAT rules apply to the paid part, and does the free event itself create any reporting duty?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"All sources checked on 2026-11-07 through the claim records named above.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locators used","u":""},{"t":"Date of the text","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 4(7), 4(8), 4(11), 5(1)(b),(c),(e),(f), 6(1)(b),(f), 6(4), 7(1)-(4), 12(3)-(4), 13(1)-(4), 21(1)-(5), 26(1)-(3), 28(1)-(4),(9),(10), Recital 32","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 27 April 2016, applies from 25 May 2018","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy), consolidated","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02002L0058-20091219"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 5(3), 13(1),(2),(4),(5)","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 19 December 2009","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2000/31/EC (e-commerce), consolidated","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/31/2024-02-17/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Art. 6(a)-(d)","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 17 February 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama (ZEK), NN 76/2022","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 5(1)(54) base text, 43(4), 50(1)-(4)","u":""},{"t":"Published 4 July 2022, in force 12 July 2022","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti, NN 14/2024","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 115(1), 116","u":""},{"t":"Published 7 February 2024, in force 15 February 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK amendments, NN 45/2026","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 3, 10-13, 38","u":""},{"t":"Published 29 April 2026, in force 7 May 2026","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2018_05_42_805.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 4(1)-(3)","u":""},{"t":"Published 9 May 2018, in force 25 May 2018","u":""}],[{"t":"Inteligo Media, C-654/23, ECLI:EU:C:2025:871","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62023CJ0654"},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 38-39, 43-48, 53-69, operative points 1-2","u":""},{"t":"Judgment of 13 November 2025","u":""}],[{"t":"Planet49, C-673/17","u":""},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 52-65 and 74-81, operative part points 1 and 3","u":""},{"t":"Judgment of 1 October 2019","u":""}],[{"t":"Guidelines 05/2020 on consent","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_202005_consent_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 43-45, 64-65, 104-108","u":""},{"t":"Version 1.1, adopted 4 May 2020","u":""}],[{"t":"Guidelines 2/2019 on Art. 6(1)(b) in online services","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines-art_6-1-b-adopted_after_public_consultation_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 22-30, 45-47","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, adopted 8 October 2019","u":""}],[{"t":"Guidelines 2/2023 on the technical scope of Art. 5(3) ePrivacy","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2024-10/edpb_guidelines_202302_technical_scope_art_53_eprivacydirective_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Section 3.1, paragraphs 46-51","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, adopted 7 October 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Part II, paragraphs 112-114, 143-145","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, adopted 7 July 2021","u":""}],[{"t":"Guidelines on transparency, WP260 rev.01","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-09/wp260rev01_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party, endorsed by the EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 35-36, Annex storage-period row","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 11 April 2018","u":""}],[{"t":"Endorsement 1/2018","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/sites/default/files/files/news/endorsement_of_wp29_documents_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Item 2","u":""},{"t":"25 May 2018","u":""}],[{"t":"EU-US Data Privacy Framework FAQ for European businesses","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-04/edpb_dpf_faq-for-businesses_v2_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Question 3, page 4, Question 3.2, Question 3.3, pages 5-6","u":""},{"t":"Version 2, adopted 15 January 2026","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/1795/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Art. 1, Annex I, Section I.3","u":""},{"t":"10 July 2023","u":""}],[{"t":"Zlonamjerne i neželjene EK","u":"https://www.hakom.hr/hr/zlonamjerne-i-nezeljene-ek/11398"},{"t":"HAKOM","u":""},{"t":"\"Neželjene elektroničke komunikacije\", first two paragraphs","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Kolačići i GDPR","u":"https://azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Separate category controls, policy must match installed tools","u":""},{"t":"Published 14 August 2026","u":""}],[{"t":"Kontakt","u":"https://azop.hr/kontakt/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"\"Kontakt\" and \"HELP - DESK\" sections","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-04","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: One inbox for a one-person business with several domains","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or sole trader in Croatia with a few brand domains, a site that sends confirmation emails, and perhaps a newsletter.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-058, Q-062, Q-083, Q-085, Q-086, Q-106, Q-108, Q-211, Q-213, Q-215]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-08, F-EMAIL-11, F-GDPR-BASIS-07, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-01, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"inbox":{"title":"One inbox for a one-person business with several domains","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"#","u":""},{"t":"Fact","u":""},{"t":"Why it changes the answer","u":""},{"t":"Question id","u":""}],[{"t":"1","u":""},{"t":"Which tools send mail as each domain, and who set each one up","u":""},{"t":"Each sender needs its own SPF entry or subdomain, DKIM key and vendor terms","u":""},{"t":"Q-083","u":""}],[{"t":"2","u":""},{"t":"Which companies, locations and support teams can reach the mail, logs and backups","u":""},{"t":"Decides the processor list and whether a transfer happens","u":""},{"t":"Q-085, Q-106","u":""}],[{"t":"3","u":""},{"t":"Whether a US sending tool's recipient entity is actively on the EU-US DPF List","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether you may need another Chapter V route, such as SCCs, instead","u":""},{"t":"Q-108","u":""}],[{"t":"4","u":""},{"t":"Whether the vendor's DPA binds your exact account and plan","u":""},{"t":"A public DPA does not prove which terms your account accepted","u":""},{"t":"Q-086","u":""}],[{"t":"5","u":""},{"t":"Whether each message is marketing, a requested service message, or mixed","u":""},{"t":"A confirmation that also sells something can need send permission","u":""},{"t":"Q-058, Q-213","u":""}],[{"t":"6","u":""},{"t":"Whether Croatian law governs the campaign or the recipient","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether ZEK Article 50 is the starting rule","u":""},{"t":"Q-211","u":""}],[{"t":"7","u":""},{"t":"Whether an unsubscribe in one tool reaches every other tool","u":""},{"t":"Matters most when you merge or drop a newsletter tool","u":""},{"t":"Q-062, Q-215","u":""}],[{"t":"8","u":""},{"t":"Which addresses are separate mailboxes and which are aliases","u":""},{"t":"Decides how many inboxes you check and pay for","u":""},{"t":"Technical, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"9","u":""},{"t":"Whether wildcard DNS records are intentional, for example for preview or tenant subdomains","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether a non-mail policy at the root is enough","u":""},{"t":"Technical, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"10","u":""},{"t":"Whether a domain sends or receives any mail at all","u":""},{"t":"Decides between a mail setup and a non-mail policy","u":""},{"t":"Technical, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"11","u":""},{"t":"Who controls DNS and the registrar","u":""},{"t":"Decides who can make and roll back changes","u":""},{"t":"Technical, no kit question yet","u":""}]]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"Marketing email to individuals needs prior consent (Croatia)","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Email direct promotion and sales to an individual needs prior consent. The same rule covers SMS and MMS.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Croatian law applies, the recipient is a natural person, and the purpose is promotional.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The customer exception in Article 50(2), and the legal-person carve-out in Article 50(4). Assess each separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama (ZEK), NN 76/2022, Article 50(1), (2) and (4). Amendment chain: NN 14/2024, Article 115(1), repeals Article 41 only. NN 45/2026 leaves Article 50 unchanged and entered into force on 7 May 2026. It renumbers the consumer definition from Article 5(1)(54) to 5(1)(56). English wording is a researcher translation, not verified.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"The EU baseline and the customer exception","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The EU starting rule for email marketing to natural-person subscribers is prior consent. A customer exception lets the same sender market its own similar products or services to customers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions for the exception.","t":"You obtained the address from your customer in a sale context. You market your own similar offerings. Collection and every message offer a clear, easy and free objection. The person did not refuse at the start.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions and limits.","t":"Bought lists do not qualify. National law decides protection for legal-person subscribers. Where the customer exception applies, Inteligo Media holds that the sending needs no separate GDPR Article 6(1) assessment, because of GDPR Article 95. The ruling does not cure an address that was collected unlawfully, and it does not cover unrelated profiling.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Directive 2002/58/EC (consolidated 19 December 2009), Article 13(1), (2) and (5). GDPR Articles 6(1) and 95. CJEU, Inteligo Media, C-654/23, 13 November 2025, paragraphs 38, 47 to 48 and 63, and paragraphs 48 to 69 with operative rulings 1 and 2.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Sender identity and a free stop channel always apply","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"You must not hide or disguise the sender. Every marketing message needs a valid, free address or number to stop further messages. A message must not push people to a site that breaks e-commerce information rules.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Any commercial email, including to companies. Article 50(4) excludes legal persons only from paragraphs 1 and 2, so paragraph 3 still applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters for setup.","t":"A From domain that does not identify you, or a no-reply address with no working Reply-To, can work against this rule.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Article 50(3) and (4). Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 13(4). Directive 2000/31/EC (consolidation of 17 February 2024), Article 6(a) to (d).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-01, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-11.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"An objection must stop marketing in every tool","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A person can object to direct marketing at any time. You must stop that use. No balancing test lets you continue.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"GDPR applies to the processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Limits.","t":"A small suppression record can stop a refused address from being reimported. That is an implementation inference, not an express duty. It needs its own basis, minimal data and a retention limit. Never reuse it for marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679), Article 21(2) to (5). Articles 5(1)(b) to (f), 6(1) and 21(3) for the suppression record. Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 13(2) and (4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-EMAIL-08, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Consent needs evidence you can produce","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Where you rely on consent, you must be able to show it. Withdrawal must be as easy as giving consent. A pre-ticked box is not consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters for setup.","t":"If you drop a newsletter tool, the evidence of how each contact joined can go with it. New copy cannot recreate old consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(11) and 7(1) to (4). Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 2(f), read with GDPR Article 94(2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-EMAIL-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Your mail host and sending tools are usually processors","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A vendor that stores or sends mail for you, on your behalf, is usually a processor. Processing must rest on a written contract or other binding legal act with set contents.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The vendor handles personal data, such as client messages, contact lists, delivery logs or DMARC failure reports.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What to check.","t":"The contract covers subject, duration, nature, purpose, data types and the people affected. Sub-processors need your prior authorisation, and with general authorisation you get notice of changes and a chance to object. At the end of the service you choose return or deletion. Your duty to check guarantees continues after you sign.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions and limits.","t":"Roles depend on what each party actually decides, not on contract labels. A vendor that uses data for its own purposes may be a controller for that part.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8), 28(1) to (4), 28(3)(g), 28(9) and 28(10). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor, paragraphs 94 to 99, 112 to 114 and 143 to 145.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"A sending region is not the same as where your data lives","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A tool can send from an EU region and still store account data, metadata and logs elsewhere. If a separate entity in a third country can access personal data, that is a transfer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You are subject to GDPR, you make data available to another entity, and that entity is outside the EEA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Mechanisms.","t":"DPF adequacy covers only US organisations actively on the official DPF List, within their listed scope. Certifications renew yearly. DPF does not replace Article 28 terms. DPF-covered transfers need no Article 46 tool. Without DPF coverage, you need another Chapter V route, such as an Article 46 safeguard like SCCs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Notice.","t":"Your privacy notice must name recipients or their categories, and state any third-country transfer and its safeguard.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paragraphs 9 to 13. Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795, Article 1 and Annex I, Section I.3. EDPB DPF FAQ for businesses (2026), Question 3 (page 4), Questions 3.1 and 3.3. EDPB information note on the US adequacy decision (July 2023), Question 1. EDPB Recommendations 01/2020, Section 2.1, paragraphs 8 to 14. GDPR Articles 13(1)(e) to (f) and 14(1)(e) to (f).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Vendor rule, not law: Gmail sender guidelines","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"All senders to personal Gmail accounts need SPF or DKIM, valid forward and reverse DNS, TLS, a spam rate below 0.3% in Postmaster Tools, and messages formatted to RFC 5322. Senders of more than 5,000 messages a day to Gmail accounts also need SPF and DKIM, a DMARC record (p=none is allowed), From-domain alignment and one-click unsubscribe for marketing. DKIM keys must be 1024 bits or longer, and 2048 is recommended.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters.","t":"A small sender is far below 5,000 a day, but meeting the bulk rules anyway helps delivery.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"support.google.com/mail/answer/81126, checked 2026-11-07. No claim id.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Technical standards, not law","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"SPF","t":"(RFC 7208). Lists which servers may send for a domain. ~all is a soft fail, -all a hard fail. An SPF record may cause at most 10 DNS lookups (section 4.6.4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"DKIM","t":"(RFC 6376). Signs each message with a key published at <selector>._domainkey.<domain>.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"DMARC","t":"(RFC 9989, which with RFC 9990 and 9991 obsoletes RFC 7489). Final handling is \"left to the discretion of the Mail Receiver\" (section 5.4). When sp is absent, the p policy applies to subdomains (sections 4.7 and 4.10.1). Read in part only. Other details, such as pct, are not re-verified.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Null MX","t":"(RFC 7505, section 3). MX 0 . says a domain has no mail exchanger. It does not stop anyone spoofing the domain in a From address.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Implicit MX","t":"(RFC 5321, section 5.1). With no explicit MX, a sender falls back to the domain's address records. Cited from knowledge, not fetched.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each step says how you verify it, and what an outside check can show. Here it reads public DNS only. It sees MX, root SPF, the _dmarc record, DKIM at known selector names (presence only), random-label behaviour that points to a wildcard, and null MX. It cannot see mailbox count, aliases, delivery, which tool sent a message, consent evidence or vendor contracts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Write an inventory.","t":"List each domain, each address (mailbox or alias), and each tool that sends as each domain. No passwords.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the list matches your mail host's admin console and each sending tool's domain settings.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: lists MX hosts, SPF includes, DMARC tags and DKIM at known selectors per domain. Cannot see mailboxes or aliases.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Read one real header from each sending system.","t":"Look at From, Reply-To, Return-Path, the DKIM d= domain, and the SPF and DMARC results in Authentication-Results.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: dmarc=pass, with the DKIM d= or the envelope domain aligned to the From domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: cannot see headers. Only you can supply one.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Check an upgrade in place first.","t":"In your current mail host's console, confirm for your plan: IMAP or API access, aliases, domain aliases, send-as from an alias, extra domains, the price shown to you, and any annual commitment.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a dated screenshot or plan page saved with your records.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: nothing. MX shows routing only, not plan or features.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Collapse to one mailbox.","t":"Turn role addresses such as hello@ and info@ into aliases of one mailbox. Set replies to go out from the alias the mail arrived at.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: from an outside account, write to each alias, reply, and check the From on the reply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: MX for yourdomain.com unchanged.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Give each sending brand domain a reply route.","t":"If yourproduct.com sends confirmations but has no explicit MX, a reply can fall back to the web host and get lost. Either set Reply-To to your main mailbox, or add MX records and one alias such as contact@yourproduct.com. Add a root SPF record and a DMARC record starting at p=none.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: reply to a real confirmation from an outside account and confirm it lands.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: MX present or absent, root SPF present, _dmarc present with p=none.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Send DMARC reports to a dedicated alias.","t":"Point rua at dmarc@yourdomain.com with a filter, so reports stay out of client mail. Drop ruf, or point it at the same alias, because failure reports can carry message headers and content. A third-party report service that reads them is a processor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the _dmarc record shows the new rua and no ruf, or ruf at the alias.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: reads the rua and ruf addresses.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Give non-mail domains a non-mail policy.","t":"For spare-domain.com, if you confirm it sends and receives nothing: null MX 0 ., SPF v=spf1 -all, and DMARC p=reject.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"First: list every subdomain in use. If random labels resolve (a wildcard), a root null MX does not cover subdomains that fall back to the wildcard address. Do not delete the wildcard or add a wildcard MX until preview, tenant and mail subdomains are checked. Check that your DNS host accepts a wildcard MX before relying on one.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no tool you use sends as spare-domain.com (step 1 and DMARC reports).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: sees null MX, -all, p=reject, and whether random labels resolve.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Move campaigns to one tool on a sending subdomain.","t":"For example news.yourdomain.com, with its own SPF, DKIM and DMARC. Before you drop a tool, export how each contact joined (form wording, source, date, purpose) and the suppression list. Import the suppression list into the tool you keep. Then remove the dropped tool's SPF include and DKIM key.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: unsubscribe a test address in one place and confirm no tool still mails it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: SPF include gone, DKIM gone at known selectors. Selector probing cannot prove a key is absent, especially under a wildcard.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Collect vendor paperwork per service.","t":"For each remaining vendor: a DPA that binds your account, the sub-processor list and how changes are notified, where storage and logs sit, the transfer mechanism, and the exit and deletion process.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: dated copies stored with your records, and the DPF List entry checked on the day for any US recipient.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Tighten DMARC slowly.","t":"When aggregate reports show only your own senders for a few weeks, consider p=quarantine. Set sp on purpose, because without it the root policy also applies to subdomains.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: aggregate reports after the change show no legitimate mail failing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: reads p and sp.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Migrate only if step 3 fails.","t":"Use the cutover below.","lk":[]}],"children":[{"h":"Cutover with rollback","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Common practice, not a legal requirement. Do one domain at a time.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Save the current MX, SPF, DKIM and DMARC values and their TTLs in a rollback note.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Lower the TTL on the MX record a day or two before the switch.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"At the new host, create the mailbox, aliases and send-as first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Copy old mail across and compare folder counts. Keep a local export.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"Add the new host's SPF include and DKIM key next to the old ones. Both can coexist during the overlap. Watch the 10-lookup SPF limit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"Switch MX. Keep the old account active and paid through the overlap.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"","t":"Test inbound from an outside account. Watch bounces and DMARC aggregate reports.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"","t":"Rollback: put the saved MX values back. This works while the old account is still active and the TTL is low.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"","t":"After a stable period, remove the old SPF include and DKIM key. Ask the old host for return or deletion of your data under GDPR Article 28(3)(g) (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07). Keep your export.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A wildcard A record.","t":"Random subdomains resolve to your web host. A root null MX then does not cover them, and mail to a mistyped subdomain falls back to that address. The wildcard also makes DKIM probes return empty answers, so a checker cannot prove a key is absent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Mistaking a bounce subdomain for a sending identity.","t":"Many sending tools ask for a return-path subdomain, such as send.yourdomain.com, for bounces. The visible From usually still uses the root domain, and the DKIM signature often sits on the root. Check your own headers (step 2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Reading p=none as \"receivers do nothing\".","t":"It means you request no action. Receivers still filter or reject on their own policies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Leaving out sp.","t":"Without it, a root move to reject also hits subdomains that have no DMARC record of their own.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating a campaign subdomain as a firewall.","t":"It helps keep campaign reputation apart, but receivers can still weigh the parent domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Believing null MX, -all and p=reject stop spoofing.","t":"They reduce misuse of the exact domain. They do nothing about lookalike domains or display-name abuse.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Stale SPF includes.","t":"An include for a tool you stopped using keeps that tool authorised to send as you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Using forwarding as the design.","t":"Forwarding can break SPF and makes replies messy. Use it as a bridge only.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Assuming the sending region is the storage region.","t":"Read the vendor's region page and DPA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Dropping a newsletter tool without exporting join evidence and suppressions.","t":"You lose your consent proof and can re-mail people who objected.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A confirmation email that drifts into marketing.","t":"A joining link is usually a service message. A renewal offer, another product or a \"join our list\" request may be marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"DMARC failure reports in the client inbox.","t":"They can carry message content, which is personal data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Personal webmail as a product-site contact.","t":"It is a valid choice. The questions are continuity, who can reach the mail, and how long it is kept.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Read-only by default. Propose DNS changes as a diff for the owner to approve. Never log in, send test mail to third parties, or open SMTP connections.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each domain, record current values and TTLs before any change.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +noall +answer MX yourdomain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +short TXT yourdomain.com (look for one v=spf1 record only)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +short TXT _dmarc.yourdomain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Probe for a wildcard with two random labels.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +short A zq7-check.yourdomain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If both resolve, flag \"wildcard likely\" and stop before proposing a root null MX.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Check DKIM at selector names the owner gives you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +short TXT <selector>._domainkey.yourdomain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Report presence and key length only. Never paste key material or verification tokens into a report.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Count SPF DNS lookups (each include, a, mx, ptr, exists and redirect). Flag more than 10.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Flag a sending domain with no explicit MX and no stated Reply-To route.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Flag ruf pointing at a working inbox.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Flag p=reject or a null MX proposal on any domain that a tool still sends from.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Write a rollback note with old values before the owner applies a change. After the change, re-run the same lookups and diff them against the proposal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Do not wire an AI assistant to live client mail until the owner confirms processor terms, a lawful basis, notice changes and any client permissions are in place. Drafts only, a human sends.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does Croatian law govern a list with recipients in several countries, and which national rule applies to each (Q-211)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How does the ZEK consumer definition (Article 5(1)(56) after NN 45/2026) work inside Article 50(2)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How should sole traders, obrtnici, private renters and named employee addresses be treated? An obrtnik is a natural person under the Obrt Act, Article 4 (N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Is a given renewal reminder, follow-up offer or consent-request email marketing (Q-058, Q-213)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does each vendor's DPA and transfer mechanism hold for this exact account and plan (Q-086, Q-108)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"What retention period suits the consent evidence and the suppression record?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Before any AI tool reads live client mail: controller and processor roles, the Article 6 basis, any Article 9 material, confidentiality, client authorisation of sub-processors, transparency and transfers. A pilot, a no-training setting or human send approval does not replace these decisions.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How are foreign SaaS subscriptions invoiced and booked for VAT for a Croatian sole trader?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How is an annual prepayment for mail tools booked?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Law, case law and official guidance (with claim ids)","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Claim ids","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama, NN 76/2022, narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html"},{"t":"Article 50(1) to (4)","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-01","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti, NN 14/2024, narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html"},{"t":"Articles 115(1), 116","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK amendments, NN 45/2026, narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html"},{"t":"Articles 3, 10 to 13, 38. In force 7 May 2026","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03","u":""}],[{"t":"HAKOM laws register, hakom.hr/hr/zakoni-2038/2038","u":"https://hakom.hr/hr/zakoni-2038/2038"},{"t":"ZEK list","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o obrtu, NN 143/2013, narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2013_12_143_3065.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2013_12_143_3065.html"},{"t":"Articles 2(1) to (2), 4","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-02","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC, consolidated 19 December 2009, CELEX 02002L0058-20091219","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02002L0058-20091219"},{"t":"Articles 2(f), 13(1), (2), (4), (5)","u":""},{"t":"F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-08, F-EMAIL-11","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2000/31/EC, consolidation of 17 February 2024","u":""},{"t":"Article 6(a) to (d)","u":""},{"t":"F-EMAIL-11","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU, Inteligo Media, C-654/23, 13 November 2025, ECLI:EU:C:2025:871","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 38, 47 to 48, 63 (F-EMAIL-02). Paragraphs 48 to 69 and operative rulings 1 and 2 (F-GDPR-BASIS-07)","u":""},{"t":"F-EMAIL-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)","u":""},{"t":"Articles 4(7), 4(8), 4(11), 5(1), 6(1), 7, 95, 13(1)(e) to (f), 14(1)(e) to (f), 21(2) to (5), 28(1) to (4), 28(3)(g), 28(9), 28(10)","u":""},{"t":"F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-08, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-BASIS-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 94 to 99, 112 to 114, 143 to 145","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021 on Article 3 and Chapter V","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 9 to 13","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Recommendations 01/2020 on supplementary measures","u":""},{"t":"Section 2.1, paragraphs 8 to 14","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795 (EU-US DPF)","u":""},{"t":"Article 1, Annex I Section I.3","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB DPF FAQ for businesses, version 2 (2026)","u":""},{"t":"Question 3 (page 4), Questions 3.1 and 3.3","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB information note on the US adequacy decision (July 2023)","u":""},{"t":"Question 1","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"All claims above are draft research with legal review not requested, checked 2026-11-07. Croatian texts are researcher translations.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Technical standards and vendor rules (no claim ids)","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Status","u":""}],[{"t":"Google, Email sender guidelines, support.google.com/mail/answer/81126","u":"https://support.google.com/mail/answer/81126"},{"t":"Scope, all-sender rules, more than 5,000 a day, DKIM key length","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 9989 (DMARC), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9989","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9989"},{"t":"Sections 4.7, 4.10.1, 5.4","u":""},{"t":"Read in part, 2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 7489 info page, rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7489","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7489"},{"t":"Obsoleted by RFC 9989, 9990, 9991","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 7505 (null MX), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7505","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7505"},{"t":"Section 3","u":""},{"t":"Read, 2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 5321 (SMTP), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5321","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5321"},{"t":"Section 5.1, implicit MX","u":""},{"t":"Cited from knowledge, not fetched","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 7208 (SPF), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7208","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7208"},{"t":"Section 4.6.4, lookup limit","u":""},{"t":"Cited from knowledge, not fetched","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 6376 (DKIM), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376"},{"t":"Selector and key record","u":""},{"t":"Cited from knowledge, not fetched","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-05","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Email campaigns to mixed lists from Croatia","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A small Croatian business, such as a solo studio, that mails individuals, sole traders, companies and past buyers from more than one signup form","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-057, Q-058, Q-059, Q-060, Q-062, Q-199, Q-201, Q-205, Q-206, Q-214]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-03, F-EMAIL-04, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-07, F-EMAIL-08, F-EMAIL-09, F-EMAIL-10, F-EMAIL-11, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-02, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-04, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-06, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-03, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-04, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-05, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-06, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-01, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-02, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-03, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-04, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-05, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-06, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-07, F-GDPR-BASIS-05, F-GDPR-BASIS-06, F-GDPR-BASIS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-ECOMMERCE-03, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"campaigns":{"title":"Email campaigns to mixed lists from Croatia","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who the recipient is","t":"(Q-057, Q-199). An individual consumer, a sole trader or obrtnik, a company, or a named employee at a company. Each one takes a different route. Ask for the document that shows legal form, such as a court register or obrt register extract. A company-looking domain does not prove legal form.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What kind of mailbox it is","t":"(Q-201). A role address like info@yourdomain.com and a named address like ana@yourdomain.com raise different questions. A named address can be personal data, even at work.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What the email is for","t":"(Q-058). A service message, a marketing message, or a mix. A booking confirmation is service. An upsell inside it makes it mixed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Where each address came from","t":"(Q-059). Which form, which wording, which purpose, and whether the person refused marketing at that point.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether a sale happened","t":"(Q-205). The customer route needs an address that you, the same trader, got from your own consumer for a sale.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the new offer is similar","t":"(Q-206). Your own similar products only. Not a partner's products and not an unrelated line.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether you can prove the route","t":"(Q-060, Q-214). Consent wording, date, form and choice, or an order record for a past buyer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether an unsubscribe reaches every system","t":"(Q-062). Imports, automations, processors and every list.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"1. Prior consent is the starting rule","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"You may send direct promotion or sales by email, SMS or MMS only with the end user's consent, obtained in advance.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Croatian law governs the campaign. The message is promotional. The recipient is an end user.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The customer route (rule 2) and the legal-person carve-out (rule 3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK, NN 76/2022, Art. 50(1). EU counterpart: Directive 2002/58/EC Art. 13(1). HAKOM's consumer page says the same in short form.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-02, F-EMAIL-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"2. The existing-customer route is narrow","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A trader may use email addresses it obtained from its own consumers \"u svrhu prodaje\" (for the purpose of selling). It may use them only for its own similar products or services.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"All of these must hold. Same trader. A consumer relationship. Collection for a sale. A similar own offering. A clear, free, easy way to object at collection and in every message. No refusal at the start. The address was lawfully obtained in the first place.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None of these qualify: bought lists, a related company's customers, third-party offers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Wording gap.","t":"The Croatian text says \"potrošača\" (consumers) and \"for the purpose of selling\". The Directive says \"customers\" and \"in the context of the sale\". A cautious reading is that an enquiry with no completed sale gets no customer route. A broader reading is possible. Neither is confirmed. Claim id for the wording comparison: N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Free signups.","t":"The CJEU in Inteligo Media (C-654/23, 13 November 2025) treated one free publishing account, linked to paid content, as a sale context. It did not approve every free download, lead magnet or event registration. A free online workshop signup is not automatically a customer relationship.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK Art. 50(2). Directive 2002/58/EC Art. 13(2). Inteligo paras 38-39, 43-48, 53-63 and operative point 1.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-03, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-06, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-04, F-EMAIL-10.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"3. The legal-person carve-out covers legal persons only","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to communication sent to legal persons. Paragraph 3 still applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The actual recipient is a legal person, for example a d.o.o. or j.d.o.o., and Croatian law applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions and limits.","t":"An obrtnik is a natural person under Zakon o obrtu Art. 4. A business purpose does not create legal personality. A personal address in a business directory did not become a legal-person recipient in a 2019 HAKOM inspector decision. That decision applied the old Art. 107 and is historical. Its appeal outcome was not checked. Whether an email to a named employee counts as communication \"to the legal person\" is open.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"EU note.","t":"Directive Art. 13(5) leaves protection of non-natural persons to member states, with a duty to protect their legitimate interests. There is no EU-wide permission for cold B2B email.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK Art. 50(3)-(4). Zakon o obrtu NN 143/2013 Arts. 2(1)-(2) and 4, amended NN 127/2019, corrected NN 41/2020. NN 114/2026 amends that Act from 1 January 2027. HAKOM decision UP/I-344-07/19-01/03, 4 March 2019, pp. 2-3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-01, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-02, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-03, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-04, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-07, F-EMAIL-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"4. Who counts as a consumer in ZEK","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"ZEK defines \"potrošač\" as a natural person who uses or requests a public electronic communications service for purposes outside their business, trade (obrt) or profession. \"Krajnji korisnik\" (end user) is a user who does not provide public networks or services.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"NN 45/2026 Art. 3 renumbered the definitions. The consumer is now Art. 5(1) point 56 (was 54). User is point 35 (was 33). End user is point 36 (was 34). The wording did not change.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters.","t":"A sole trader or a private holiday renter who buys for their business is likely an end user, so Art. 50(1) likely applies. If they are not a \"potrošač\", Art. 50(2) may not cover them. They are not a legal person, so Art. 50(4) does not exempt them. On that plain reading, prior consent is the cautious route for this group. Counsel must confirm it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022 Art. 5(1), Art. 5(2) (consent takes its meaning from data protection law). NN 45/2026 Art. 3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03. These cover the consumer point only. The user and end-user point numbers come from a researcher reading of NN 45/2026 Art. 3 and have no claim id yet.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"5. Every promotional email has to meet three safeguards","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Do not send promotional email that hides or misstates the sender and breaks e-commerce rules. Do not send it without a valid address or number where the recipient can ask, free of charge, for messages to stop. Do not send email that encourages visits to websites that break e-commerce rules.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Applies to every recipient, including legal persons.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Wording gap.","t":"Art. 50(3) joins the hidden-sender clause and the e-commerce clause with \"i\" (and). The matching offence in Art. 170(1) uses \"ili\" (or). The same three habits satisfy both readings: name the sender, follow the e-commerce rules and give a working stop address.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"E-commerce link.","t":"ePrivacy Art. 13(4) points to E-Commerce Directive Art. 6. A commercial communication must be identifiable as such and must name the person it is made for. Promotions and competitions need clear conditions. Croatia's Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini (NN 173/2003) Art. 6 requires provider identity, seat and contact details to be directly and permanently available. The Croatian article that transposes ECD Art. 6 was not verified.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK Art. 50(3). Directive 2002/58/EC Art. 13(4). Directive 2000/31/EC Art. 6(a)-(d). ZET NN 173/2003 Art. 6(1).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-05, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-06, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-11, F-ECOMMERCE-03, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"6. Consent has to meet the GDPR standard and be provable","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Consent must be freely given, specific, informed and unambiguous, by a clear affirmative act. You must be able to prove it. Withdrawal must be as easy as giving it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Applies whenever you rely on consent to send.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Details from EDPB Guidelines 05/2020.","t":"GDPR consent conditions apply to ePrivacy consent (para 7). Pre-ticked boxes and silence are not consent (para 79). Do not make consent a condition of a service that does not need it (section 3.1.2). Separate purposes need separate choices (sections 3.1.3 and 3.2). \"Correct configuration\" of the website alone is not proof (para 108). Collect only enough data to link the consent to the processing (para 106).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Double opt-in.","t":"A useful evidence practice. Neither ZEK Art. 50 nor GDPR Art. 7 requires it. It does not repair a bundled or misleading request.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 4(11), 7(1)-(4), Recital 32. Directive 2002/58/EC Art. 2(f). EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 v1.1.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-07, F-GDPR-BASIS-05, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-06.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"7. Send permission and GDPR basis are two separate questions","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Permission to send comes from ZEK Art. 50. Naming a GDPR basis such as legitimate interest never replaces a required send consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Inteligo.","t":"For processing covered by a compliant customer-route email, GDPR Art. 6(1) does not need a separate assessment. Other processing, such as tracking, profiling or list enrichment, still needs its own basis. Do not say that every soft opt-in needs a second Art. 6 basis. Do not say that GDPR disappears either.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Withdrawal.","t":"When consent is withdrawn, stop that purpose. Do not switch to legitimate interest to keep mailing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Generic mailboxes.","t":"A role address that identifies no person may fall outside GDPR. A named address usually does not.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 6(1), 7(3), 95. Inteligo paras 64-69 and operative point 2. EDPB 05/2020 paras 117-123.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"F-EMAIL-03, F-GDPR-BASIS-06, F-GDPR-BASIS-07, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-03, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"8. Notices and the right to object","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"When you collect an address directly, give GDPR Art. 13 information: who you are, purposes, basis, recipients, retention and rights. For data you got indirectly, Art. 14 usually requires it within one month, or earlier at the first message or disclosure. Check the Art. 14(5) exceptions, such as information the person already has. Bring the right to object to direct marketing to the person's attention clearly and separately, at the latest with the first message (Art. 21(4)).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Objection.","t":"A person can object to direct marketing at any time. You must stop. There is no balancing test (Art. 21(2)-(3)).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 13(1)-(4), 14(1)-(5), 21(2)-(4), 95.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"F-EMAIL-09, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-04, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-04, N-HR-EMAIL-B2B-05, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"9. Suppression after an objection","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Keep a minimal suppression record so an old import cannot bring a refused address back. This is an implementation inference, not a named legal duty.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Store only the address or a hash, the date and the reason. Document purpose, basis, access and a review period. Never reuse it for marketing. A deterministic hash of an email is still linkable and is not automatically anonymous.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 5(1)(b), (c), (e), (f), 6(1), 21(3). Directive 2002/58/EC Art. 13(2) and (4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"F-EMAIL-08, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"10. Renewal and consent-request emails can be marketing","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Classify a message by its purpose and wording, not its label. An invoice, a joining link for a booked event or an essential contract notice is usually a service message. An invitation to renew or buy another term is probably marketing. An email asking for marketing consent may itself need send permission. Do not use a service confirmation to retrofit consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK Art. 50(1) covers \"izravne promidžbe i prodaje\" (direct promotion and sales).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"None yet. The consent-request point appears as a counterexample in the F-EMAIL research file. The renewal reading is an inference. No time limit for a customer relationship was found, so do not invent one.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"11. Amendment chain and enforcement locators","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The base Act is NN 76/2022. NN 14/2024 (the Cybersecurity Act) repealed ZEK Art. 41 only, with effect from 15 February 2024. NN 45/2026 was published on 29 April 2026. Its Art. 38 brings it into force on the eighth day, which is 7 May 2026. It left Art. 50 unchanged. Older guidance cites \"Art. 107\" of the repealed 2008 Act.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Enforcement.","t":"HAKOM or AZOP can order a breach to stop under Art. 51(1). NN 45/2026 changed the starting article in Art. 51(1)-(2) from \"41.\" to \"42.\". The offences for Art. 50(1), (2) and (3) are now Art. 170(1) points 13 to 15, after NN 45/2026 Art. 29. Art. 170 is the euro penalty article (Arts. 186-187). Base brackets are EUR 13,270 to 132,720 for a legal person, EUR 2,650 to 13,270 for its responsible person and EUR 1,320 to 6,630 for a natural person.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"NN 76/2022 Arts. 51, 170, 186-187. NN 14/2024 Art. 115(1). NN 45/2026 Arts. 1, 3, 29, 38.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim ids.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03. The Art. 51 and Art. 170 locators have no claim id yet.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Pause campaigns to any list whose source you cannot show.","t":"Keep sending real service messages.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: for each list, write down the form, the exact wording shown, the date range and any objections.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. It needs an owner answer to Q-059 and Q-060.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Do not delete old evidence while tidying up.","t":"New consent text cannot create consent for people who signed up earlier. Do not send one blanket re-permission email to every list, because that email can itself be marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: old form wording and signup records are archived and dated.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Tag every contact with a route.","t":"Use one of: consent, customer, legal_person or service_only. Also record legal form (consumer, natural person for business, obrt, company, unknown) and mailbox type (role or named). Treat unknown as consent-needed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no contact in a campaign segment has route unknown.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. It reads owner answers to Q-057, Q-199 and Q-201.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Fix each signup form.","t":"One unticked choice per marketing purpose. Separate the event signup from news. A link to the privacy notice at the form. A short Art. 21 objection line for any direct marketing to an identifiable person.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: submit a test entry with every box unticked. No marketing flag is stored.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: can observe the form markup, pre-ticked boxes, whether purposes are separate controls, and whether a privacy link sits next to the form. It does not submit forms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Show who you are on the site.","t":"Provider name, seat, email and registration details, directly and permanently reachable (ZET Art. 6).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the details are one click from every page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: can observe an imprint or contact page and the listed fields.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Make every campaign email carry the sender's business name, a reply address and a free stop link.","t":"Add the separate Art. 21 notice by the first message.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: send a test campaign to yourself. Click stop. Confirm the address leaves every list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: can review a sample email only if you give it one. It cannot see what you send.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Store a consent record per contact.","t":"Wording version, timestamp in UTC, page URL, purposes chosen, confirmation time if you use double opt-in. Do not add IP addresses or device data just to look stronger.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: pick five contacts and show each record with the exact text they saw.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Wire unsubscribes to one suppression record.","t":"Every import, automation and processor reads it before sending.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: import an old CSV that contains a suppressed address. It must not become mailable.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. It reads the owner answer to Q-062.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Treating a signup for a free online workshop as permission to send newsletters or paid offers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Treating an address on a company domain as a legal person. Check the register.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Treating an obrtnik as a company because the email is about business.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Mailing past buyers of one subscription product about an unrelated product and calling it similar.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Calling a renewal pitch a service message.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Asking for consent in a promotional email and assuming the ask is free of the rules.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Listing \"legitimate interest\" in the privacy notice and treating that as send permission.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"One checkbox that bundles event updates, news and partner offers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Deleting every trace of an unsubscribe, so an old list brings the address back.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Citing old ZEK Art. 107, or the pre-2026 definition numbers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Sending to recipients outside Croatia on Croatian rules alone.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Find every form that collects an email. List its endpoint and stored fields.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: grep the codebase for email inputs and form handlers. Every hit is in the list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Make sure no marketing checkbox is pre-checked and each purpose has its own control.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test asserts that the default form state stores no marketing purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Store a consent record with these fields: email, source, route, legal_form, address_type, sale_ref, consent_text_version, objection_notice_version, timestamp (UTC), page_url, confirmation, purposes, unsubscribed_at, objection_at, suppression_reason.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test submission writes one row with the exact text version shown.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Refuse to queue a campaign for any contact whose route is unknown or whose purposes do not include the campaign topic.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a unit test with an unknown-route contact returns zero recipients.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Block customer-route sends unless sale_ref is set and the topic is marked similar by the owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a unit test without sale_ref fails to queue.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add sender business name, reply address, free unsubscribe link and the Art. 21 objection line to the campaign template.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: render the template and assert all four strings exist.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Route unsubscribe webhooks into the suppression record and check it on every import and send.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: re-import a suppressed address in a test. It stays suppressed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Keep transactional templates free of promotional blocks.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: review each transactional template for offers or upgrade links.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Do not log full addresses in debug output. Store a hash only where the suppression design needs it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: grep logs from a test run for the test address.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Questions for Croatian counsel:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"How does ZEK's own \"potrošač\" definition (Art. 5(1) point 56) work inside Art. 50(2)? How are sole traders, private renters and named employees treated?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Does \"u svrhu prodaje\" in Art. 50(2) need a completed sale, or can an enquiry or a free registration count after Inteligo?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"Does Art. 50(4) cover an email to a named employee at a company, or only role addresses?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Only if it changes advice: how should \"i\" in Art. 50(3) and \"ili\" in Art. 170(1) point 15 be read?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"Which country's rules apply to recipients outside Croatia, before a mixed-country campaign?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"Does AZOP's legitimate-interest recommendation on direct marketing fit Inteligo paras 68-69?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Questions for your accountant or registrar:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"What is the registered legal form of each business customer, and which document proves it?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Which of your trading identities made each sale, so that the sender and the customer record match?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"How long must you keep order records, so the sale reference behind each customer-route contact stays available?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Checked","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK, NN 76/2022","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 5(1) old points 33, 34, 54, Art. 5(2), Art. 50(1)-(4), Art. 51(1), Art. 170, Arts. 186-187","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti, NN 14/2024","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 115(1), repeal of ZEK Art. 41. Effective 15 February 2024","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK amendments, NN 45/2026","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 1, 3, 29, 38. Published 29 April 2026, in force 7 May 2026","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"HAKOM laws register","u":"https://www.hakom.hr/hr/zakoni-2038/2038"},{"t":"HAKOM","u":""},{"t":"ZEK amendment list","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"HAKOM, Zlonamjerne i neželjene EK","u":"https://www.hakom.hr/hr/zlonamjerne-i-nezeljene-ek/11398"},{"t":"HAKOM","u":""},{"t":"Neželjene elektroničke komunikacije, first two paragraphs","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"HAKOM inspector decision UP/I-344-07/19-01/03","u":"https://www.hakom.hr/UserDocsImages/2019/odluke_rjesenja_presude/Rje%C5%A1enje%20inspektora%20za%20D.N.%20d.o.o%20oko%20ne%C5%BEeljene%20komunikacije.pdf"},{"t":"HAKOM","u":""},{"t":"4 March 2019, pp. 2-3. Historical, old Art. 107","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o obrtu, NN 143/2013","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2013_12_143_3065.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 2(1)-(2), 4","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Obrt amendments, NN 127/2019","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2019_12_127_2560.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 1-3","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Obrt correction, NN 41/2020","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2020_04_41_880.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Cross-reference correction","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Obrt amendments, NN 114/2026","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_10_114_1370.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 1, 44. In force 1 January 2027","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2003_10_173_2504.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 6(1)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC, consolidated 19.12.2009","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02002L0058-20091219"},{"t":"EUR-Lex","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 2(f), 13(1)-(5)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2000/31/EC, consolidation 17.2.2024","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/31/2024-02-17/eng"},{"t":"EUR-Lex","u":""},{"t":"Art. 6(a)-(d)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02016R0679-20160504"},{"t":"EUR-Lex","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 4(1), 4(11), 5, 6(1), 7, 13, 14, 17(3), 21(2)-(4), 95, Recital 32","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU, Inteligo Media, C-654/23","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62023CJ0654"},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"13 November 2025, ECLI:EU:C:2025:871, paras 38-69, operative points 1-2","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_202005_consent_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"v1.1, paras 7, 79, 104-108, 113-114, 117-123, sections 3.1.2, 3.1.3, 3.2","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP legitimate-interest recommendation","u":"https://azop.hr/preporuka-za-provedbu-testa-legitimnog-interesa-prema-clanku-6-stavku-1-tocki-f-opce-uredbe-o-zastiti-podataka/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Izravni marketing passage not read, retrieval timed out","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Gaps: no HAKOM, AZOP or court source was found that settles \"potrošač\" in Art. 50(2), named employee mailboxes, or the no-sale reading. The Croatian e-commerce article on commercial communications was not verified. Cross-border choice of law was not researched.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-06","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Analytics and tracking on small sites","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small business that runs a few marketing sites, a small SaaS or a free online workshop page, and loads analytics, counters, fonts or form services from other providers.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-027, Q-028, Q-029, Q-031, Q-178, Q-181, Q-182, Q-184, Q-189, Q-075]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-02, F-DEVICE-03, F-DEVICE-05, F-DEVICE-06, F-DEVICE-07, F-DEVICE-08, F-DEVICE-09, F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-11, F-DEVICE-13, F-DEVICE-14, F-DEVICE-M01, F-DEVICE-M02, F-DEVICE-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-04, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-05, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-08, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-10, F-GDPR-BASIS-08, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"analytics":{"title":"Analytics and tracking on small sites","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each fact links to a question in questions.json. \"Unknown\" is a valid answer. It keeps the related checks visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What runs before the visitor makes a choice.","t":"If nothing optional loads on first visit, you may not need a consent banner at all. If an analytics tag loads at once, the order is the first thing to fix. (Q-178)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether each tool stores or reads anything on the device, including temporary memory.","t":"This covers cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage, in-memory IDs and scripts that read device properties such as screen size or language. (Q-027)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What each script, pixel and storage key actually does.","t":"Do not rely on its marketing label. Read the code or the network log. (Q-028)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether anything computed in the browser is sent to someone else.","t":"Use that stays wholly inside the browser is treated differently from data or results that leave it. (Q-029)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which function the visitor asked for, and whether the tool also serves another purpose.","t":"A login session for a user who signs in can be necessary. A visit total or page statistics are not something the visitor requested. (Q-031)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether your notice matches a current technical inventory.","t":"A notice that says \"no cookies\" while the page loads a third-party font, or names a tool that is no longer installed, does not match. (Q-181)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether choices are affirmative and optional categories start off.","t":"Pre-ticked boxes, silence and continued browsing are not consent. (Q-182)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether a visitor can reject on the first layer as easily as they accept.","t":"(Q-184)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether requests and device access really stop after Reject or withdrawal.","t":"A saved \"rejected\" flag is not proof. (Q-189)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who receives visitor data, and from which countries.","t":"Font CDNs, icon CDNs, analytics vendors and form relays all receive at least the visitor's IP address. (Q-075)","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"Device storage and access: the core rule","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Storing information on a visitor's device, or reading information already stored there, needs the visitor's consent after clear and complete information, particularly about purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The operation happens through an electronic communications network. The information does not have to be personal data. Planet49 confirms that the rule protects device information whether or not it identifies anyone.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"There are two. Access only to transmit a communication, and access strictly necessary for a service the visitor expressly asked for.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EU: Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy), Article 5(3), both sentences, as amended by Directive 2009/136/EC. Claims F-DEVICE-01 and F-DEVICE-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Croatia: Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama (ZEK), NN 76/2022, Article 43(4), first sentence for the rule and second sentence for the two exceptions. Claims N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01 and N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Non-personal information: CJEU C-673/17 Planet49, judgment of 1 October 2019, paragraphs 68 to 71 and operative part point 2. Claim F-DEVICE-03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Dates.","t":"ZEK took effect on 12 July 2022. NN 14/2024 (Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti) Article 115(1) repealed ZEK Article 41, from 15 February 2024. NN 45/2026 amended ZEK from 7 May 2026. Neither change touched Article 43(4). This is a provision-level check, not a full audit of Croatian law. Claims N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03 (amendment chain) and N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04 (commencement dates).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"\"Cookieless\" is not a legal conclusion","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The rule is technology-neutral. It covers cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage, temporary storage and memory. Storage and access are separate operations, and each can bring a tool into scope on its own.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A script that reads device properties, or tells the browser to send information, can be access even when nothing is stored first. IP-based tracking can be in scope when the address comes from the visitor's device. If you cannot rule out that the address comes from the device, you take the steps Article 5(3) requires.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Use wholly inside the browser that gives no other party the information or a result is not access. That limits the access limb only. A write to the device still needs its own assessment. A server-side calculation on data you already hold lawfully may involve no new device access.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 on the technical scope of Art. 5(3) ePrivacy Directive, version 2.0, adopted 7 October 2024:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraph 6 and paragraphs 35 to 39 for technology-neutral storage and independent operations (F-DEVICE-06)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraphs 35 to 36, 44 and 52 to 53 for local use versus external access (F-DEVICE-M01)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraphs 4, 40 and 52 to 55 for cookieless analytics (F-DEVICE-10)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraphs 54 to 56 and footnotes 28 to 29 for IP-based tracking (F-DEVICE-11)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraph 55, last sentence, for an IP address of uncertain origin (F-DEVICE-M02)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"localStorage gets the same storage and access test. This is an inference from the guidelines, not a named exemption. Claim F-DEVICE-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Fingerprinting: Article 29 Working Party Opinion 9/2014 (WP224), adopted 25 November 2014, section 6 and sections 7.1 to 7.2. A tool that reads device properties to recognise a visitor is in scope, and WP224 rejects an exemption for fingerprinting used for first-party analytics. Claim F-DEVICE-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"In scope does not always mean consent","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The technical guidelines decide whether something is in scope. They leave the exemptions to a separate assessment of the facts, national law and authority guidance.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You must know the exact operation and the function the visitor requested.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Business usefulness alone does not establish either exemption.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paragraphs 4, 6 and 40. Claim F-DEVICE-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Analytics is not strictly necessary by default","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"First-party analytics are not strictly necessary just because the operator values them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"This applies to page statistics, funnel events, visit counters and performance metrics collected for the owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"No analytics exemption was found in the EU or Croatian sources checked. The 2012 opinion suggested a future analytics exemption. That suggestion is not an enacted exemption. Do not copy another country's audience-measurement exemption into Croatia.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Article 29 Working Party Opinion 04/2012 on cookie consent exemption (WP194), adopted 7 June 2012, sections 4.2 to 4.3, pages 9 to 11. Claim F-DEVICE-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"No general Croatian analytics exemption was found. Article 43(4) has only its two exceptions. A cookieless or first-party label does not prove that device access is absent. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03 (bounded research conclusion).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"What AZOP says (Croatia)","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"AZOP is the Croatian data protection authority. Its current page is \"Obrada osobnih podataka putem kolačića i usklađivanje s Općom uredbom o zaštiti podataka\", published 14.8.2026, at azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Optional cookies stay off until consent.","t":"Non-essential analytics and marketing cookies must stay inactive until valid consent. Preselected choices, continued browsing, silence and inactivity are not consent. Locator: paragraphs beginning \"Ako se, međutim, koriste analitički\" and \"Nužni kolačići\". Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Necessary-only sites.","t":"A site that uses only technically necessary cookies does not need a banner asking visitors to accept. It still has to explain its cookie use. Locator: paragraph beginning \"Ako internetska stranica koristi isključivo tehnički nužne kolačiće\". This does not excuse unexamined pixels or other tracking. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Inventory and policy match.","t":"Make a technical inventory of installed cookies and tracking tools. The policy must match actual behaviour. A policy's claim about a tool is not proof that the tool is installed. The owner stays responsible when a designer built the site. Locator: paragraphs beginning \"Ističemo da činjenica\", \"Stoga je prije svega potrebno\" and \"Sama tvrdnja\", plus numbered recommendations 1 to 4. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Separate purposes, separate choices.","t":"Separate processing purposes get separate consent choices. Before you switch on anything that needs consent, explain who you are, the purposes, the data, the recipients, the storage period and how to withdraw. Sources: EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent, paragraphs 43 to 45 and 64 to 65, the AZOP 2026 page, and GDPR Articles 7(3) and 13(1) to (2). Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Consent records.","t":"You must be able to show valid consent. Keep proportionate records of when and how consent was given and what was shown. Do not collect extra identifying data only to make the record look stronger. Sources: GDPR Article 7(1), EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 paragraphs 104 to 108. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Banner states: reject, close and withdraw","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Equal first-layer choice.","t":"Visitors must be able to accept or reject non-essential cookies equally easily on the first layer of the banner. Locator: AZOP 14.8.2026, paragraph beginning \"Banner koji sadrži samo gumb\". Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Equal design.","t":"Accept and Reject should be displayed and designed equally. Avoid design that steers people to Accept. The sources set no exact size or colour. Locator: paragraph beginning \"Sukladno AZOP-ovoj Preporuci\". Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Closing the banner.","t":"AZOP's recommendation updated 6 August 2024 says a close control should let the visitor continue without tracking. Closing is not consent. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Later withdrawal.","t":"AZOP recommends a cookie-settings link in every page footer. Withdrawal must be as easy as giving consent (GDPR Article 7(3)). Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-05.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Withdrawal must work.","t":"After withdrawal, future optional reads, writes and tracking requests must stop. Test it. Do not only hide the banner. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09 (inference from AZOP recommendations 2 and 5 and EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 paragraph 117).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"No penalty for Reject.","t":"Rejecting cookies must not block the site's basic content and functions. Locator: AZOP 14.8.2026, paragraph beginning \"Nužni kolačići\", second sentence, and EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 paragraph 114. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-10.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Pixels, including email pixels","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Tracking pixels and tracked links, in web pages and in email, are storage and access mechanisms. Temporary caching and instructions to return identifiers can bring them into scope.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"An ordinary image request with no tracking is not automatically a tracking pixel.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, section 3.1, paragraphs 46 to 51. Claim F-DEVICE-08. Email open and click tracking in your mail provider belongs here too.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"GDPR still applies separately","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A device-access exemption does not settle the GDPR question. Where GDPR applies and the tool processes personal data, that processing needs an Article 6 basis and must meet the other GDPR rules. The EDPB says service-improvement metrics are generally not necessary to perform an online contract.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 2, 4(1), 5, 6 and 95. Claim F-DEVICE-M03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 4(1), 5(1)(c) and 6(1), with EDPB Guidelines 2/2019 paragraphs 48 to 49. Claim F-GDPR-BASIS-08.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do not rely on legitimate interest to replace consent where Article 43(4) requires consent. Withdrawn device-access consent cannot be swapped for legitimate interest (N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-08, exclusions).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Notice at collection and recipients","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Timing.","t":"When you collect data directly, for example through a form, give the Article 13 information at the time you obtain it. GDPR Article 13(1) to (3). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Recipients and transfers.","t":"Name the recipients or meaningful categories of recipients, and say whether data goes outside the EU and on what basis. GDPR Article 13(1)(e) to (f). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-03. Naming each vendor is clearer, but categories meet the minimum.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Layering.","t":"Use clear, concise language. Put the key facts at the point of collection and link to the full notice. GDPR Article 12(1), WP29 Guidelines on transparency (WP260 rev.01) paragraphs 35 to 36, endorsed by the EDPB. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Form relays and other processors","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A form relay, analytics vendor or email sender that handles visitor data on your behalf is usually your processor. Processing by a processor needs a written contract or other binding legal act with the Article 28(3) terms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Roles are decided per activity, by who decides purposes and means. A vendor that also uses the data for its own purposes may not be a pure processor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8) and 28(10) (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01). GDPR Article 28(3) opening sentence and 28(9) (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04). Review each service: DPA, security annex, sub-processor list, transfer terms and exit (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Third-party fonts and icon CDNs","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement, inference.","t":"A font or icon loaded from another provider's CDN sends the visitor's IP address and request headers to that provider. That is a disclosure of personal data under GDPR, and it may be a transfer if the provider sits outside the EEA. Whether the request is also in scope of Article 5(3) is unsettled. It depends on whether the IP address comes from the device and whether the resource is used for tracking (F-DEVICE-11, F-DEVICE-M02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"No claim record covers fonts directly. This position is built from F-DEVICE-11, F-DEVICE-M02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01 (EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paragraphs 9 to 13, the three transfer criteria) and F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20 (map each flow).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Smallest fix.","t":"Self-host the font and icon files. That ends the request to the outside provider, so neither question arises for that provider and there is no font recipient to name in the notice.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"The cheapest path on every site is to remove what you do not read. Anything you keep needs its own assessment, not a cookie check.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"List every tool on each page.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: write down every script, font, icon, pixel, iframe, counter and form destination. Note who it sends to and why you have it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: compare your list with the browser's network panel on a clean, private window.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: every third-party request on each page from the Playwright network log, under \"Third parties\". It cannot see server-side hashing, vendor account settings or your plan tier.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Remove dead tags.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: delete any analytics tag whose script returns 404 or points at a project you no longer run. The vendor records nothing, but the browser still sends a request with the visitor's IP address, referrer and user agent on every page load.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: reload and confirm the request is gone from the network log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: the failed request and its host. It cannot see whether the host logs that request. A 404 says nothing about who controls the host name.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Remove GA4 if you do not read it.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: delete the tag. If you keep it, load it only after an affirmative Accept.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: on first load with no choice, no request goes to the Google tag host, and no _ga or _ga_<container-id> cookie appears.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Consent order\", whether an analytics request fires before any choice, and the cookies in the first-load context. Google documents _ga and _ga_<container-id> with a two-year default expiry. It also says its libraries \"do not require you to set cookies\", so the result depends on configuration. Only a clean-browser test shows what happens. Some Consent Mode setups still send requests before a choice. Judge by the network log, not by the setting name.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Remove the visitor counter.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: a visible visit total is not a service the visitor asked for. Drop the counter, or at least the cookie that marks returning visitors. Moving the count to the server is not an automatic way out. A wholly server-side calculation on data you already hold lawfully may involve no new device access, but the collection and later processing still need assessment (F-DEVICE-10, exclusions). A counter that tells visitors apart by IP address is IP-based tracking and gets the same test (F-DEVICE-11, F-DEVICE-M02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no counter cookie after first load, and no counter request from the browser.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: the cookie in the first-load context and the counter request. It cannot see what the counter endpoint stores, such as IP addresses.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Self-host fonts and icons.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: download the font and icon files and serve them from your own domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no request to a font or icon CDN in the network log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: font and image requests to third-party hosts. Images inside hidden sections are often fetched anyway, so check those too.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Decide on each cookieless analytics tool and on performance metrics.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: if you do not read the numbers, remove the script. If you keep it, do the four-part assessment in step 8.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: re-run the check and confirm the script's host is gone, or that its four-part assessment is written down.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: the script's requests and their timing, and any storage it writes. It cannot see server-side hashing or salts, how long the vendor keeps sessions, or whether a script is \"cookieless\" by design. Some hosted analytics only record custom events on paid plans. The browser still sends them on any plan, so plan tier does not change the device question.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Common patterns to assess:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"A host's built-in web analytics that identifies visitors by a hash of the incoming request.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"A hosting platform's performance tool that reads the user agent and connection details and posts web vitals.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"A cookieless vendor whose script reads screen size and language and sends them with the URL and referrer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Funnel events. Keep them free of email addresses and form values, even if you keep the tool.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Put a short notice next to every form, and review each form relay.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: add one or two lines next to the submit button (who you are, what the data is for, a link to the full notice). Check that each form relay or signup endpoint has usable processor terms for your account. See UC-03 for workshop signups and UC-12 for quizzes and waitlists.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the notice text is visible before submit. You have the DPA or terms you accepted, with the version.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Forms\", where each form posts, whether notice text sits next to it, and whether any marketing consent is a separate unticked box. It never submits a form. It cannot see whether you accepted a DPA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Assess every tool you keep, in four parts.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: for each retained tool, answer:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"(a) Does it store or read anything on the device, including memory?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"(b) What data or identifiers leave the device, and to whom?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"(c) For what purpose?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"(d) Is it strictly necessary for a service the visitor expressly asked for?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"If (a) is yes and (d) is no, it is likely to need prior consent. If you want to keep it without consent, that is a specialist question.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: write the four answers down per tool, with evidence from the network log and the code.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: facts for (a) and (b) from storage and network logs, labelled \"observed\". Parts (c) and (d) are labelled \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"If anything optional stays, add a banner and test all five states.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: put equal Accept and Reject on the first layer. Close means no tracking. Add a \"Cookie settings\" link in the footer of every page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: in separate clean sessions, check first load with no choice, after Reject, after Accept, after closing, and after withdrawal followed by reload. Optional requests and storage appear only after Accept and stop after withdrawal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: storage in three fresh contexts (first load, after Reject, after Accept), then a withdrawal and reload, plus request timing. It cannot judge button design. It flags it as \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Make the notice match the live site.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: describe each tool you kept, its purpose, the recipient or category, the transfer route and the retention period. Replace \"we set no cookies\" with an accurate description. That sentence can be true and still incomplete, because the rule is wider than cookies. Remove lines about tools you deleted.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: repeat the outside check after each change and compare the inventory with the notice line by line.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: a privacy link on each page under \"Pages\", and the third-party inventory to compare. It cannot read your notice for accuracy. That comparison is yours.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Check email tracking.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: in your sending provider, check whether open and click tracking is on. Many providers ship it off by default. If it is on for marketing mail, treat the pixel like a web tracker (F-DEVICE-08).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: send yourself a test marketing email and confirm it has no 1x1 image and no rewritten links.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. Mail settings are outside the site. Record this as an answer.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"No cookies, so no banner.\"","t":"The rule covers reading from the device and storing in localStorage or memory too. A storage-only test cannot clear a script (F-DEVICE-06, F-DEVICE-10).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Trusting the vendor's label.","t":"\"Privacy-friendly\", \"cookieless\" and \"no banner needed\" are vendor claims. They are not evidence about every operation (F-DEVICE-10, exclusions).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating \"first-party\" as \"necessary\".","t":"Your own analytics on your own domain is still analytics (F-DEVICE-13).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Accept-only or uneven banners.","t":"A big Accept and a small \"settings\" link does not meet AZOP's equal-choice guidance (N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Loading the tag first and asking second.","t":"Optional tools must stay off until consent (N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A \"rejected\" flag that changes nothing.","t":"If the tag still fires after Reject or withdrawal, the processing has not stopped (N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A notice copied from a template or another site.","t":"It must describe this site's actual tools (N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08). A notice that says fonts are self-hosted while a page loads them from a CDN is a mismatch.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Dead tags left in place.","t":"They collect nothing for you but still send visitor requests to a third-party host.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Email in localStorage.","t":"Copying a typed email into the browser's storage is a write to the device. Ask whether the requested service needs it. Usually the server copy is enough (F-DEVICE-07).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"An \"I have read the privacy policy\" checkbox.","t":"Reading a notice is not consent. Give the notice as text, and keep any consent box for one specific optional purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Assuming plan tier or region settings settle where data lives.","t":"A sending region or a data region setting does not prove where the provider stores account data, logs and metadata. Check the provider's own statement and your accepted terms (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15).","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work site by site. Never submit a form, never log in and never claim a site is compliant.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Run the outside check (see the README) on each domain the owner names.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For every third-party host in the report, ask the owner: remove or keep? Record the answer against Q-028 and Q-031.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove dead tags (scripts that return 404). Verify: re-run the check, the host is gone from the third-party list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove analytics tags the owner does not read. Verify: no analytics request in the first-load context, and no new cookie or storage key.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Self-host fonts and icons. Verify: no request to a font or icon CDN.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove any client-side visitor cookie used only for counting. Verify: the cookie is absent in all three contexts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Strip email addresses and form values from analytics events. Verify: inspect event payloads in the network log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Stop copying typed emails into localStorage unless the owner records why the requested service needs it. Verify: storage in the after-submit state shows no email.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each kept tool, fill the four-part assessment (access or storage, data sent, purpose, necessity). Answer Q-027, Q-029 and Q-031 with source: agent_from_owner_files and cite the code path.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] If any optional tool stays, gate it behind an affirmative Accept. Load nothing optional before a choice. Add equal Accept and Reject on the first layer and a footer \"Cookie settings\" link on every page. Verify: re-run the check and confirm all three contexts plus withdraw-and-reload (Q-178, Q-182, Q-184, Q-189).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a short notice beside each form with a link to the full notice. Verify: the \"Forms\" check shows notice text next to each form.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Update the privacy notice from the final inventory, one line per kept tool (purpose, recipient or category, transfer, retention). Remove lines for deleted tools. Ask the owner to confirm every line (Q-075, Q-181).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Leave anything marked \"needs a specialist\" for the owner. Do not decide it.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If I keep a cookieless analytics tool or performance metrics without consent, is each one in scope of ZEK Article 43(4) for my exact setup, and does either exception fit?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does Croatian law apply to my site and to each visitor's device? Does that change if I operate from outside Croatia, or if my visitors are mostly outside Croatia (Q-177, Q-183)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Is loading a font or icon from a third-party CDN in scope of Article 43(4) for my setup, or only a GDPR disclosure and transfer question?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For each analytics vendor and form relay, is it my processor or a separate controller? Are the terms I accepted enough under GDPR Article 28(3)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For a vendor outside the EEA, which transfer route applies, and is the exact entity covered (Q-106 to Q-108)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which consent records should I keep, and for how long?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant:","t":"nothing in this module, unless a paid analytics plan or a paid consent tool raises a VAT or invoicing question. See UC-11.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Version or date","u":""},{"t":"Claim ids","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy)","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2002/58"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Article 5(3), both sentences","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 19 December 2009, as amended by 2009/136/EC","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-02","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK, NN 76/2022","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 43(4), first and second sentences, Article 187","u":""},{"t":"In force 12 July 2022","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti, NN 14/2024","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 115(1), third indent, Article 116","u":""},{"t":"In force 15 February 2024","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK amendment, NN 45/2026","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Articles 1 to 38, especially 10 to 11 and 38","u":""},{"t":"In force 7 May 2026","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04","u":""}],[{"t":"HAKOM law directory","u":"https://www.hakom.hr/hr/zakoni-2038/2038"},{"t":"HAKOM","u":""},{"t":"ZEK entries NN 76/22, 14/24 and 45/26","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP cookie guidance","u":"https://azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs named in each rule above","u":""},{"t":"Published 14.8.2026","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-04, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-05, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-10","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP cookie recommendation","u":"https://azop.hr/obrada-osobnih-podataka-kolacici/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"First-layer choice, close control, footer link, equal design","u":""},{"t":"Updated 6 August 2024, background to the 2026 page","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-04, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-05","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, technical scope of Art. 5(3)","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2024-10/edpb_guidelines_202302_technical_scope_art_53_eprivacydirective_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 4, 6, 35 to 40, 44, 46 to 56, footnotes 28 to 29","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, adopted 7 October 2024","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-05, F-DEVICE-06, F-DEVICE-07, F-DEVICE-08, F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-11, F-DEVICE-14, F-DEVICE-M01, F-DEVICE-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03","u":""}],[{"t":"Planet49, C-673/17","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62017CJ0673"},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 68 to 71, operative part point 2","u":""},{"t":"Judgment 1 October 2019","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-03","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Opinion 04/2012 (WP194)","u":"https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/documentation/opinion-recommendation/files/2012/wp194_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party","u":""},{"t":"Sections 4.2 to 4.3, pages 9 to 11","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 7 June 2012","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-13","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Opinion 9/2014 (WP224)","u":"https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/documentation/opinion-recommendation/files/2014/wp224_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party","u":""},{"t":"Section 6, sections 7.1 to 7.2","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 25 November 2014","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-09","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_202005_consent_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 43 to 45, 64 to 65, 104 to 108, 114, 117 to 120","u":""},{"t":"Version 1.1, adopted 4 May 2020","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-08, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-10","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Cookie Banner Taskforce report","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-01/edpb_20230118_report_cookie_banner_taskforce_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Section 9, paragraphs 31 to 35","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 17 January 2023","u":""},{"t":"Background to N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-05","u":""}],[{"t":"GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 4(7) to (8), 6, 7, 12(1), 13(1) to (3), 13(1)(e) to (f), 28(3), 28(9)","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-M03, F-GDPR-BASIS-08, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2019 on Article 6(1)(b) in online services","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines-art_6-1-b-adopted_after_public_consultation_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 48 to 49, printed p. 14","u":""},{"t":"Version adopted after public consultation","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-BASIS-08","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Guidelines on transparency, WP260 rev.01","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-09/wp260rev01_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 35 to 36, printed p. 19","u":""},{"t":"Endorsed by the EDPB","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-09","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Endorsement 1/2018","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/sites/default/files/files/news/endorsement_of_wp29_documents_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Item 2","u":""},{"t":"25 May 2018","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-09","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021 on Article 3 and Chapter V","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 9 to 13","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, 14 February 2023","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20","u":""}],[{"t":"Google Analytics Help, answer 11397207","u":"https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11397207"},{"t":"Google (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Cookie table, opening paragraph","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor statement, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel Web Analytics privacy page","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"\"Visitor identification and data storage\"","u":""},{"t":"Last updated 2026-06-26","u":""},{"t":"Vendor statement, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel Speed Insights privacy page","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/privacy-policy"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"\"Data collected\"","u":""},{"t":"Last updated 2026-03-18","u":""},{"t":"Vendor statement, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel custom events","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/custom-events"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Plan banner","u":""},{"t":"Last updated 2026-06-26","u":""},{"t":"Vendor statement, not law","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"Gaps.","t":"No claim record covers third-party fonts or icon CDNs directly, so that section is an inference. No live site, banner or vendor setting was tested for this module. The territorial reach of Article 43(4) for operators outside Croatia is not settled here. Vendor statements describe products, not your configuration.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-07","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Building and selling an AI assistant or RAG product","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small software business that builds an assistant on a third-party model, often with retrieval over documents, and sells it under its own name to professionals such as lawyers, accountants or consultants.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-001, Q-002, Q-004, Q-005, Q-006, Q-007, Q-084, Q-086, Q-131, Q-134]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-AI-01, F-AI-02, F-AI-03, F-AI-04, F-AI-05, F-AI-06, F-AI-07, F-AI-08, F-AI-10, F-AI-11, F-AI-12, F-AI-13, F-AI-14, F-AI-15, F-AI-16, F-AI-17, F-AI-18, F-AI-19, F-GDPR-SCOPE-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-04, F-GDPR-BASIS-M02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-06, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-08, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-11, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-13, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-13, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20, F-SECTOR-06, F-SECTOR-07, F-SECTOR-08, F-SECTOR-09, F-SECTOR-10, F-SECTOR-12, F-SECTOR-13, F-SECTOR-15, F-SECTOR-16, F-ECOMMERCE-01, F-ECOMMERCE-02, F-ECOMMERCE-07, F-CRA-02, N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-02, N-HR-AUTH-06, N-HR-AUTH-07, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"ai-product":{"title":"Building and selling an AI assistant or RAG product","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each fact links to a question in questions.json. \"Unknown\" is a valid answer. It keeps the related checks visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What the system is and which models it uses.","t":"Write down each model, its vendor and what your code adds on top: prompts, retrieval, tools, memory. (Q-001)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whose name it is supplied under.","t":"Your brand on the product points to you as provider. A customer who rebrands it may change the picture. (Q-002)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Where you, your customers and their users are, and where the output is used.","t":"EU use of the output can bring you into scope even from outside the EU. (Q-003)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether it talks to people, generates content or analyses biometrics.","t":"Chat and generated text trigger different Article 50 duties. (Q-004)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"When each version was first placed on the market or put into service.","t":"Before or after 2 August 2026 decides whether the December 2026 marking transition helps you. (Q-005)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the intended use is listed in Annex III.","t":"Recruitment, credit scoring, education admissions and the administration of justice are the listed areas closest to a professional assistant. (Q-006)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether anything it writes is published to inform the public, and who reviews it.","t":"A public newsletter, digest or blog summary is the typical case. (Q-007)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether you use customer content for your own purposes.","t":"Training, evaluation, analytics or retrieval across customers changes your GDPR role. (Q-084)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether processor terms bind your exact account and plan with each vendor.","t":"A public DPA page is not proof that your account accepted it. (Q-086)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether prompts or uploads can hold special-category or criminal-offence data.","t":"Legal, HR and health files often do. (Q-131)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the product gives legal advice or a protected professional service.","t":"Also ask whether it diagnoses or treats (Q-132) or personalises investment advice (Q-133). (Q-134)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who receives data and from which countries.","t":"Model vendors, vector databases, hosting, logging and support tools all count. (Q-075, Q-076)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether any output is a solely automated decision with legal or similarly significant effects.","t":"(Q-079)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether scale or sensitivity calls for a DPIA.","t":"(Q-136)","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"AI Act scope: small size is not an exemption","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The AI Act can cover you as a provider when you place a system on the EU market or put it into service, wherever you are based. EU-based deployers are covered. Providers and deployers outside the EU are covered where their AI output is used in the EU.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The software meets the AI-system definition. There is an EU link through market placement, EU establishment or EU use of output.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"No AI system or relevant model activity. No EU territorial link. Incidental overseas use of output is an open question on the facts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 2(1)(a) to (c) and Article 3(1). Claim F-AI-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Provider or deployer","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A provider develops or commissions an AI system and supplies it under its own name, even for free. A deployer uses a system under its authority for professional purposes. Wrapping a third-party model in your own branded service can make you the provider of that system. It does not make you the provider of the underlying general-purpose model.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Look at who builds or commissions the system, whose brand is on it, the contract chain and who controls its professional use.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Purely personal, non-professional use falls outside the deployer definition. API wrappers and embedded widgets need a system-boundary assessment.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 3(3), (4) and (68). Claim F-AI-02 (inference from those definitions). The 2 August 2027 transition for general-purpose models placed on the market before 2 August 2025 is in Article 111(3). It does not apply to every downstream chatbot. Claim F-AI-12.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Research, testing, \"demo\" and open-source labels","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Article 2 excludes systems developed and used only for scientific research, and research, testing and development before market placement. Real-world testing is not covered by that pre-market exclusion. Free and open-source systems are not excluded if they are high-risk or fall under Article 5 or Article 50.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The exclusion depends on what you actually do, not on the label. A product that real customers can use is not shown to be pre-market because its page says \"demo\" or \"beta\" (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None beyond the listed exclusions. They also do not switch off GDPR or other EU law.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 2(6), (8), (10) and (12). Claim F-AI-17.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Prohibited practices: screen before anything else","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Article 5 prohibits, among others, manipulative or deceptive techniques and exploitation of vulnerabilities that meet the significant-harm test, specified social scoring, criminal-risk prediction based only on profiling, untargeted facial-image scraping, emotion inference at work or in education (with medical and safety exceptions), and specified biometric categorisation. From 2 December 2026, Article 5(1)(ba) and (bb) add prohibitions on non-consensual intimate imagery of identifiable people and on child sexual abuse material, where that is the intended purpose or a reasonably foreseeable outcome without adequate safeguards, or where a deployer uses the system for that purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Each prohibition has its own facts and test. A text assistant for professionals is unlikely to meet them on an ordinary scope, but write the screen down.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Narrow law-enforcement exceptions. Disclosure never makes a prohibited practice lawful.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 5(1)(a) to (h) and (2) to (7), applying from 2 February 2025. Claim F-AI-15. Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Article 1(7), inserting Article 5(1)(ba) to (bb) and (1a) to (1b). Claim F-AI-16.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"AI literacy: simplified, not abolished","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"From 27 July 2026, amended Article 4 requires providers and deployers to take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and of people acting for them. The measures should reflect their knowledge, experience, training, use context and the people affected. You need not guarantee a specific literacy level for each person.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You provide or deploy an AI system. This covers you and anyone who operates the product for you, such as a contractor or support helper.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"No blanket microenterprise exemption. The original, stricter wording (\"to their best extent, a sufficient level\") applied from 2 February 2025 to 26 July 2026 and is history now.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 4(1) to (3). Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Article 1(5) and Article 4. Claims F-AI-04 and F-AI-03. A short written note on what the system does, what it must not see and how outputs are checked is useful evidence. It is not a safe harbour (inference).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Chat disclosure: Article 50(1) and 50(5)","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Since 2 August 2026, providers must design systems that interact directly with people so those people know they are dealing with AI. The information must be clear, distinguishable and accessible, at the latest at the first interaction or exposure.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You are the provider and the system interacts directly with natural persons. This likely includes a widget your customers embed on their own client-facing sites, because the duty sits in your design (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Where AI interaction is obvious to a reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect person in that context. A narrow law-enforcement exception.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 50(1) and (5), Article 113 second paragraph. Commission AI Act implementation timeline, 2 August 2026 milestone. Claim F-AI-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Machine-readable marking: Article 50(2) and the December 2026 transition","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Providers of systems that generate synthetic audio, images, video or text must mark outputs in a machine-readable format and make them detectable as artificially generated, within the technical-feasibility limits of the provision. This normally applies from 2 August 2026.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You provide the generating system. Text answers and generated documents are in scope unless an exception fits.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Standard assistive editing, and processing that does not substantially alter the input or its meaning, to the extent the provision states. Under new Article 111(4), a system placed on the market before 2 August 2026 has until 2 December 2026 to comply with Article 50(2). That transition covers Article 50(2) only. It gives no extra time for chat disclosure under Article 50(1) or deployer disclosure under Article 50(4). A system first placed on the market on or after 2 August 2026 gets no transition.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 50(2), Article 111(4) and Article 113. Commission AI Act implementation timeline, 2 December 2026 milestone. Claims F-AI-06 and F-AI-07. The Commission's regulatory framework page dates its transparency guidelines 20 July 2026 and gives a 9 July 2026 Commission opinion on the labelling code. Neither was read in full for this module (gap).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Published text and deepfakes: Article 50(4)","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Since 2 August 2026, deployers must disclose AI-generated or manipulated deepfake images, audio and video. AI-generated text published to inform the public on matters of public interest must also be disclosed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You or your customer publish the output yourselves. A public newsletter, digest or blog summary on a matter of public interest is the case to test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The text duty does not apply where the text underwent human review or editorial control and a person or entity holds editorial responsibility. Evidently artistic, fictional or satirical works get a tailored disclosure, not a full exemption. The text exception does not remove the deepfake duty. A private reply a professional reviews and sends as themselves is not shown to be public-interest publication (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 3(60), Article 50(4) to (5) and Article 113. Claim F-AI-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"High-risk: Annex III and the new dates","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Under the amended dates, Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 (except Article 6(5)) apply from 2 December 2027 to Annex III high-risk systems and from 2 August 2028 to Annex I product-linked systems. Using AI does not by itself make a system high-risk. Recruitment and applicant filtering, education admission decisions and creditworthiness assessment of natural persons are listed Annex III examples.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Your intended purpose, or the purpose a customer gives it, falls in an Annex III area. Article 25 can shift the provider role to someone who rebrands, substantially modifies or changes the intended purpose of a high-risk system.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 6(3) can exclude an Annex III system that poses no significant risk of harm and meets one of its narrow-task, completed-human-work, pattern-review or preparatory-task conditions. Profiling of natural persons blocks that exclusion. Document the assessment.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Articles 6, 25 and 113(c), Annex III points 3(a), 4(a) and 5(b). Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Article 1, replacing Article 113(c). Claims F-AI-11 and F-AI-18. Annex III also has an entry for the administration of justice, point 8(a), covering systems intended to be used by or on behalf of a judicial authority to research and interpret facts and law and apply the law to facts, or used in a similar way in alternative dispute resolution. This module has no claim record for point 8. Read the consolidated text and ask counsel if courts or dispute-resolution bodies are among your users.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Which changes are law and which are proposals","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 (Digital Omnibus on AI) was adopted on 8 July 2026, published on 24 July 2026 and entered into force on 27 July 2026. Treat its literacy and timing changes as law. Under amended Article 113, Articles 102 to 110 apply from 27 July 2026. Chapters I and II applied from 2 February 2025. The general application date is 2 August 2026.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Check each provision's own date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The general Digital Omnibus, COM(2025) 837 (procedure 2025/0360/COD), and the medical-device proposal COM(2025) 1023 (procedure 2025/0404/COD) were still ongoing in the checked record. They change nothing yet.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, title, Official Journal date, Articles 1 and 4. AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 113(a) to (d). Procedure records 2025/0360/COD and 2025/0404/COD. Claims F-AI-13, F-AI-10 and F-AI-14.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Bias testing is not a sensitive-data licence","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"New Article 4a allows special-category data only where strictly necessary for the specified bias detection and correction, with technical reuse limits, pseudonymisation, documented access, deletion and records of why other data would not do.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Other, synthetic or anonymised data must be insufficient. GDPR still applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"It is not a general training-data exemption. Paragraph 2 creates no duty to test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 4a(1) and (2), Article 2(7). Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Article 1(6). Claim F-AI-19.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"GDPR roles: processor for customer documents, controller for your own purposes","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A controller decides the purposes and means of processing. A processor processes on the controller's behalf. Assess each activity separately. When a professional uploads client files and asks your assistant about them, they usually decide the purpose, and you usually act as their processor. For your own account, billing, support and marketing data you are a controller.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The activity involves personal data within GDPR Articles 2 and 3. Look at who decides purpose, data types, recipients and retention.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Labels in contracts do not decide roles. If you use customer content for your own purposes, such as training, product improvement, evaluation or retrieval across customers, you act as a controller for that use. A vendor's own-use terms matter in the same way for your model vendor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8) and 28(10). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part I, paragraphs 12 to 13 and 39 to 41. Claims F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01 and F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02. Scope is assessed per activity: GDPR Articles 2 and 3, claim F-GDPR-SCOPE-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Article 28 terms in both directions","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"You need a binding written contract (or other qualifying legal act) with each customer for whom you are a processor, and you need one with each processor you use, such as the model vendor, vector database, hosting and logging tools. It must set out the subject, duration, nature and purpose of processing, data types, people affected, documented instructions (including transfers), confidentiality, Article 32 security, sub-processor rules, assistance, audits, breach notice and return or deletion at the end.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Sub-processors need the controller's prior specific or general written authorisation. With general authorisation you must give notice of intended changes and a chance to object, and you must flag changes actively. A silently updated web list does not meet the EDPB reading. Your processor must tell you of a breach without undue delay. Your own duty to keep checking a vendor's guarantees does not end at signature.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A privacy notice is not the contract. Completed Modules 2 or 3 of the 2021 transfer SCCs can supply Article 28 terms for covered processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Article 28(1) to (4), 28(3)(a) to (h), 28(9) and Article 33(1) to (2). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part II, paragraphs 99, 112 to 114, 128 and 143 to 145. EDPB Opinion 22/2024, paragraphs 22 to 29. Claims F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, -05, -07, -09, -11, -12, -15, -M01 and -M02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Vendor terms to read, not law.","t":"Model vendors often split their terms. A commercial agreement may say the vendor will not train on customer content and may point to a separate DPA. The same vendor's consumer terms may be written for individuals and say nothing about a DPA. Some API terms allow only paid tiers when you serve users in the European Economic Area. These are examples of vendor statements, not law, and they change. Read the current terms for your own account and plan. A consumer plan with a training opt-out is not Article 28 terms (inference).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Lawful basis and new purposes","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Each purpose needs its own Article 6 basis, set before processing. For your own customers, running the paid service can rest on contract necessity for the data objectively needed. If your customer is a firm, its staff are not automatically the contracting party for that basis. Legitimate interests need a recorded test of interest, necessity and balance.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Reusing data for a new purpose, such as training on customer prompts or building an evaluation set from real conversations, needs a compatibility assessment unless it rests on consent or a qualifying law. Articles 13(3) and 14(4) require information before the new purpose starts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A new notice or a newly named basis does not by itself make a purpose compatible. As a processor you do not choose a basis for customer documents. The customer, as controller, does.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 5(1)(b), 6(1), 6(1)(b), 6(1)(f), 6(4)(a) to (e), 13(3) and 14(4). Claims F-GDPR-BASIS-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-04 and F-GDPR-BASIS-M02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Sensitive and criminal data in prompts and files","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Special categories are data revealing racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs or trade-union membership, plus genetic data, biometrics used for unique identification, health data and data on sex life or sexual orientation. Processing them is prohibited unless an Article 9(2) condition applies, on top of an Article 6 basis. Data on criminal convictions and offences may be processed only under official authority or where EU or national law authorises it with safeguards.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Free text, uploaded files, inferences and model outputs can all reveal these categories. Legal, HR, insurance and medical files often do.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Explicit consent is one Article 9 route, but law may block it, and it does not replace the Article 10 authorisation test. National law may add conditions for genetic, biometric and health data. A keyword filter does not keep this data out (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 6, 9(1) to (4) and 10, recital 51. Claims F-SECTOR-06, F-SECTOR-07 and F-SECTOR-15. Documents in Croatia often carry the personal identification number (OIB). GDPR Article 87 lets Member States set conditions for national identification numbers. This module has no claim on the Croatian rule (gap).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Notices for your own corpus and your own customers","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Tell people who you are, why you process, on what basis, who receives the data, about third-country transfers and their safeguards, how long you keep data and what rights they have. If you build a retrieval corpus from sources that name people, such as published decisions or registers, you collect that data indirectly. Article 14 then requires the data categories and their source.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Direct collection: inform at collection. Indirect collection: within a reasonable time and no later than one month, or by the first communication or first disclosure if sooner. Inform before any new purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 14(5) has narrow exceptions, including impossible or disproportionate effort and regulated professional secrecy. The disproportionate-effort route still needs protective measures, including making the information public. It is not a small-business exemption. If you make no solely automated decisions with significant effects, establish that from the facts before you write it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1) to (4), 14(1) to (5), 22(1) and (4). Claims F-GDPR-NOTICE-02, -03, -06, -07 and -08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Rights requests must reach the index and the logs","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Recognise a rights request even if it does not name GDPR, log it and route it to the controller for that activity. Erase without undue delay when an Article 17(1) ground applies, subject to Article 17(3). As a processor you must help the customer answer requests.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Copies live in uploads, chunked text, embeddings, caches, conversation history, logs, evaluation sets and backups. Treat derived copies such as embeddings of personal data as copies you must be able to find and delete (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 17(3) lets you keep data actually needed for a listed exception, such as legal claims.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 12(1) to (2), 17(1) and (3), 28(3)(e). EDPB Guidelines 01/2022 on access, paragraphs 47 to 57. Claims F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01 and F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Transfers to model vendors outside the EEA","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A transfer happens when an exporter subject to GDPR makes personal data available to a separate entity in a third country. That includes remote access and support. Each such flow needs a Chapter V route.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"For a US vendor, the EU-US Data Privacy Framework covers only organisations actively listed on the DPF List, within the scope of their certification and named subsidiaries. Certifications renew yearly. DPF remained available within its scope on the checked date (inference): Decision 2023/1795 is in force, the appeal C-703/25 P is in progress, and the EDPB's 31 July 2026 letter asks for an assessment without suspending anything. Without DPF, use the right SCC module, complete the annexes and do the Clause 14 assessment. Do not use the 2021 SCCs automatically for an importer that is already subject to GDPR for the same processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"DPF does not replace Article 28 terms or other GDPR duties. A vendor's EU data-region setting does not prove where support, logs or sub-processors sit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paragraphs 9 to 13. Decision (EU) 2023/1795, Article 1 and Annex I, Section I.3. EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses (version 2.0, 15 January 2026), Questions 3, 3.1 and 3.3. Decision (EU) 2021/914, Article 1 and Annex Clauses 14 to 16. Claims F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, -04, -08, -09, -11, -13, -15 and -20.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Automated decisions, DPIA and DPO","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Article 22 protects people from decisions based only on automated processing with legal or similarly significant effects. A draft a professional reviews before use is unlikely to meet that test on an ordinary scope (inference). A DPIA is required where processing is likely to create high risk, including large-scale special-category processing and certain automated evaluations. A DPO is required where core activities involve large-scale regular and systematic monitoring or large-scale special-category or criminal data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Meaningful human involvement, the effect of the output, the scale and the data categories.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 22 exceptions need contract necessity, authorising law with safeguards or explicit consent. The contract and consent routes also need at least human intervention, a chance to give a view and a way to contest. Headcount alone does not trigger a DPO. Absence of a DPO trigger does not remove the DPIA test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 22(1) to (4), 35(1) to (4), 36(1) and 37(1). Claims F-SECTOR-16, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-13 and F-SECTOR-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Professional-sector triggers","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Personalised legal advice, representation, reserved drafting and use of a protected professional title call for a country-specific check of professional rules. Medical-purpose software can be a medical device. Personal recommendations on financial instruments can be investment advice that needs authorisation. A disclaimer does not settle whether the actual activity is reserved.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Look at what the product actually does and what your marketing says it does, for whom, in which country.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A general legal-information article or search over public law is not automatically a reserved service. General information or a booking function is not automatically a medical purpose. General education is not automatically a personal recommendation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"Directive 2000/31/EC, Articles 5(1)(e) to (f), 8(1), 8(4) and recital 33. Your Europe, regulated professions. Regulation (EU) 2017/745 (MDR), consolidated 19 July 2026, Articles 2(1) and 6, Annex VIII Rule 11. Directive 2014/65/EU (MiFID II), consolidated 6 June 2026, Articles 4(1)(4) and 5(1). Claims F-SECTOR-12, F-SECTOR-13, F-SECTOR-09 and F-SECTOR-10. National rules on who may give legal assistance in Croatia were not researched for this module (gap).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Provider information on your site, B2B included","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"An online service must keep your identity, establishment address, effective contact details including email, and any registration, supervisory, professional and VAT details directly and permanently accessible. This can apply to B2B services too.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You run an information society service, paid or funded by advertising.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The VAT and professional limbs are conditional. If you also sell to consumers, a chatbot can be an extra contact channel. It must not obstruct the contact methods consumer law requires.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"Directive 2000/31/EC, Article 5(1)(a) to (g). Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, Article 6(1). Commission Notice 2021/C 525/01, section 3.2.2.2. Claims F-ECOMMERCE-01, F-ECOMMERCE-02, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01 and F-ECOMMERCE-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Croatia: authority and breach route","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"AZOP (Agencija za zaštitu osobnih podataka) is the Croatian GDPR supervisory authority under Article 4 of the implementing act, Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018, in force 25 May 2018. AZOP's breach page is the reporting entry point, with the GDPR test of without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours of awareness, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk to people's rights and freedoms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"AZOP is the competent authority for your processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not assume AZOP is the only authority because a customer is in Croatia. Articles 55, 56 and 77 allocate competence and complaint routes. The Croatian authority for the AI Act was not identified in this research (gap).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"NN 42/2018, Articles 1, 4 and 57. AZOP breach page. GDPR Articles 33(1), 55, 56 and 77. Claims N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-02, N-HR-AUTH-06 and N-HR-AUTH-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Not usually the Cyber Resilience Act","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The Commission FAQ says standalone SaaS is not itself a product with digital elements.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"If you also ship a desktop app, mobile app, browser extension or on-premise package whose function depends on your backend, assess that product separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None recorded for the SaaS limb.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"Commission CRA implementation FAQ v1.4 (4 September 2026), section 1.2. Regulation (EU) 2024/2847, Article 3(1) to (2), recitals 11 to 12. Claim F-CRA-02.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Write a one-page system card.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: record each model and vendor, your brand, the first market date of each version, intended users, intended purpose and uses you forbid. Add a two-line screen against Article 5 and Annex III, including the administration-of-justice entry.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: Q-001, Q-002, Q-005 and Q-006 have answers with source: owner, and the card is dated.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. This is \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Add the AI disclosure at the first interaction.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: show a short, plain line such as \"You are chatting with an AI assistant\" in the chat itself, before or with the first reply. Do the same in every embeddable version your customers use. Do not rely on the terms of service.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: open the chat in a fresh private window and on a phone. The line is visible without scrolling, has enough contrast and is read by a screen reader.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Third parties\", the chat widget's script and iframe hosts on each public page, and under \"Device storage\", any conversation or user ID the widget stores. It never types into a chat, so it cannot see the disclosure. That stays \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Write the AI literacy note.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: one page for you and anyone who operates or supports the product. Cover what it does, what it must not see, known failure modes, how outputs are checked and who to call when it goes wrong. Offer a customer version for their staff.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the note is dated and names the version it describes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Check your provider information.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: put your legal name, address, email, registration and VAT details on a page linked from every site, the app and the chat window.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the page loads from the footer on every domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Pages\", whether a privacy notice link and an imprint or trader-information page exist on each site.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Confirm processor terms for each vendor account.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: for the model vendor, vector store, hosting, logging and email, save a dated copy of the terms your account accepted, the DPA, the sub-processor list, the data region, the retention of prompts and outputs, and whether content is used for training. Move off any consumer plan for business data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each vendor has a row with \"accepted on\" and a link to the saved copy. Unknowns are marked unknown (Q-086).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Vendors\", a register of the vendors it saw in the browser. Server-side model calls never appear in a browser log, so add those vendors to the vendor facts file yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Publish your own DPA and sub-processor list for customers.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: offer Article 28 terms that match what the product does, list your sub-processors with location and purpose, and email customers before you add or replace one.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test customer receives a change notice and has a way to object.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing beyond the \"Pages\" links. It cannot read a DPA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Map every copy of customer data and set retention for each.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: list uploads, chunks, embeddings, caches, conversation history, request and error logs, traces, evaluation sets, analytics events and backups. Give each a retention period and an owner. Strip document text and prompts from analytics and error reporting.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run synthetic documents through the system, force a failure, then inspect what each log, trace and error tool stored. Include a forced failure, because failed runs often keep content when successful runs do not.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: browser-side storage keys and third-party requests only. Server logs and vendor retention are \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Build deletion that reaches every copy.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: one delete path per customer and per document that removes the file, its chunks and embeddings, cached answers and history, and schedules backup expiry. Ask each vendor for deletion where it holds copies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: delete a synthetic customer, then query the index for its text and search the logs. Nothing returns.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Keep customers apart and keep their content out of training.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: scope every retrieval query by tenant at the database level, not only in the prompt. Turn off any use of customer content for training or evaluation unless the contract and notice say otherwise (Q-084).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: load two synthetic tenants with distinct marker phrases and confirm neither can retrieve the other's marker.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Treat retrieved text as data, not instructions.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: give the model only the tools it needs. Never hand it a general credential. An approval prompt in the interface is an application control, not a credential boundary (inference). If it can call tools, put a small broker in front that exposes only the allowed actions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run negative action tests through the broker (send, delete, export, cross-tenant read) and confirm each is refused. Then run adversarial documents that tell the model to do those things. Observed good behaviour alone does not prove the capability is absent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Add machine-readable marking to generated output.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: decide your Article 50(2) method for text answers and exported files, for example provenance metadata in API responses and document metadata in downloads. If your system was on the market before 2 August 2026, finish by 2 December 2026. If it launched later, the duty already applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: generate a sample answer and a sample export, and read the marker back with a script.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. It does not generate output.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"12","b":"Update your privacy notice from the final data map.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: name the model vendor or its category, transfers and their safeguards, retention per data set, and your rights route. If you build a corpus from sources that name people, add the Article 14 facts (data categories and source) or record why an exception applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: every row of the data map appears in the notice and every line of the notice matches a row.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Pages\", the privacy link, and under \"Forms\", whether notice text sits next to each upload, signup and contact form. It never submits a form.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"13","b":"Set editorial control for anything you publish.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: for a public newsletter, digest or summary, name a person who reviews each issue and holds editorial responsibility, and keep a review log. Otherwise label it as AI-generated (Q-007).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each published issue has a reviewer name and date in the log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. Whether a page is AI text is not visible to it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"14","b":"Run a sector perimeter check on your marketing and features.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: remove claims such as \"legal advice\", \"diagnosis\" or \"investment advice\" unless you hold the licence. Write down what the product does for the user and in which countries. Take the result to counsel.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the counsel answer is filed with the system card.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. This is \"needs a specialist\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"15","b":"Write and test a stop procedure.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: one page to disable the assistant, cancel queued and retrying jobs, and revoke model keys and data-source tokens.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run it while synthetic jobs are running, waiting and queued, then check the vendor console for calls after the stop time. Revoking a key does not delete what vendors already hold, so record their retention.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"We only call an API, so we are not a provider.\"","t":"Supplying a system under your own name can make you its provider (F-AI-02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"It is a demo.\"","t":"Real users on a live product are not shown to be pre-market testing, and real-world testing is not excluded (F-AI-17).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Article 50 starts in December.\"","t":"Only Article 50(2) marking has a transition, and only for systems on the market before 2 August 2026. Chat disclosure has applied since 2 August 2026 (F-AI-07, F-AI-05).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"High-risk moved to 2027, so nothing applies yet.\"","t":"Prohibitions, literacy and transparency already apply (F-AI-10, F-AI-15, F-AI-04, F-AI-05, F-AI-11).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"The model vendor's 2027 transition covers us.\"","t":"The Article 111(3) date is for general-purpose models, not your downstream system (F-AI-12).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating a proposal as law.","t":"The general Digital Omnibus and the medical-device proposal were still pending (F-AI-14).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Disclosure hidden in the terms.","t":"Article 50(5) asks for clear, distinguishable information by the first interaction (F-AI-05).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"A disclaimer makes it not legal advice.\"","t":"The actual activity decides (F-SECTOR-12).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A consumer plan with a training opt-out.","t":"That is not Article 28 terms (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, vendor terms above).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Product improvement\" on customer documents.","t":"Using them for your own purposes makes you a controller for that use (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-M02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Embeddings are not personal data.\"","t":"Treat them as copies that deletion must reach (F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Success logs off, so no content kept.","t":"Error logs, traces and retry queues often keep it. Test with a forced failure.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"DPF covers every US vendor.\"","t":"Only active certified entities within their scope (F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A silently updated sub-processor page.","t":"Customers need notice and a chance to object (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Bias testing lets us keep sensitive data.\"","t":"Only under the strict Article 4a conditions (F-AI-19).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A keyword filter as the sensitive-data control.","t":"It misses data phrased in other words and data in quoted threads (F-SECTOR-06, inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"The CRA covers our SaaS.\"","t":"Standalone SaaS is outside the product definition. A shipped app may not be (F-CRA-02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Revoking the key deleted the data.\"","t":"Vendor copies stay until their retention ends or you get them deleted.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work on synthetic data until the owner says real data may enter. Never log in to production, never submit a form on a live site and never claim the product is compliant.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Run the outside check (see the README) on each domain the owner names.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Draft the system card from the code: models, vendors, prompts, tools, retrieval sources. Answer Q-001 and Q-004 with source: agent_from_owner_files and cite file paths. Leave Q-002, Q-005 and Q-006 for the owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a first-interaction AI disclosure to every chat surface and embed. Verify: a Playwright test opens the chat in a fresh context and asserts the text is visible before the first reply and has an accessible name.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] List every server-side call to a model, embedding, vector or logging vendor (grep for SDK imports and base URLs). Add each to the vendor facts file. Verify: the \"Vendors\" section lists them after a re-run.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove prompts, document text and user identifiers from analytics events and error reports. Verify: a forced synthetic failure leaves no document text in the error tool, and the network log shows no prompt text in analytics payloads.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Enforce tenant scoping in the retrieval query itself. Verify: a test with two synthetic tenants fails if either can retrieve the other's marker phrase.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Implement delete-by-customer and delete-by-document across files, chunks, embeddings, caches and history. Verify: a test deletes a synthetic tenant and then finds no rows and no vector hits for its marker.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Put tool calls behind an allowlist broker. Verify: tests for each forbidden action (send, delete, export, cross-tenant read) assert a refusal, and adversarial-document tests produce no forbidden call.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add machine-readable provenance to generated answers and exports. Verify: a script reads the marker back from a sample answer and a sample file.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Gate any training or evaluation pipeline behind an explicit per-customer flag that defaults to off. Verify: a test asserts no customer content enters the pipeline when the flag is off (Q-084).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Update the privacy notice and sub-processor page from the final vendor list. Ask the owner to confirm every line (Q-075, Q-076).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Write the stop procedure as a script with dry-run mode. Verify: a dry run lists every key, job queue and token it would revoke.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Leave anything marked \"needs a specialist\" for the owner. Do not decide it.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Am I the provider, a deployer or both for each way the product is used? Does a customer who rebrands or embeds it change that under Article 25?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which version dates count as first placement on the market, given updates? Does Article 111(4) cover my system?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Is AI interaction obvious enough in my interface for the Article 50(1) exception, or do I need the line everywhere?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which marking method meets Article 50(2) for text and for exported documents?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If I publish a newsletter or digest, is it public-interest text under Article 50(4), and does my review process meet the editorial-control exception?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Could any customer's intended use make the system high-risk, including Annex III point 8 on the administration of justice? Should I record an Article 6(3) assessment?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For uploaded documents, am I a processor? Do my customers' own clients need to authorise my sub-processors (Q-084, Q-086)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do professional-secrecy and bar rules let a lawyer or accountant send client files to me and my vendors? Do I need confidentiality undertakings beyond Article 28?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How should special-category and criminal-offence data in uploads be handled, and by whom (Q-131)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which conditions apply to OIB and other national identification numbers under GDPR Article 87 and the Croatian implementing act?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which transfer route applies to each vendor, and is the exact entity covered (Q-106 to Q-108)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do I need a DPIA, and should I keep an Article 30 record of processing (Q-136)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does any feature amount to reserved legal assistance under Croatian law, or a regulated service in another country where I sell (Q-134, Q-135)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which Croatian authority supervises the AI Act, and where would I report to it?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Selling a subscription to businesses in other EU states: which place-of-supply rule applies, is it reverse charge, and what must the invoice say (Q-139, Q-141, Q-144, Q-145)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Paying a model vendor outside Croatia: do I self-account for VAT on that purchased service (Q-144)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If I pass usage-based model costs through to customers, how do I invoice them? See UC-11.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Version or date","u":""},{"t":"Claim ids","u":""}],[{"t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02024R1689-20260727"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 2(1), 2(6), 2(8), 2(10), 2(12), 3(1), 3(3), 3(4), 3(60), 3(68), 4, 4a, 5, 6, 25, 50(1) to (5), 111(2) to (4), 113, Annex III","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 27 July 2026, retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-01, -02, -04 to -08, -10 to -12, -15, -17 to -19","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Digital Omnibus on AI","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2026/1744/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Art. 1(5), 1(6), 1(7), Art. 1 replacing Art. 113, Art. 4","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 8 July 2026, published 24 July 2026, in force 27 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-03, -04, -11, -13, -16, -19","u":""}],[{"t":"AI Act, original Official Journal text","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 4 and 113(a)","u":""},{"t":"Historical wording to 26 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-03","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission AI Act implementation timeline","u":"https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/timeline/timeline-implementation-eu-ai-act"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Milestones 2 August 2026 and 2 December 2026","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-05, -07, -10","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission regulatory framework on AI","u":"https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/regulatory-framework-ai"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Transparency guidelines (20 July 2026), labelling code opinion (9 July 2026)","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07, not read in full","u":""},{"t":"Gap, no claim","u":""}],[{"t":"Procedure 2025/0360/COD and Procedure 2025/0404/COD","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/procedure/EN/2025_360"},{"t":"EUR-Lex","u":""},{"t":"Procedure status","u":""},{"t":"Ongoing as checked 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-14","u":""}],[{"t":"GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 2, 3, 4(7) to (8), 5, 6, 9, 10, 12, 13, 14, 17, 22, 28, 33, 35 to 37, 55, 56, 77, recital 51","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-SCOPE-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-01, -02, -04, -M02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-02, -03, -06 to -08, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, -04, -05, -07, -09, -11, -15, -M01, -M02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01, -07, -13, F-SECTOR-06 to -08, -15, -16","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, controller and processor","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Part I paras. 12 to 13, 39 to 41, Part II paras. 99, 112 to 114, 128, 143 to 145","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.1","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, -15, -M01, -M02","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Opinion 22/2024, reliance on processors","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2024-10/edpb_opinion_202422_relianceonprocessors-sub-processors_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 22 to 29, 34 to 41, 69 to 71","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 7 October 2024","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 01/2022, right of access","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-04/edpb_guidelines_202201_data_subject_rights_access_v2_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 47 to 57","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, Article 3 and Chapter V","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 9 to 13","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, 14 February 2023","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, -20","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2023/1795, EU-US DPF","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/1795/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Art. 1, Art. 3, Annex I Section I.3","u":""},{"t":"In force as checked 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, -08","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-04/edpb_dpf_faq-for-businesses_v2_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Questions 3, 3.1, 3.3","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, adopted 15 January 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, -11","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU case list, C-703/25 P","u":"https://juris.curia.europa.eu/juris/liste.jsf?num=C-703/25&language=en"},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Case status","u":""},{"t":"\"Case in progress\" on 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB letter of 31 July 2026","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-08/edpb_letter_20260731_us_supremecourt_judgment_trump_v_slaughter_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Page 2, final substantive paragraph","u":""},{"t":"31 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2021/914, standard contractual clauses","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Art. 1, Annex Clauses 14 to 16","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 4 June 2021","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-13, -15","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2000/31/EC (e-Commerce)","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/31/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 5(1)(a) to (g), 8(1), 8(4), recital 33","u":""},{"t":"Consolidation of 17 February 2024 checked","u":""},{"t":"F-ECOMMERCE-01, -02, F-SECTOR-12, -13","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Notice 2021/C 525/01 on Directive 2011/83/EU)","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52021XC1229(04"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Section 3.2.2.2","u":""},{"t":"29 December 2021","u":""},{"t":"F-ECOMMERCE-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Your Europe, regulated professions","u":"https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/work/professional-qualifications/regulated-professions/index_en.htm"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"What is a regulated profession","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-SECTOR-12, -13","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2017/745 (MDR), consolidated 19 July 2026","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02017R0745-20260719"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 2(1), 2(12), 6, Annex VIII Rule 11","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 19 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-SECTOR-09","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2014/65/EU (MiFID II), consolidated 6 June 2026","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02014L0065-20260606"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 4(1)(4), 5(1), Annex I Section A","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 6 June 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-SECTOR-10","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission CRA implementation FAQ v1.4","u":"https://ec.europa.eu/newsroom/dae/redirection/document/123307"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Section 1.2","u":""},{"t":"4 September 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-CRA-02","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2018_05_42_805.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 1, 4, 57","u":""},{"t":"Published 9 May 2018, in force 25 May 2018","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-AUTH-01, -02","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP homepage and AZOP breach reporting","u":"https://azop.hr/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Homepage introduction, breach page first paragraph","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-AUTH-01, -06","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 3/2018, territorial scope","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_3_2018_territorial_scope_after_public_consultation_en_1.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Section 2 introduction, printed p. 13","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.1","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-AUTH-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2003_10_173_2504.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 6(1)","u":""},{"t":"Original act, retrieved 2026-11-07. Amended by NN 67/2008, 36/2009, 130/2011, 30/2014 and 32/2019, with no Article 6 change identified","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01","u":""}],[{"t":"Model vendor commercial, consumer and API terms (examples)","u":""},{"t":"Vendor","u":""},{"t":"Training, DPA and EEA-use clauses","u":""},{"t":"Read your own vendor's current version","u":""},{"t":"Vendor statements, not law","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-08","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: An AI inbox helper with a human approving every reply","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small business that answers lead, client, billing and event mail by hand and wants AI to suggest labels and draft replies that the owner edits and sends.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-001, Q-073, Q-074, Q-075, Q-076, Q-077, Q-080, Q-084, Q-086, Q-131]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-BASIS-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-04, F-GDPR-BASIS-07, F-GDPR-BASIS-09, F-GDPR-BASIS-M02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-06, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-08, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-02, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02, F-SECTOR-06, F-SECTOR-08, F-SECTOR-16, F-AI-02, F-AI-04, F-AI-05, F-AI-06, F-AI-07, F-AI-08, F-AI-10, F-AI-11, F-AI-13, F-AI-15, F-AI-18, N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-02, N-HR-AUTH-06, N-HR-AUTH-07, N-HR-AUTH-M04]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"ai-inbox":{"title":"An AI inbox helper with a human approving every reply","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each fact links to a question in questions.json. \"Unknown\" is a valid answer. It keeps the related checks visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which AI system, model provider and plan you would use.","t":"A consumer chat plan, a commercial seat and a paid API key carry different terms. A built-in assistant in your mail suite is a different system from a workflow tool that calls a model API. (Q-001)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which mail the helper would read, and whose data it holds.","t":"Your own non-client mail, lead enquiries and active client threads are different inputs. Quoted earlier messages and signatures bring in third parties who never wrote to you. (Q-073)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which lawful basis covers sending message content to each provider.","t":"Answering an enquiry and running it through an AI tool can be separate purposes. Write the basis down for each one. (Q-074)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who receives message content, and from which countries they can access it.","t":"Count the mail provider, the workflow tool or your own server, the model provider and every place a copy lands. (Q-075)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which transfer mechanism covers each provider outside the EEA.","t":"A provider with EU hosting can still have support or sub-processors elsewhere. (Q-076)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How long each copy is kept, and what starts that clock.","t":"Copies include workflow execution logs, error notices, the task sheet, the daily digest, backups and the model provider's own logs. (Q-077)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"When people are told.","t":"For senders and for people in quoted threads, the first disclosure to a new recipient can set the deadline. A short pilot is still processing. (Q-080)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether a provider uses your content for its own purposes.","t":"Training or product improvement on your mail changes the provider's role and your notice. A training opt-out on a consumer plan is not processor terms. (Q-084)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the processor agreement is binding for your exact account and plan.","t":"A public DPA page does not prove your account accepted it. (Q-086)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether mail can contain special-category data.","t":"Health details, beliefs or similar facts arrive in free text without warning. If they can, Article 9 applies and a keyword filter does not keep them out. (Q-131)","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"Each provider's role","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A controller decides why and how personal data is processed. A processor handles it on the controller's behalf. Assess each activity separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The mail contains personal data and the processing falls within GDPR Articles 2 and 3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A product category or a document called \"DPA\" does not settle the role. A provider that reuses content for its own model training may need a separate role analysis.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8) and 28(10). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01. EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, version 2.1, Part I, paragraphs 12 to 13 and 39 to 41. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"A processor contract for every provider in the path","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Processing by a processor must rest on a binding contract or other legal act, in writing, that states the subject, duration, nature, purpose, data types and people affected.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The terms must require documented instructions (including on transfers), confidentiality, Article 32 security, lawful sub-processing, assistance, audits, and return or deletion at the end. Sub-processors need prior specific or general written authorisation, with notice of changes and a chance to object.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Transfer SCC Modules 2 and 3, properly completed, can carry the Article 28 terms. A general privacy notice is not the agreement. A signed DPA does not end your duty to keep checking the processor's guarantees.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Article 28(1), 28(2), 28(3) opening sentence, points (a) to (d) and (g), 28(4) and 28(9). Claims F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09 and F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01. Points (e), (f) and (h) on assistance and audits have no claim in this set. Verify them against the GDPR text. Commission SCC questions and answers, Question 29, and Decision (EU) 2021/914, Article 1(2), recital 9 and Annex, Modules 2 and 3. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14. EDPB Opinion 22/2024, paragraphs 22 to 29, on knowing every processor in the chain. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12. A service-by-service match of each DPA, sub-processor list, transfer terms and exit process to the real data flows, such as logs, backups and support access (inference). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Inference.","t":"A consumer AI plan meant for individuals, with a training opt-out, usually does not supply Article 28 terms. Use an account whose accepted terms include processor terms before any real message.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"A lawful basis for each purpose","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Each processing purpose needs an Article 6 basis, set before processing starts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"If you rely on legitimate interests, record the interest, why the AI step is necessary, less intrusive alternatives such as plain mailbox filters, and the balance with the sender's reasonable expectations.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Reusing mail collected to answer a customer for a new purpose needs a compatibility assessment and advance notice, unless the person consents or a qualifying Union or Member State law applies under Article 6(4). A new notice alone does not make the reuse compatible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 5(1)(b), 5(2), 6(1), 6(1)(f) and 6(4). Claims F-GDPR-BASIS-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-04 and F-GDPR-BASIS-M02. CJEU C-621/22, paragraphs 37 to 45, on the three cumulative conditions. Claim F-GDPR-BASIS-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Special-category data in free text","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Health, beliefs, sexual orientation and the other Article 9(1) categories are prohibited from processing unless an Article 9(2) condition applies. An Article 6 basis is also needed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The processed data reveals an Article 9(1) category. Free text and model outputs can reveal protected attributes (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Ordinary financial data is not Article 9 data by default. A small business has no general exemption.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Article 9(1) and 9(2), recital 51. Claim F-SECTOR-06. Article 10 for criminal data, and Article 9 alongside Article 6. Claim F-GDPR-BASIS-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Telling senders and third parties","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"For data collected from the person, give Article 13 information at collection. For data not collected from the person, such as someone named in a quoted thread, give Article 14 information within a reasonable time and at most one month, or earlier at the first communication or first disclosure to another recipient. Before processing for a new purpose, inform people about that purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The notice must name recipients or categories, any third-country transfer and its safeguard, and the retention period or the criteria for it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Articles 13(4) and 14(5)(a) avoid repeating information the person already has. Article 14(5)(b) to (d) has narrow exceptions with conditions. Lack of budget alone does not establish disproportionate effort. Article 14(5)(b) is not an exception for Article 13 direct collection.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1) to 13(3), 14(3) and 14(4). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-07. Articles 13(4) and 14(5)(a) to (d). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-08. Articles 13(1)(e) and (f), 14(1)(e) and (f). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-03. Articles 13(2)(a), 14(2)(a) and 5(1)(e), WP260 rev.01 Annex, printed pp. 38 to 39. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Transfers outside the EEA","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A transfer happens when an exporter subject to GDPR makes personal data available to a separate entity in a third country. Chapter V then needs adequacy, appropriate safeguards or a narrow derogation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"For a US provider under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, check the official DPF List for active certification that covers the exact entity and data. Certifications renew yearly.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"DPF coverage removes the need for an Article 46 tool for covered transfers. It does not replace Article 28 terms. EU hosting alone does not rule out support access or onward transfers from elsewhere.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paragraphs 9 to 13. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01. GDPR Articles 44, 45(1), 46(1) and 49(1). Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-02. Decision (EU) 2023/1795, Article 1 and Annex I Section I.3. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04. EDPB DPF FAQ for businesses, version 2.0 of 15 January 2026, Questions 3 and 3.1. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09. Question 3.3 and the 2023 EDPB information note. Claims F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11 and F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13. Mapping each flow. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Automated decisions and impact assessments","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Article 22 covers decisions based solely on automated processing with legal or similarly significant effects. Article 35 requires a DPIA where processing is likely to create high risk.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Routine labelling and drafting that you review before anything is sent appears unlikely to be a solely automated significant decision on this scope (inference). Large-scale special-category processing or systematic evaluation can still trigger a DPIA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not let the helper hide, archive or delete complaints, deadlines or contract notices. Hiding them could turn a label into a decision with real effects (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Article 22(1) to 22(4). Claim F-SECTOR-16. Articles 13(2)(f), 14(2)(g). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-06. Articles 35(1) to 35(4) and 37(1). Claim F-SECTOR-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Rights requests and complaints that arrive by mail","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Recognise a request to access, erase or object by its substance, even when it does not name the GDPR. EDPB guidance says an access request has no prescribed form. Respond without undue delay and within one month. Where needed because of complexity or the number of requests, the period can extend by two further months. Explain the extension and the reasons within the first month.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The request reaches you through an appropriate channel, which includes the inbox the helper reads (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None found that let an AI label delay the clock (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 12(1) to 12(4). Claims F-GDPR-RIGHTS-01 and F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02. EDPB Guidelines 01/2022 on access, paragraphs 47 to 57.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"If the helper sends, forwards or leaks mail","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"An unintended send or a stored copy you did not expect can be a personal data breach. Notify the competent authority without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours, unless the breach is unlikely to risk people's rights. A notice after 72 hours needs reasons for the delay. Document every breach. If high risk to people is likely, also tell them without undue delay, subject to the Article 34 exceptions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"In Croatia the authority is AZOP. Check competence first if processing is cross-border.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Low risk removes the notification, not the documentation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 33(1), 33(4) and 33(5), 34(1) to 34(3). Claim N-HR-AUTH-M04. AZOP breach page, https://azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/. Claim N-HR-AUTH-06. NN 42/2018-805, Article 4. Claim N-HR-AUTH-01. GDPR Articles 55, 56 and 77. Claim N-HR-AUTH-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Record of processing (no claim in this set)","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"GDPR Article 30 requires a record of processing activities. Article 30(5) exempts organisations with fewer than 250 employees, with limits.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The exemption does not apply where the processing is likely to result in a risk to people's rights, is not occasional, or includes Article 9 or Article 10 data. Ongoing mail processing is unlikely to be occasional (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None beyond the three limits above. A one-page record of this processing is cheap even where it is not required (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 30(1) and 30(5).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"None in this set. Verify against the GDPR text before you rely on it.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"National identification numbers (no claim in this set)","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"GDPR Article 87 lets Member States set conditions for processing a national identification number.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The helper reads mail that holds a personal identification number, such as an 11-digit number in an invoice or signature.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Not checked. Redacting these numbers before the model call avoids the question for the draft step.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Article 87. Croatian implementing act NN 42/2018-805, published 9 May 2018, in force 25 May 2018, Articles 1 and 57 for identity and commencement.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"N-HR-AUTH-02 covers only the act's identity, scope and commencement. No claim in this set covers its rules on identification numbers. Verify.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"AI Act: your role and AI literacy","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 (Digital Omnibus on AI) amended the AI Act. It was adopted on 8 July 2026, published on 24 July 2026 and entered into force on 27 July 2026. From that date, amended Article 4 requires providers and deployers to take measures to support AI literacy of staff and people acting for them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You use an AI system under your authority for professional purposes, which makes you a deployer. Building an own-brand AI service that you supply to others can make you a provider of that system, without making you the provider of the underlying model.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 4 does not require you to guarantee a specific literacy level for any individual. Purely personal, non-professional use falls outside the deployer definition. A short written note on what the helper does, what it must not see and how each draft is checked is useful evidence, not a safe harbour (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Reg. (EU) 2026/1744, title, Article 1(5) and Article 4. AI Act consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 3(3), 3(4) and 3(68), Article 4(1) to 4(3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-AI-13, F-AI-02 and F-AI-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"AI Act: transparency for interactions and publications","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Since 2 August 2026, Article 50(1) requires providers to design systems that interact directly with people so that people know they are dealing with AI. Article 50(4) requires deployers to disclose deepfakes and AI text published to inform the public on matters of public interest.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Article 50(1) applies to direct interaction with a person. Article 50(4) text duties apply to publication on matters of public interest. Article 50(5) requires the information by the first interaction or exposure.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 50(1) does not apply where AI interaction is obvious in context. The Article 50(4) text duty does not apply where human review or editorial control occurred and a person holds editorial responsibility. A private reply that you review and send as yourself is not shown to be a direct AI interaction or a public-interest publication (inference). No blanket duty to add an AI disclaimer to your mail was established. Adding one is your choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"AI Act consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 50(1), 50(4), 50(5), Article 3(60) and Article 113.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-AI-05 and F-AI-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"AI Act: machine-readable marking","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Article 50(2) requires providers of systems that generate synthetic text, audio, images or video to mark outputs as artificial in a machine-readable, detectable form.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"You are the provider of the generating system. A deployer using a third-party model is not the addressee of this duty.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Standard assistive editing that does not substantially change the input is excluded to the stated extent. Article 111(4) gives systems placed on the market before 2 August 2026 until 2 December 2026, for Article 50(2) only. It gives no extra time for Article 50(1) or 50(4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"AI Act consolidated 27 July 2026, Article 50(2), Article 111(4) and Article 113.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-AI-06 and F-AI-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"AI Act: high risk and prohibited practices","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Annex III high-risk duties in Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from 2 December 2027. Article 5 prohibitions have applied since 2 February 2025, with further prohibitions from 2 December 2026 that do not appear to concern email drafting (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"High risk turns on intended use. Screening job applicants through the inbox is an Annex III recruitment use and needs escalation. Ordinary mailbox triage is not shown to have an Annex III purpose (inference).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"AI use alone does not make a system high risk. Article 6(3) has a limited, conditional Annex III exclusion, which profiling of natural persons prevents.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"AI Act consolidated 27 July 2026, Articles 5, 6(2) to 6(4), 113(a) to 113(d), Annex III point 4(a).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-AI-11, F-AI-18, F-AI-15 and F-AI-10.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"When a reply becomes marketing","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A drafted reply that adds an unrequested offer can become direct marketing. Electronic marketing to natural persons generally needs prior consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The existing-customer rule needs all of these: the same sender, contact details obtained lawfully in the context of a sale, similar products or services, a clear and free objection at collection and in every message, and no earlier refusal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A necessary service reply without promotion is not marketing by default. A published email address is not the existing-customer exception.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 13(1) to 13(5). CJEU C-654/23 Inteligo Media, paragraphs 48 to 69 and operative rulings 1 and 2. GDPR Articles 21(2), 21(3) and 95.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-GDPR-BASIS-07. See UC-05 for the Croatian marketing rules.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each step names its pass evidence. \"Outside check\" means the by-hand checks in the README. Most steps happen inside your accounts, where an outside check cannot see, so the evidence comes from you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Write the objective and a baseline week.","t":"Name the first problem to solve: fewer inboxes, faster replies or fewer missed messages. List mailboxes and aliases with their provider, no passwords. Record business messages a day and inbox minutes a day for one normal week. Without that baseline, no later number shows the helper helped. Write your own time and budget limits and who approves a purchase. Note whether you act as a processor for any client, because that question goes to counsel before client mail.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the four items exist in writing before anything is bought.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: can read public MX records to show which provider receives mail for a domain. It cannot see plan, mailbox count or volume.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Confirm a read route on your current provider first.","t":"Do not move mail for a reversible test. Confirm the route gives read access through a read-only credential, or through the broker in step 3, and confirm the scopes the credential actually grants. Check also whether the route can support a draft-only limit. If it cannot, the pilot can still run with drafts kept as plain text that you copy by hand.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a written list of granted scopes. If the only route is a full mailbox login and no broker exists, the flow does not run. Help on request, with text you copy in and out by hand, remains.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Owner evidence: the scope list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Build the draft-only boundary and test it on synthetic mail.","t":"Write synthetic messages, including adversarial ones that tell the helper to send, forward or delete. Put a small broker between the flow and the mailbox. The broker holds the mail token and exposes only \"create draft\" and, if you want, \"apply one label from a fixed list\". Redact signatures, phone numbers, IBANs, 11-digit numbers, quoted history and attachments before text reaches the model.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: through the boundary, call send, forward, delete, archive, move and label removal. Each must be refused. Then run the adversarial set. Refusal tests prove the capability is absent. Adversarial runs only show observed behaviour.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Owner evidence: the refusal-test log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Without a boundary, nothing writes to the mailbox. Drafts stay plain text in the digest for you to copy by hand.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Turn off stored content in the workflow tool and prove it.","t":"Set every execution save setting (failed, successful, manual and per-step progress) to \"do not save\" unless you chose otherwise. Apply the change with any required restart.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: after the settings take effect, force a failure with a synthetic message and inspect what was stored. Only evidence from a failure run after the change counts. A log retention limit describes pruning, not that no content is kept.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Owner evidence: the forced-failure log and a screenshot of the settings.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Test the stop procedure.","t":"Write one procedure: deactivate the flow, cancel running and waiting executions, clear queued and retry work, revoke the mail token, and revoke the model API key.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: start the procedure while one synthetic run is active, one is waiting, one is queued and one is due for retry. Send a new synthetic message. Confirm no model call, draft, label or task line appears afterwards, and check the model provider's console for calls after the stop time.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Owner evidence: the stop-test record with timestamps.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Settle terms, basis, notices, transfers and retention before any real message.","t":"This includes your own non-client mail. For each provider in the path, confirm the accepted account terms include processor terms. Write the Article 6 basis. Update your privacy notice first if it needs to name new recipients, transfers or retention. Identify each transfer route. Document retention for every processor and every copy, including the model provider's, which you take from its terms and account settings.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a one-page record listing each provider, its accepted DPA, transfer route and retention, plus the dated notice change.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: can read the published privacy notice and report whether it names an AI provider, the workflow tool and any third-country transfer. It cannot see whether an account accepted a DPA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Run your own non-client mail, approved one message at a time.","t":"Apply an approval label by hand. Show that the trigger selects approved message IDs before it fetches any body. Skip messages with special-category data, client matters or confidential terms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the digest lists every processed message, and each one carries your approval label.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Client mail only after counsel answers.","t":"Start with a small client subset you approve by hand. Keep every earlier control. Repeat the refusal tests and the full stop test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: written counsel answers to the questions under \"Ask a specialist\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Measure against the baseline and apply the stop rules.","t":"Write the rules down before each gate starts. These are proposed decision rules, not validated statistics.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"Stop immediately:","t":"any message processed that you did not approve, any send, forward or delete by the helper, any mailbox write outside the boundary, any boundary call that should be refused and is not, stored content found after the log test said none would be kept, or an adversarial message that changes the flow's behaviour.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"Severe:","t":"a wrong fact in a draft, a missed urgent message, or a deadline or complaint not surfaced. Two severe errors stop the gate until the cause is fixed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"Cosmetic:","t":"tone, typos, formatting. Track only.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"Not useful:","t":"compare minutes per week over the same whole-week period. Baseline: inbox minutes. Pilot: inbox minutes plus review time plus build and upkeep time in that period. Agree any longer horizon for spreading build time before the gate starts and apply it to both figures. If the pilot figure is not lower, stop. Plain mailbox filters may be enough.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"About 30 messages per gate is a proposed minimum for a decision. It does not prove safety. If fewer arrive, the low volume is itself an answer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Also track drafts sent unchanged, edited or discarded, labels you corrected, missed or mislabelled messages, duplicates, review time per draft and actual model spend from the provider console.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Roll back in two parts.","t":"First the copies you can delete: run the stop procedure, delete the workflow and stored executions, delete the API key, remove the task sheet, digest and backups. Then the copies providers hold: revoking a key does not delete their records. Send a deletion request where offered and record the contractual retention that still applies.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A draft scope that can send.","t":"Google's Gmail scope page describes gmail.compose as \"Manage drafts and send emails\". No scope on that page allows drafts without send. On that route, a credential that can draft can also send. Check the same point for any other mail provider.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating a missing Send step as a boundary.","t":"A workflow without a send node is an application control. The credential still allows sending. Only a broker or an equivalent enforced limit counts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"An approval prompt is not a boundary.","t":"A chat connector that asks before sending still holds a general mailbox credential. Draft text you copy by hand stays within the rule. Mailbox writes through that connector do not.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Filtering after the fetch.","t":"On a hosted workflow tool, check whether the trigger receives the full message before any filter step runs. If it does, the tool has already seen mail the filter later drops, and a code step there is not a local pre-filter.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Saving only successful runs off.","t":"Failed runs and error notifications can hold message content. Test with a forced failure.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Forgetting the other copies.","t":"The task sheet, digest, backups and the model provider's logs are copies with their own retention.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A keyword filter as the privacy control.","t":"Pattern matching misses sensitive content in other words and third-party data in quoted threads. Use it only as a second layer that routes a match to needs-me.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A consumer plan with a training opt-out.","t":"That is a product setting, not Article 28 terms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Labels that hide mail.","t":"Use a neutral label set such as lead, client-active, billing, event, review-later and needs-me. Never archive, hide or delete. Rename any \"spam\" or \"ignore\" label to review-later.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Auto-drafting a rights request or complaint.","t":"Route access, erasure and objection requests, and complaints, to needs-me with the one-month clock noted. Never auto-draft them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Letting message content steer the flow.","t":"The model's output is only a label from a fixed list and a draft body. Text inside a message never becomes an instruction.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Timing a purchase around a promotion or annual plan.","t":"Confirm currency, tax, monthly versus annual billing, trial end, renewal price and cancellation before you commit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Migrating mail to run a test.","t":"A mail cutover is its own task with alias mapping, old-mail preservation and a tested rollback. It is not step one of a pilot.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Act on these in order. Stop at the first item that fails and report it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Confirm the baseline file exists with objective, mailbox list, limits and one week of counts. Verify: file path and date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] List the scopes the mail credential actually grants. Verify: paste the scope list from the provider's token info, not from documentation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Build the broker with exactly two actions: create_draft(thread_id, from_address, body) and optional apply_label(message_id, label) where label is in a fixed enum. Verify: unit tests that call send, forward, delete, archive, move and remove-label through the broker and assert each is refused.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Give the flow and the model no general mailbox token and no general authenticated HTTP route to the mailbox. Verify: search the flow config and environment for mail tokens outside the broker.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add redaction before the model call for signatures, phone numbers, IBANs, 11-digit numbers, quoted history and attachments. Verify: run the synthetic set and diff model inputs against expected redacted text.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Constrain model output to {label, draft_body} with label in the enum. Reject anything else. Verify: adversarial messages produce no tool call and no extra field.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Select only messages with the approval label at the trigger, before any body is fetched. Verify: log message IDs fetched and compare with approved IDs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Set every execution save setting to off and apply it. Verify: force a failure after the change and inspect stored data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Script the stop procedure. Verify: the four-state stop test passes and the model console shows no calls after the stop time.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Write the digest: every message processed, every draft, every task line. Verify: digest count equals approved count.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Do not process real mail until the owner confirms step 6 in writing. Do not process client mail until counsel answers exist.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Counsel:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"For this mail, am I the controller, or a processor for some clients? Are the mail provider, workflow tool and model provider my processors?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Which Article 6 basis covers sending client messages to these processors?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"How should special-category data be handled if it arrives?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Do my client contracts limit disclosure to third parties or require client approval of sub-processors?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"Which notice changes are needed before the first live disclosure, given Articles 13, 14(3), 13(3) and 14(4)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"Which transfer route applies to each provider, including US-based ones?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"","t":"Which agreement did each provider account actually accept, and does it match the public terms?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"","t":"Is a DPIA needed for this scope, and does Article 30(5) exempt me from a record of processing here?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"","t":"Do Croatian rules on personal identification numbers under NN 42/2018 affect what the helper may read?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Accountant:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Does an annual SaaS commitment for the workflow tool or model credits need any special treatment in my books?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Do foreign SaaS and API purchases trigger a reverse-charge VAT entry for my business form?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"All retrieved or checked 2026-11-07 unless noted.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679. Articles 4(7), 4(8), 5, 6, 9, 10, 12 to 14, 21, 22, 28, 30(5), 33, 34, 35, 37, 44 to 49, 55, 56, 77, 87 and 95.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2021/914 (standard contractual clauses), https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj/eng. Article 1(2), recital 9, Annex Modules 2 and 3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"European Commission, New Standard Contractual Clauses, questions and answers, https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/international-dimension-data-protection/new-standard-contractual-clauses-questions-and-answers-overview_en. Question 29.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor, version 2.1, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf. Part I paragraphs 12 to 13 and 39 to 41, Part II paragraphs 94 to 99.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Opinion 22/2024 on processors and sub-processors, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2024-10/edpb_opinion_202422_relianceonprocessors-sub-processors_en.pdf. Paragraphs 22 to 29.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021 on Article 3 and Chapter V, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf. Paragraphs 9 to 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795 (EU-US DPF), https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/1795/oj/eng. Article 1, Annex I Section I.3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB DPF FAQ for businesses, version 2.0, adopted 15 January 2026, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-04/edpb_dpf_faq-for-businesses_v2_en.pdf. Questions 3, 3.1 and 3.3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"WP29 Guidelines on transparency, WP260 rev.01, endorsed by the EDPB, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-09/wp260rev01_en.pdf. Annex, storage-period row.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 01/2022 on the right of access, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-04/edpb_guidelines_202201_data_subject_rights_access_v2_en.pdf. Paragraphs 47 to 57.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"CJEU C-621/22, judgment of 4 October 2024, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62022CJ0621. Paragraphs 37 to 45.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"CJEU C-654/23 Inteligo Media, judgment of 13 November 2025, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62023CJ0654. Paragraphs 48 to 69.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2002/58. Article 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"AI Act, consolidated 27 July 2026, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02024R1689-20260727. Articles 2 to 6, 50, 111(4), 113, Annex III.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Digital Omnibus on AI, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2026/1744/oj/eng. Article 1, Article 4.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Commission AI Act implementation timeline, https://ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu/en/ai-act/timeline/timeline-implementation-eu-ai-act.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018-805, published 9 May 2018, https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2018_05_42_805.html. Articles 1, 4 and 57. Rules on identification numbers not checked.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"AZOP breach-reporting page, https://azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Google, Gmail API scopes, https://developers.google.com/workspace/gmail/api/auth/scopes. Entry for gmail.compose, \"Manage drafts and send emails\". Vendor page, retrieved 2026-11-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Gaps: workflow-tool logging behaviour, model-provider retention and draft-only options for non-Google mail routes vary by vendor and were not checked for any named product. The stop procedure has no vendor guarantee of immediate cancellation. AZOP guidance on email and AI, and the national AI Act authority, remain open.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-09","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: A script that measures visits from AI assistants, on your own and client sites","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small agency that adds its own or a third-party script to count visits referred by AI assistants or other referrers, on its own marketing sites and on sites it builds or runs for clients.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-027, Q-029, Q-030, Q-031, Q-178, Q-181, Q-189, Q-075, Q-083, Q-084]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-02, F-DEVICE-03, F-DEVICE-05, F-DEVICE-06, F-DEVICE-09, F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-11, F-DEVICE-13, F-DEVICE-14, F-DEVICE-M01, F-DEVICE-M02, F-DEVICE-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09, F-GDPR-BASIS-01, F-GDPR-BASIS-04, F-GDPR-BASIS-08, F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-08, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-03, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"referral":{"title":"A script that measures visits from AI assistants","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each fact links to a question in questions.json. \"Unknown\" is a valid answer. It keeps the related checks visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the script stores or reads anything on the device, including temporary memory.","t":"A random ID held only in memory for one page load can still count as information on the device. It is not automatically out of scope. (Q-027)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the browser computes a result and sends it to someone else.","t":"A script that decides \"this visit came from an AI assistant\" inside the browser and sends only that yes or no is still making a locally computed result available to another party. Cutting the payload reduces data. It does not take the script out of scope. (Q-029)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Where the IP address in the request comes from.","t":"Every report the browser sends carries the visitor's IP address to the receiving server. If you cannot show that the address does not come from the visitor's device, treat it as in scope. (Q-030)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which function the visitor asked for.","t":"The visitor asked to read a page. Counting which assistant sent them is a purpose of the site owner. If the script also feeds marketing reports, sales pitches or client benchmarks, list each purpose. (Q-031)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What runs before the visitor makes a choice.","t":"If the script loads and reports on first page view, before any banner choice, that order is the first thing to change. (Q-178)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether the notice matches what the live page does.","t":"A notice that says \"no cookies\" or \"no tracking\" while a referral script reports to a server does not match. (Q-181)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether reports really stop after Reject or withdrawal.","t":"A saved \"rejected\" flag is not proof. The network requests have to stop. (Q-189)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who receives the reports, and from which countries.","t":"Name the server that receives them, its host and any provider that can reach the data, including support access and backups. (Q-075)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"On client sites, who decides the purpose.","t":"If the client asked for AI referral numbers and you run the script for it, the client likely decides purposes and you act on its behalf. If you added the script for your own reasons, you decided. (Q-083)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether you reuse the data for yourself or pool it across clients.","t":"Building your own benchmark, case studies or a product dataset from several clients' visits is your own purpose, not the client's. That changes your role. (Q-084)","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"Device access: the referral script is in scope","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Storing information on a visitor's device, or gaining access to information already there, needs consent after clear and complete information, particularly about purposes. The information does not have to be personal data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The script runs in the visitor's browser and tells it to send information to a server. EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 treat storage and access as separate operations, each enough on its own. They treat storage as technology-neutral, so memory-only or session-only handling is not automatically outside scope. Use that stays wholly inside the browser is not access, but a locally computed result that is made available externally is.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Two: access only to transmit a communication, and access strictly necessary for a service the visitor expressly asked for. Business usefulness alone establishes neither.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EU: Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy), Article 5(3), both sentences, consolidated text of 19 December 2009 including Directive 2009/136/EC. Claims F-DEVICE-01 and F-DEVICE-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Croatia: ZEK, NN 76/2022, Article 43(4), first sentence for the rule and second sentence for the exceptions. Claims N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01 and N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Non-personal information is covered: CJEU C-673/17 Planet49, judgment of 1 October 2019, paragraphs 68 to 71 and operative part point 2. Claim F-DEVICE-03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 on the technical scope of Art. 5(3) ePrivacy Directive, version 2.0, adopted 7 October 2024:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraph 6 and paragraphs 35 to 39, storage is technology-neutral and memory-only is not automatically outside scope (F-DEVICE-06)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraphs 35 to 36, 44 and 52 to 53, local use versus results made available externally (F-DEVICE-M01)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraphs 4, 40 and 52 to 55, \"cookieless\" is not a legal conclusion (F-DEVICE-10)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"paragraphs 4, 6 and 40, scope and exemptions are separate assessments (F-DEVICE-05)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Dates.","t":"ZEK took effect on 12 July 2022. NN 14/2024 Article 115(1) repealed ZEK Article 41 from 15 February 2024. NN 45/2026 amended ZEK from 7 May 2026. Neither change touched Article 43(4). This is a provision-level check, not a full audit of Croatian law. Claims N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03 (amendment chain) and N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04 (commencement dates).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"The IP address travels with every report","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"IP-based tracking can fall within Article 5(3) when the address comes from the visitor's device. An entity that cannot ensure the address does not come from the device takes the steps Article 5(3) requires.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The browser sends the request, so the receiving server gets the address whether or not the script reads it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Addresses generated by carrier-grade NAT can be analysed differently. Being in scope does not by itself mean consent is required. The exemptions still need testing. Necessary network transmission and later tracking are separate purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paragraphs 54 to 56 and footnotes 28 to 29 (F-DEVICE-11), and paragraph 55, last sentence (F-DEVICE-M02).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Note.","t":"Dropping or truncating the IP address on the server is good minimisation under the GDPR. It does not settle the Article 5(3) question for the request itself.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"No analytics exemption fits referral measurement","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"First-party analytics are not strictly necessary merely because the operator values them. The checked Croatian sources establish no general analytics exemption. A \"cookieless\" label does not show that device access is absent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"This applies to any count of where visitors came from, including counts that keep no identifier.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"WP194 suggested a possible future analytics exemption. That suggestion is not enacted law. Do not import another country's audience-measurement exception.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Article 29 Working Party Opinion 04/2012 on cookie consent exemption (WP194), adopted 7 June 2012, sections 4.2 to 4.3, pages 9 to 11. Claim F-DEVICE-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"ZEK Article 43(4), AZOP page \"Obrada osobnih podataka putem kolačića i usklađivanje s Općom uredbom o zaštiti podataka\", published 14.8.2026, paragraph beginning \"Ako se, međutim\", and EDPB 2/2023 paragraphs 44 and 52 to 56. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"AZOP 14.8.2026: non-essential analytics stay inactive until valid consent. Preselected choices, continued browsing and silence are not consent. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Do not read device properties to tell visitors apart","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Reading screen size, language, time zone or similar properties to recognise a visitor is fingerprinting, and it is in scope. WP29 rejected a consent exemption for fingerprinting used for first-party analytics.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"This applies when properties are read from the device and combined or sent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None for analytics in the cited opinion.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"WP29 Opinion 9/2014 on device fingerprinting (WP224), adopted 25 November 2014, section 6 final paragraphs and sections 7.1 to 7.2. Claim F-DEVICE-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Consent design, if you keep the script","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"If the script needs consent, it stays off until the visitor chooses. Accept and Reject sit on the first layer, are equally easy and are designed equally. You can show what each person chose, when and what they saw. Separate purposes get separate choices.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"This applies to the site where the visitor lands, whether you or a client runs it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not collect extra identifying data only to prove consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"AZOP 14.8.2026, paragraphs beginning \"Banner koji sadrži samo gumb\" and \"Sukladno AZOP-ovoj Preporuci\", and AZOP recommendation updated 6 August 2024. Claims N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-02 and N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 7(1) and EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent, version 1.1, adopted 4 May 2020, paragraphs 104 to 108. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 paragraphs 43 to 45 and 64 to 65, and GDPR Articles 7(3) and 13(1) to (2). Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"After withdrawal, prevent future reads, writes and tracking requests for the withdrawn purpose, and test it. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"GDPR basis and data minimisation for what the server keeps","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"If the reports involve personal data (an IP address, an identifier, a path that names a person), each purpose needs an Article 6 basis. Service-improvement metrics are generally not necessary to perform an online contract. A legitimate-interest assessment does not replace a device-access consent that ePrivacy requires. Collect only what the purpose needs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Legitimate interest under Article 6(1)(f) needs a legitimate interest, necessity, and a balance in which the person's interests and rights do not override yours, with less intrusive means considered. Record the assessment.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A device-access exemption, if one ever fits, does not by itself make the later personal-data processing lawful. The two tests are separate.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679) Articles 5(1)(a) to (c), 5(2) and 6(1). Claim F-GDPR-BASIS-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 6(1)(f) and CJEU C-621/22, paragraphs 37 to 45 and 49 to 50. Claim F-GDPR-BASIS-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 4(1), 5(1)(c) and 6(1), EDPB Guidelines 2/2019 on Article 6(1)(b), paragraphs 48 to 49, and ePrivacy Article 5(3). Claim F-GDPR-BASIS-08.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 2, 4(1), 5, 6 and 95, WP194 sections 1 and 5, Planet49 paragraphs 68 to 71. Claim F-DEVICE-M03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Data protection by design and by default: GDPR Article 25. No claim id in the research set.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Notice: say what the script does, at the time it runs","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The notice names the controller, the purpose (\"measuring which sites and assistants send visitors\"), the basis, the recipients or categories of recipients, any transfer outside the EEA, and how long data is kept. It reaches the visitor when the data is collected. In practice that points to a link next to the banner choice, not only a page in the footer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Use a short first layer with a direct link to the detail. Keep both layers consistent. A policy must match a current technical inventory. A policy's claim is not proof of what is installed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Under Article 13(4) you need not repeat information the person already has. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-08.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1)(a) to (d). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1)(e) to (f). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 13(2)(a), WP260 rev.01 annex, storage-period row. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1) to (3), timing. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 12(1), WP260 rev.01 paragraphs 35 to 36, layered notice. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-09.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"AZOP 14.8.2026, paragraphs beginning \"Ističemo da činjenica\", \"Stoga je prije svega potrebno\" and \"Sama tvrdnja\", and numbered recommendations 1 to 4. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Client sites: roles, written terms and who answers for the banner","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A controller decides the purposes and means. A processor handles data on the controller's behalf. Roles follow what each party actually decides, not the contract label. If you run the script for a client who wants the numbers, the client is likely the controller and you its processor. Processing by a processor needs a written contract that sets the subject, duration, nature, purpose, data types and people affected, and binds you to documented instructions, confidentiality, security and lawful use of sub-processors.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"If you and the client decide purposes together, or you reuse the data for your own benchmark or product, you move toward joint controller or controller for that part. Joint controllers need an Article 26 arrangement. Sub-processors (your host, your database) need the client's prior written authorisation, specific or general.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Article 28 sets no small-provider exception. AZOP states that the site owner stays responsible when an outside designer builds the site, so a script you add does not move the client's duty to you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8) and 28(10). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor, version 2.1, adopted 7 July 2021, Part I paragraphs 12 to 13 and 39 to 41. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 26(1) to (3). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(3) opening sentence and 28(9). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(3)(a) to (d). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(2) and 28(4). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Service-by-service review of terms against actual data flows. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Owner responsibility: AZOP 14.8.2026. Claim N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Transfers, if the receiving server sits outside the EEA","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A transfer happens when an exporter subject to the GDPR makes personal data available to another entity in a third country. Map who receives the reports, where it stores them, and who can reach them remotely, then match each flow to a mechanism.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"This matters when your endpoint, its host or a support provider is outside the EEA.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"No transfer question arises if no entity in a third country receives or can remotely access the personal data. Check that against the host's real regions, support access and backups.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, version 2.0, 14 February 2023, paragraphs 9 to 13. Claims F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01 and F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20. UC-06 covers the DPF and SCC details.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Decide whether you need the number at all.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: if nobody reads the AI referral report, remove the script from every site.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: search the built site for the script tag and the endpoint host. Load the page with an AI-assistant referrer and confirm no request goes out.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: script tags in the HTML and outbound requests on page load.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Stop it running before a choice.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: load the script only after the visitor accepts an analytics purpose. Make Reject as easy as Accept, on the first layer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: in a clean browser, load the page with an AI-assistant referrer, do nothing, and record requests. Repeat after Reject, after Accept and after withdrawal. Record what the script reads, writes, sends and uses in each state (F-DEVICE-14).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: requests to the endpoint before any choice, after Reject and after withdrawal, and whether the banner shows equal choices.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Cut the payload.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: send only the referrer's origin (scheme and host), the page path without its query string or fragment, and a site label. A query string can carry an email, a token or a campaign identifier. A full referrer URL can carry more than the site name.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: read the request body in the network log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: the fields in each request and whether they include query strings or full referrer URLs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Send no identifier, and read no device properties.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: drop any visitor ID. If you must avoid double counting within one page load, use a fresh random value created per page load and held only in memory, never written to storage. That value is still in scope. Do not read screen size, language or time zone.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: inspect cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage and IndexedDB after each consent state. Read the script for screen., navigator.language and storage calls.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: storage contents after each state and the script text.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Send without cookies, to as few recipients as possible.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: send the request with credentials omitted. Prefer an endpoint on your own or the client's domain over a separate third-party host, so fewer parties receive the IP address.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: check the request's cookie header and destination host.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: the destination host and whether cookies were attached.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Keep aggregates and drop the rest on the server.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: discard or truncate the IP address at ingestion. Turn off or shorten raw request logs on the endpoint. Store counts per day, path and referrer origin. Set and write down a retention period.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: read the endpoint code and the host's log settings. Confirm the stored table has no IP column and no identifier.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"An outside check cannot see this. It needs the owner's server code and host settings.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Update the notice.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: add one line per site: purpose, data sent, recipient, location, retention, basis. Link it beside the banner choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: compare the notice line with the request fields from step 3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: whether the notice mentions referral measurement and the receiving host. It cannot judge whether the basis is right.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"On client sites, get the client's decision in writing first.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: describe the script to the client in plain words, with the data list, recipient, retention and sub-processors. Sign a processing agreement under Article 28(3) before go-live. Give the client a notice line and put the script behind the client's own consent tool. Do not pool client data for your own use unless the client agrees to a separate arrangement and your role is assessed again.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a signed agreement exists for each client site that runs the script, and the client's banner lists the purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check can show: the script on the client site, its order against the client's banner and the client's notice text. It cannot see contracts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"If you want to keep counting without a browser script, assess it first.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: counting referrers from your own server's request logs avoids a script that tells the browser to send data. It does not settle the device-access question. EDPB guidance says IP-based tracking can fall within scope, and necessary transmission and later tracking are separate purposes. Collection and later use still need assessment. Treat this as a counsel question, not a fix (F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-11).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a written assessment exists before you rely on it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"An outside check cannot see server-side counting.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"It sets no cookies, so no banner.\"","t":"Storage is only half the rule. EDPB guidance treats a script that tells the browser to send data as access.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"It only sends a yes or no.\"","t":"Under EDPB guidance a result computed in the browser and sent out is still access. A smaller payload is better, not exempt.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"The ID is random and never stored.\"","t":"Memory-only handling is not automatically outside scope. It reduces risk. It does not decide consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"We delete IP addresses on the server.\"","t":"That is GDPR minimisation. The request still carried the address from the device.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Legitimate interest covers analytics.\"","t":"A GDPR balancing test does not replace a device-access consent that ePrivacy requires.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Testing without the referrer.","t":"A referral script often fires only when the visitor arrives from a matching site. A checker that loads the page directly sees nothing and reports a clean page. Test with a spoofed referrer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Snippet in the template.","t":"Shipping the script inside a site template or starter kit puts it on client sites the client never reviewed. The client stays responsible and has not decided anything.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Your benchmark, their visitors.","t":"Combining several clients' referral data into your own report or product is your purpose. You cannot rely on the client's processor agreement for it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Full URLs in the payload.","t":"Sending location.href or the full referrer can leak query strings and identifiers you never meant to collect.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Hiding the banner after withdrawal.","t":"The requests must stop, not only the banner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Notice says \"no tracking\".","t":"If the script runs, the notice must say what it sends and to whom.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Act on each item, then run its verify step. Report results with evidence (request log, file path, line).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Inventory. Search the repo and built output for the referral script, its endpoint host and any inline referrer checks. Verify: list every file and page that loads it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Gate on consent. Load the script only after the visitor accepts the analytics purpose in the site's consent tool. On withdrawal, stop sending and remove the listener. Verify: run the four-state test below and confirm zero requests to the endpoint in the first-load, Reject and withdrawn states.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Trim the payload. Send document.referrer reduced to its origin, location.pathname only, and a site label. Do not send location.href, location.search, location.hash or the full referrer. Verify: capture one request and list its fields.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] No storage, no fingerprinting. No cookie, localStorage, sessionStorage or IndexedDB writes. No reads of screen, navigator.language or time zone. Verify: grep the script for those names and check storage after each state.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] No credentials. Send with credentials: 'omit'. Prefer a same-site endpoint. Verify: the request has no cookie header.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Server side. Drop or truncate IP at ingestion. Store daily aggregates only. Set a retention job. Verify: show the table schema and the retention setting. Note that an outside check cannot see this.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Notice. Add the per-site line (purpose, fields, recipient, location, retention, basis) and link it beside the banner. Verify: diff the notice against the captured request fields.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Client sites. Do not add the script to a client site without a recorded client decision and a processing agreement. Verify: list client sites that run it and the agreement reference for each. Flag any site without one to the owner. Do not decide the legal role yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Four-state test. Use a clean browser profile and a referrer that matches the script's trigger. With Playwright, pass the referrer on navigation, for example await page.goto(url, { referer: 'https://chat.yourdomain.com/' }). Record cookies, storage and requests for first load, after Reject, after Accept, and after withdrawal and reload. Verify: attach the four logs.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Does a referral-only script that sends the referrer origin and path, with no identifier and no storage, fall within ZEK Article 43(4)? Does either exemption fit it?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"If we count referrers only from our own server's request logs, with no browser script, is there new device access? What GDPR basis and notice do we need?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"On client sites, are we the client's processor for this script? What changes if we also use the data for our own benchmarks or case studies?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"If the endpoint host or its support access sits outside the EEA, which transfer mechanism applies, and what goes in the client's notice?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"How long can we keep daily aggregate referral counts, and does that retention need its own basis?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"If we sell referral measurement to clients as a separate paid service, does it change how we describe and invoice it, including for clients in other EU countries?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Date","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy), consolidated, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:02002L0058-20091219","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:02002L0058-20091219"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Article 5(3), both sentences","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 19 December 2009","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama (ZEK), NN 76/2022, https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2022_07_76_1116.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 43(4)","u":""},{"t":"In force 12 July 2022","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o kibernetičkoj sigurnosti, NN 14/2024, https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_02_14_254.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 115(1), third indent, Article 116","u":""},{"t":"From 15 February 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK amendment, NN 45/2026, https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_04_45_523.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Articles 1 to 38, no change to Article 43(4)","u":""},{"t":"In force 7 May 2026","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 2, 4(1), 4(7), 4(8), 5, 6(1), 7, 12(1), 13, 25, 26, 28, 95","u":""},{"t":"27 April 2016","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU C-673/17 Planet49, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62017CJ0673","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62017CJ0673"},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 68 to 71, operative part point 2","u":""},{"t":"1 October 2019","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU C-621/22, ECLI:EU:C:2024:858, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62022CJ0621","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:62022CJ0621"},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 37 to 45 and 49 to 50","u":""},{"t":"Judgment of 4 October 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 on technical scope of Art. 5(3), https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2024-10/edpb_guidelines_202302_technical_scope_art_53_eprivacydirective_v2_en_0.pdf","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2024-10/edpb_guidelines_202302_technical_scope_art_53_eprivacydirective_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 4, 6, 35 to 40, 44, 52 to 56, footnotes 28 to 29","u":""},{"t":"v2.0, adopted 7 October 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Opinion 04/2012 (WP194), https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/documentation/opinion-recommendation/files/2012/wp194_en.pdf","u":"https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/documentation/opinion-recommendation/files/2012/wp194_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 WP","u":""},{"t":"Sections 4.2 to 4.3, pages 9 to 11","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 7 June 2012","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Opinion 9/2014 (WP224), https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/documentation/opinion-recommendation/files/2014/wp224_en.pdf","u":"https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/documentation/opinion-recommendation/files/2014/wp224_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 WP","u":""},{"t":"Section 6, sections 7.1 to 7.2","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 25 November 2014","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP, \"Obrada osobnih podataka putem kolačića i usklađivanje s Općom uredbom o zaštiti podataka\", https://azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/","u":"https://azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs beginning \"Ako se, međutim\", \"Banner koji sadrži samo gumb\", \"Ističemo da činjenica\", \"Sama tvrdnja\", recommendations 1 to 4","u":""},{"t":"Published 14.8.2026","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP recommendation on cookies, https://azop.hr/obrada-osobnih-podataka-kolacici/","u":"https://azop.hr/obrada-osobnih-podataka-kolacici/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"First-layer banner examples","u":""},{"t":"Updated 6 August 2024","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_202005_consent_en.pdf","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_202005_consent_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 43 to 45, 64 to 65, 104 to 108, 117","u":""},{"t":"v1.1, 4 May 2020","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2019 on Article 6(1)(b), https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines-art_6-1-b-adopted_after_public_consultation_en.pdf","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines-art_6-1-b-adopted_after_public_consultation_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 48 to 49","u":""},{"t":"v2.0, 8 October 2019","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Guidelines on transparency (WP260 rev.01), https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-09/wp260rev01_en.pdf","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-09/wp260rev01_en.pdf"},{"t":"WP29, endorsed by EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 35 to 36, annex storage-period row","u":""},{"t":"Revised and adopted 11 April 2018","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Part I paragraphs 12 to 13, 39 to 41","u":""},{"t":"v2.1, adopted 7 July 2021","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021 on Article 3 and Chapter V, https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 9 to 13","u":""},{"t":"v2.0, 14 February 2023","u":""}],[{"t":"Claim records","u":""},{"t":"This research set","u":""},{"t":"eu-helper-research/families/F-DEVICE.json, F-GDPR-BASIS.json, F-GDPR-NOTICE.json, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR.json, F-GDPR-TRANSFER.json, national/HR/N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT.json, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW.json","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-10","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Hosting and backups for a small business","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small business that runs marketing sites, client sites or a small SaaS on a managed frontend host, keeps its data in a hosted Postgres database, and is weighing a cheap EU storage box or self-hosting.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-049, Q-083, Q-085, Q-086, Q-087, Q-106, Q-107, Q-108, Q-077, Q-128, Q-144]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-10, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-11, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M02, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-02, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-06, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-07, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-13, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-14, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-16, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M02, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M03, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M04, F-GDPR-SCOPE-02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-NIS2-01, F-NIS2-02, F-NIS2-04, F-NIS2-05, F-NIS2-07, F-NIS2-11, F-NIS2-12, F-TAX-05, F-TAX-11, F-TAX-12, N-HR-AUTH-01, N-HR-AUTH-06, N-HR-AUTH-M04]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"hosting":{"title":"Hosting and backups for a small business","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each fact links to a question in questions.json. \"Unknown\" is a valid answer. It keeps the related checks visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether each site is commercial.","t":"A site that advertises paid services, takes payment, or that someone is paid to build or host, matches the commercial-use examples in common hosting terms. A purely personal page may not. (Q-049)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which plan and which data processing agreement (DPA) bind this exact account.","t":"Some public DPAs cover paid plans only. Some are opt-in and do nothing until you accept them in the account. (Q-086)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who decides the purposes for each hosting, database and backup feature.","t":"On your own sites you are usually the controller. On a client site that runs in your account, you may be the client's processor, and your host becomes your sub-processor. (Q-083)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which entities, locations and downstream providers can reach the data, including support and backups.","t":"The machine that runs your backup job sees the data too. (Q-085)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether personal data is made available to a separate entity in a third country, including remote support.","t":"(Q-106)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether a US recipient is actively certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, for the right entity and data.","t":"(Q-108)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How long backups keep data, and what starts that period.","t":"A deleted record can live on in backup rotation. (Q-077)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether you can leave each service in practice.","t":"Export, deletion at the end, and objection to sub-processor changes all depend on terms you can actually use. (Q-087)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Whether a client contract asks for EU-only hosting or security terms.","t":"Those are contract duties. They are not proof that a security law applies to you directly. (Q-128)","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How a foreign hosting invoice is taxed for you.","t":"Reverse charge can reach a small trader that is exempt from domestic VAT. (Q-144)","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"Vendor terms first: plan, DPA scope and spend controls","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"This section reports vendor terms, not law. It matters because the legal rules below assume you have a processor contract that actually covers your account. Vercel is used as the example because it is common and its terms are public. Other hosts have their own versions. Check yours.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plan terms and commercial use.","t":"Vercel's terms, section 4, say: \"You shall only use the Services under a Hobby plan for your personal or non-commercial use.\" Its fair-use guidelines (last updated 2026-09-14, \"Commercial usage\") say all commercial usage requires Pro or Enterprise. The examples include \"Any method of requesting or processing payment from visitors of the site\", \"Advertising the sale of a product or service\" and \"Receiving payment to create, update, or host the site\". Asking for donations does not count. Kind: vendor terms.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"DPA scope.","t":"Vercel's DPA (effective 2026-03-31), sections 1 and 4.1, applies to \"Customers who are on Enterprise and Pro plans.\" It does not mention Hobby. Section 4.1 also covers a customer who acts as a processor for someone else, which fits client work on a covered plan. Section 13.1 says its primary processing facilities are in the United States. Section 13.3 and Schedule 3 apply the 2021 Standard Contractual Clauses. Kind: vendor terms. Inference: a hobby team cannot rely on that public DPA, and a general GDPR page does not fill the gap. A separately agreed contract would need its own evidence.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Hobby limits.","t":"The Hobby plan page says that if you exceed usage limits, \"In most cases ... you will have to wait until 30 days have passed before you can use the feature again.\" Kind: vendor claim. Inference: a business site on a free plan carries three separate risks: the terms, the DPA scope and a pause of up to 30 days.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Paid plan cost.","t":"On 2026-11-07, Vercel Pro listed at $20 per developer seat per month, with a $20 usage credit included, billed in USD, excluding tax. Usage above the credit bills on demand. That is a base, not a ceiling. Kind: vendor claim.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Spend controls can take production offline.","t":"Vercel's Spend Management docs (last updated 2026-09-18) say:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"\"Setting a spend amount does not stop usage on its own.\" On its own it sends alerts at 50%, 75% and 100%.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"The pause action stops the production deployment of every project on the team. \"While paused, your production deployments stop serving traffic.\" Visitors get a 503. Each project must be resumed by hand, and raising the budget does not unpause them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Spend is checked every few minutes, so usage can run past the amount first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"The amount covers metered usage only, not seats or add-ons. Storage keeps billing while paused.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"A 2024 changelog is titled \"Spend Management now pauses production deployments by default.\" The current docs describe pausing as a choice to confirm. Check the real setting in your team.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Inference: alerts only means a surprise bill is possible. Pausing means every production site on the team, client sites included, can go offline at once.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Function region.","t":"New Vercel projects run functions in Washington, D.C. (iad1) by default. You can set an EU region such as fra1 in project settings or in vercel.json. Static files are served from a global CDN. Kind: vendor claim. Inference: moving functions to the EU moves that one path. It does not move the CDN, logs, analytics, support or the vendor's US primary processing.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"What a storage box is and is not","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Vendor claims from Hetzner product pages and docs, retrieved 2026-11-07. Other providers sell similar products.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What it is.","t":"Hetzner says Storage Boxes \"are designed for you to use to back up your files.\" Its storage comparison rates the box well for backups of websites, servers and databases. It marks it \"not recom.\" for storing a live database and for fast access, and says \"There is no web interface.\"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Access.","t":"File protocols only: SFTP, SCP, FTPS, Samba, WebDAV, rsync over SSH, and tools such as BorgBackup, restic and rclone. It does not speak S3. Hetzner sells S3-compatible storage as a separate product.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Location.","t":"You choose Germany or Finland.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Durability.","t":"Data sits on several disks in a RAID array, and \"The disks are on a single host server.\" Snapshots are saved on the same box. Inference: a storage box is one copy in one place. Snapshots help against accidental deletion. They do not help if you lose that host or that account.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Terms.","t":"On 2026-11-07, the 1 TB plan listed at €3.20 per month excluding VAT, with no minimum contract. The DPA is listed as \"Optional\". Inference: it is opt-in, and not in force until you accept it in the account.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What it is not.","t":"It does not run code, so it cannot host a Next.js site, a serverless function, a database or a form backend. It is not a mailbox. Buying one does not by itself mean you need one. That depends on what data you hold and how it is backed up today.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Self-hosting is a job, not a saving","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Vendor claims, retrieved 2026-11-07. Inference where marked.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Coolify needs \"2 CPU cores, 2 GB RAM, and 10 GB disk space\" before any site runs. Self-hosted Coolify is free. Its managed cloud tier still needs your own servers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Its install guide warns: \"Anyone who reaches the registration page first can become the instance admin and gain root access to your server.\"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Its scheduled database backups go to the local server or to \"an S3-compatible storage provider\". SFTP is not listed. So a storage box needs a separate restic or rclone job.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"On 2026-11-07 the smallest Hetzner Cloud server that meets that minimum listed at €5.99 per month, plus server backups from about €1.20, excluding VAT. The public plan pages showed \"This product is currently unavailable\" that day. That is a page observation, not an order check.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Inference: the list-price gap against one paid frontend seat is about $11 to $12 a month at an assumed 1.10 to 1.20 USD per EUR. You become the operator: patches, firewall, TLS, monitoring, uptime and restore tests. Sites built for one host may lose host-specific features after a move. Test each site.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Hosted Postgres backups: what the vendor does and does not cover","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Vendor claims from Supabase's \"Database backups\" docs, retrieved 2026-11-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Daily backups are listed for Pro (7 days), Team (14 days) and Enterprise (up to 30 days). The Free plan is not on that list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For free projects, the docs say: \"We recommend that free tier plan projects regularly export their data.\"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"\"Database backups do not include objects you store via the Storage API.\" Uploaded files need their own copy.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Point-in-time recovery is a paid add-on.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Inference: on a free plan, a scheduled export plus an off-site copy adds the most value for the least money. On a paid plan with no stored files, it adds less, but a tested restore still matters.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"You need a processor contract for each vendor that handles personal data","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"When a vendor processes personal data on your behalf, a contract or other binding legal act must govern it. It must be in writing, which includes electronic form. It must set out the subject, duration, nature and purpose, the data types, the people affected and your rights and duties.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The vendor acts as your processor, and the data is personal data. Assess each activity separately. Hosting, database, backup storage and the machine that runs the backup job are separate activities.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What the contract must contain.","t":"Documented instructions (including on international transfers), confidentiality, Article 32 security, lawful sub-processing, help with rights and with Articles 32 to 36, return or deletion at the end, and audit cooperation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sub-processors.","t":"They need your prior specific or general written authorisation. Under general authorisation, the processor must tell you about changes and give you a chance to object. EDPB says a web list changed without a targeted notice does not meet that.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A vendor that uses data for its own purposes may be a separate controller for that part. A general privacy notice is not the required binding agreement.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8) and 28(10) for roles. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(3), opening sentence, and 28(9) for content and written form. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(3)(a) to (d) for instructions, confidentiality, security and sub-processing. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(3)(g) for return or deletion at the end. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(2) and 28(4) for sub-processor authorisation. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, paragraph 128 and footnote 54, for flagged changes. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Service-by-service review of DPA, security annex, sub-processor list, transfer terms and exit. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15 (an inference from Article 28(1) to (4) and EDPB 07/2020).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Choosing a processor is a continuing duty","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"You may use only processors that give sufficient guarantees. Signing a DPA does not end that duty. Check the guarantees at sensible intervals.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The depth of checking depends on risk. Keep the identities of all processors in the chain available.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Obtaining every sub-processing contract is not automatic.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 28(1), with EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 paragraphs 94 to 99. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part II, paragraphs 95 to 99, 110 to 114, 125 to 127 and 130 to 145. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-10.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Opinion 22/2024, paragraphs 22 to 29, 34 to 41 and 69 to 71. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"EU location does not settle GDPR","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A server in Germany or Finland removes one path. It does not show that support access, onward transfers, the backup runner, analytics or email are inside the EU. It also does not decide whether GDPR applies to you. Equally, a US provider is not unlawful by default.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Map each flow: exporter and importer, their locations and roles, data categories, storage and remote-access routes. Match each flow to a covered mechanism and record its limits. A transfer needs all three EDPB elements: the exporter is subject to GDPR for the processing, it makes personal data available to another entity, and that importer is in a third country.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Remote access.","t":"EDPB says remote access from a third country, even by displaying data on a screen in a support situation, can be a transfer when all three elements are met. An employee of the same controller who travels is a different case from a separate foreign support company.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"An EU processor under foreign law.","t":"EDPB Example 12 covers an EU processor that is subject to a third country's law. Using it is not a transfer in itself, but you must still assess its guarantees under Article 28.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Scope.","t":"GDPR Article 3(1) covers processing in the context of an EU establishment's activities, wherever the processing happens. Server location does not settle that test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A person giving their data directly to a controller abroad is not automatically an exporter-to-importer transfer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Recommendations 01/2020, section 2.1, paragraphs 8 to 14, and EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paragraphs 9 to 13 and Examples 7 and 8.1. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20. Its exclusion reads: \"EU hosting alone does not rule out third-country support or onward transfers.\"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, version 2.0, paragraphs 9 to 13. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, version 2.0, section 2.2 and Example 12. No claim record in the pack covers section 2.2 or Example 12 directly. Read the guideline.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 3(1) and EDPB Guidelines 3/2018, version 2.1, section 1(a) and 1(b). Claim F-GDPR-SCOPE-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Chapter V applies alongside the rest of GDPR. Adequacy, safeguards and derogations are separate routes. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"US providers: the Data Privacy Framework and its status","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795 of 10 July 2023 finds adequate protection for US organisations on the Department of Commerce DPF List. It does not cover every US recipient. Check the official list for active certification, scope and the right subsidiary. Certifications renew yearly. Inactive participants cannot receive new transfers on this basis.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A DPF-covered transfer needs no Article 46 tool. You still need Article 28 processor terms with a DPF-certified processor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A US address, a vendor badge or a parent company's name is not enough. A company removed from the list must keep applying the DPF principles to data it already received, but new transfers need another ground.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Status on 2026-11-07.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"The General Court dismissed the annulment action in T-553/23, Latombe v Commission, on 3 September 2025. It assessed legality at adoption, not later US developments.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"The appeal, C-703/25 P, was lodged on 31 October 2025. CURIA showed \"Case in progress\" on 7 November 2026. An order of 4 June 2026 admitted an intervener. It did not decide the merits.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"On 31 July 2026 the EDPB asked the Commission to assess whether Trump v. Slaughter affects the decision. That letter is a monitoring request. It does not suspend or annul the decision.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EUR-Lex marks the decision in force. A dated inference is that the DPF remains available within its scope. Neither the appeal nor the letter suspends it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Decision 2023/1795, Article 1 and Annex I, Section I.3. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses (2026), Questions 3 and 3.1. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB information note (2023), Question 1, and DPF FAQ Questions 3 and 3.3. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB DPF FAQ, Question 3.3. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB DPF FAQ on removed companies. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"T-553/23, paragraphs 15, 22, 58 and 204, operative part point 1. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-06.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"C-703/25 P register and the order of 4 June 2026. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EUR-Lex status, Commission adequacy directory, COM(2024) 451 final section 5. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB letter of 31 July 2026. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Standard Contractual Clauses, when a vendor relies on them","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Decision 2021/914 offers four modules. Controller-to-processor is Module 2, processor-to-processor is Module 3. Completed Modules 2 and 3 incorporate the Article 28 requirements, so a duplicate DPA is not needed for covered processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The parties must bind themselves, complete the annexes and pick the right module. Clause 14 needs a documented assessment of the destination's laws and practices. Clause 16 needs suspension if the importer breaches or cannot comply. EDPB gives six steps: map, choose a tool, assess, add measures, complete formalities, reassess.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A link to blank Commission clauses is not a completed contract. Do not use these clauses automatically for an importer already subject to GDPR for the same processing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Decision 2021/914, Article 1(1) to (2), recital 7 and Annex. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Commission SCC questions and answers, Questions 6 to 7, 35 and 39. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-14.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Commission SCC questions and answers, Question 29. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Decision 2021/914, Annex, Clauses 14 to 16. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-15.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"EDPB Recommendations 01/2020, sections 2.1 to 2.6. Claim F-GDPR-TRANSFER-16.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Tell people about recipients, transfers and retention","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Your notice names recipients or meaningful categories, says whether data goes to a third country, and states whether an adequacy decision exists or which safeguard applies and how to get a copy. It also states how long data is kept, or the criteria.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Retention must be known per purpose and data set. \"As long as necessary\" needs enough detail to be understood.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A disclosure does not make a transfer lawful. An internal transfer map alone does not inform people.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1)(e) to (f) and 14(1)(e) to (f). Claims F-GDPR-NOTICE-03 and F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M03.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 13(2)(a), 14(2)(a) and 5(1)(e), WP260 rev.01 Annex. Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Security includes the ability to restore","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"GDPR Article 32(1) lists, where appropriate, \"the ability to restore the availability and access to personal data in a timely manner in the event of a physical or technical incident\" (point (c)), and \"a process for regularly testing, assessing and evaluating the effectiveness\" of the measures (point (d)). Article 5(1)(f) requires integrity and confidentiality. Article 5(2) makes you accountable.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Measures are appropriate to the risk, the state of the art, the cost and the nature of the processing. A small site with a contact form is not held to a bank's standard.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"None. The size of the measure scales. The duty does not vanish.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Inference.","t":"A tested restore with a written result is likely the strongest evidence a small business can keep for points (c) and (d). A scheduled dump that nobody restored is weaker evidence. An unencrypted copy on a remote box adds a confidentiality risk.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Articles 5(1)(f), 5(2) and 32(1)(b) to (d). No claim record in the pack covers Article 32 directly. Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05 covers only the duty to put Article 32 security into the processor contract.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"A lost or exposed backup can be a breach","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Accidental loss, destruction or unauthorised access to personal data is a personal data breach. A processor must tell you without undue delay after it becomes aware. You must notify the competent supervisory authority without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours, unless the breach is unlikely to risk people's rights. Document every breach.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"In Croatia the authority is AZOP (Agencija za zaštitu osobnih podataka), named by Article 4 of the GDPR implementing act, NN 42/2018. First establish that AZOP is the competent authority for your processing. AZOP's breach page is https://azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Notice to affected people under Article 34 is needed only when high risk is likely, subject to its exceptions. A notice after 72 hours needs reasons for the delay. Information can be given in phases.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Article 33(1) to (2), read with Article 28(3)(f). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-11.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018-805, Article 4. Claim N-HR-AUTH-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"AZOP breach page, heading and first paragraph, checked 2026-11-07. Claim N-HR-AUTH-06.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"GDPR Articles 33(1), 33(4) to (5) and 34(1) to (3). Claim N-HR-AUTH-M04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Retention, erasure and backups","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"When an erasure ground applies, you erase without undue delay, subject to the Article 17(3) exceptions. Your notice states retention for each data set. At the end of a processor service, you choose return or deletion, and the processor deletes existing copies unless law requires storage.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Backups are copies. How erasure applies to a record that survives in a rotating backup is not settled by any claim in this pack. Treat it as a counsel question. A common practical approach is a short, stated backup rotation, plus a rule that a restore re-applies erasures logged since the backup date. That approach is an inference, not a rule.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"A vendor cannot replace your choice with its own indefinite retention.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"GDPR Article 17(1) and (3). Claim F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07. GDPR Articles 13(2)(a), 14(2)(a) and 5(1)(e). Claim F-GDPR-NOTICE-04. GDPR Article 28(3)(g). Claim F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"NIS2 usually does not reach a small hosting customer directly","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"NIS2 covers entities of a listed type that are medium-sized or larger, plus some types regardless of size. Using cloud hosting, having a website or handling customer data is not itself the test. A micro or small enterprise generally falls below Article 2(1), after checking linked and partner enterprises and the size-independent triggers. Buying cloud hosting does not make you a cloud provider.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A covered client must manage supply-chain security. Its contract can pass security terms to you as a supplier. Those are contract duties, not proof that you are directly regulated.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"DNS service providers, domain registration services and some others are covered regardless of size. Check those separately if you offer them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Dates.","t":"Member States had to transpose NIS2 by 17 October 2024 and apply it from 18 October 2024. This module did not check Croatia's national implementation or any designation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555, Article 2(1) and Annexes I and II (F-NIS2-01), Articles 2(1) to (4) and 3 with Recommendation 2003/361/EC (F-NIS2-02), Article 6(30) and recital 33 (F-NIS2-04), Article 21(2)(d) (F-NIS2-11), the transposition dates (F-NIS2-12), Article 2(2)(a) for DNS and trust service providers regardless of size (F-NIS2-05), and Article 2(4) for domain registration services (F-NIS2-07).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"VAT on foreign hosting invoices","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Hosting is usually bought from another EU country or from outside the EU. Whether reverse charge shifts VAT to you as the customer depends on your status. Ask which country's invoice rules apply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Croatia's small-taxpayer exemption has a €60,000 domestic turnover threshold (ZPDV Article 90, as replaced by NN 152/2024). NN 152/2024, Article 16, inserts ZPDV Article 89.b. Its paragraph (2)(b) says the exemption does not apply \"u slučaju prijenosa porezne obveze na male porezne obveznike\" (in the case of a transfer of tax liability to small taxpayers). So a trader exempt from domestic VAT may still owe self-assessed VAT on a foreign supplier's service, and may not be able to deduct it. A VAT ID for cross-border services is not the same as full domestic VAT registration.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"There is no blanket reverse charge and no universal template. This module draws no conclusion about any reader's tax status.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rate.","t":"Croatia's standard rate is 25% under ZPDV Article 38. That text was not reopened for this module. Confirm it with your accountant.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sources.","t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC, Articles 196, 219a, 220 and 226 (F-TAX-05). NN 152/2024, Articles 16 to 18 and 28, inserting ZPDV Articles 89a to 89b and replacing Article 90 (F-TAX-11). Legal form and VAT status questions for the accountant (F-TAX-12). See UC-11 for invoicing.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each step is small and reversible. Do them in order. Stop when you have what you need. Most owners never reach step 11.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Write a one-page hosting inventory.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: for each site, record the host, the team or project, the plan, the function region, the database and its plan and region, any stored files, who owns each account, and whether the site is yours or a client's.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: every live domain appears once, and every row has an owner. Mark unknowns as unknown.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: the hosting headers each site returns (for example a header that names the host or a request ID with region codes). Treat region codes as hints, not proof of where functions run. It cannot see plans, teams, billing or database settings.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Check the plan for each commercial site.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: compare each site with your host's commercial-use examples. If a site advertises services, takes payment, or someone is paid to build or host it, move it to a plan that permits commercial use. Check any trial's terms and end date before relying on it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the account's billing page shows the paid plan for that team, and the project sits in that team.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing about the plan. The report raises a \"needs your answer\" item for Q-049 and Q-086.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Accept the DPA in each account, and save a copy.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: for each processor (host, database, backup storage, backup runner), find its DPA, check that it covers your plan, accept it where it is opt-in, and save the version and date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a dated PDF or screenshot of each accepted DPA sits in your records, with the plan it covers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. Acceptance happens inside accounts it never logs into.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Decide how spend controls should behave.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: choose alerts only or pause. If client sites share the team, decide whether a pause may take them offline, or move them to their own team or the client's own account.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: open the spend setting and read the action it will take. Write the choice down.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Set functions to an EU region near your database.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: set the default function region in project settings, or in vercel.json, for example \"regions\": [\"fra1\"]. Pick the region closest to your database.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: deploy, then check the function's region in the project's deployment details.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: hosting headers only. This is a latency and data-locality step. It is not a GDPR fix by itself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Decide what a backup must hold, and how much loss is acceptable.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: list the databases, stored files, client files and archives. For each, write how much data loss is acceptable (for example one day) and how fast it must come back (for example four hours). Name who owns the job.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a short table with data set, acceptable loss, restore time and owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. If your current vendor backups already meet those numbers, you may not need a new subscription.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Schedule an encrypted, off-site export of each database.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: run a nightly pg_dump in custom format, then send it encrypted to a separate provider, such as a storage box over SFTP. Use restic (it encrypts every repository) or an rclone crypt remote. Copy stored files separately, because database backups do not include them. Keep the connection string and the encryption password in your CI or secret store, never in the repository. Keep a copy of the encryption password somewhere other than the box.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Example commands, one per line:","lk":[]},{"k":"code","t":"pg_dump --format=custom --no-owner --no-privileges --file=db.dump \"$DATABASE_URL\"\nrestic -r \"$RESTIC_REPOSITORY\" backup db.dump\nrestic -r \"$RESTIC_REPOSITORY\" forget --keep-daily 7 --keep-weekly 4 --prune\nrestic -r \"$RESTIC_REPOSITORY\" check"},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Notes: the pg_dump client's major version must be the same as or newer than the server's. Your database vendor may document its own dump command for its managed schemas and roles. Follow its backup guide where it differs. Set RESTIC_REPOSITORY and RESTIC_PASSWORD from secrets. Look up your storage provider's SFTP host and port in its own docs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: restic snapshots lists a new snapshot each day, and the job's log shows success.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. An outside check never logs in or probes ports.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Test one restore, and write down the result.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: restore the latest snapshot into a fresh scratch database that no live app uses. Never restore over production for a test.","lk":[]},{"k":"code","t":"restic -r \"$RESTIC_REPOSITORY\" restore latest --target ./restore-test\npg_restore --no-owner --no-privileges --dbname=\"$SCRATCH_DATABASE_URL\" ./restore-test/db.dump\npsql \"$SCRATCH_DATABASE_URL\" -c \"select count(*) from public.your_main_table\""},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Compare row counts on your key tables with production. Point a local copy of the app at the scratch database once and load a few pages. Then delete the scratch database and the restored files.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a dated note with the snapshot date, dump size, restore time, row counts, who ran it and what failed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing. This written result can support your record for GDPR Article 32(1)(c) and (d). Whether it is enough for your risk level is a question for counsel.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Keep it running.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: look at the job log monthly. Repeat the restore test quarterly, and after any major database or schema change. Alert on a failed job.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the restore log has an entry each quarter.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Update your privacy notice from the inventory.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: list each recipient or category (host, database, backup storage, backup runner), each third-country transfer and its safeguard, and retention for each data set, including how long backups keep data.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: every row in your inventory that handles personal data appears in the notice, and nothing in the notice is gone from the inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: a privacy link on each page under \"Pages\". It cannot judge the notice's content.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"Only now, consider self-hosting.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: move only if a client contract requires every server in the EU, or if you want to run servers. Price the operator hours, not only the list fee. Plan backups to S3-compatible storage or a separate restic job. Lock the admin registration before anything else. Test each site after the move. Keep a rollback plan for each workload.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each moved site passes its own test, and a restore from the new setup works.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: the changed hosting headers after the move.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"12","b":"Plan the exit.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do: for each vendor, note how to export your data and how deletion at the end works. Cancel unused accounts and delete projects you no longer run.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the inventory has an exit line for each vendor, and no dead project remains in any account.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: dead third-party hosts that still load on a page, under \"Third parties\".","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Moving to an EU storage box makes us GDPR safe.\"","t":"A storage box holds backup files. It does not host anything, and location is one input among many (F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Our host has a DPA, so we are covered.\"","t":"Some public DPAs cover paid plans only, and some are opt-in. Check your plan and your acceptance (Q-086).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"A DPF badge on the vendor's site settles transfers.\"","t":"Check the official list for the exact entity, and keep the processor contract as well (F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"The DPF appeal means US vendors are unlawful.\"","t":"A pending appeal does not annul the decision (F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Turning on a budget prevents surprise bills.\"","t":"On its own it only alerts. The pause option can take every production site offline, client sites included.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"We have backups, the vendor does daily snapshots.\"","t":"Free plans may have none. Stored files may be excluded. Nobody knows until a restore works.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Snapshots on the box are a second copy.\"","t":"They sit on the same host. Lose the host or the account, and both go.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"The backup is encrypted, so the key can live next to it.\"","t":"A key on the same box protects nothing. A key you lose makes the backup useless.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"We tested the dump file exists.\"","t":"A file is not a restore. Restore into a scratch database and use the app against it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"The backup runner is just CI.\"","t":"It reads your database and handles the dump. It is a processor path with its own terms and location.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"Self-hosting saves money.\"","t":"The list-price gap is small. The operator hours, security and on-call duty are the real cost.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"A client asked for NIS2 terms, so NIS2 applies to us.\"","t":"It may be a contract duty only (F-NIS2-11).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"We are VAT exempt, so foreign invoices carry no VAT for us.\"","t":"Reverse charge can still reach an exempt small trader (F-TAX-11).","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work account by account. Never log in to an account on the owner's behalf, never change billing or spend settings, never restore over production, and never claim a setup is compliant.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Run the outside check (see the README) on each domain the owner names. Note the response headers that name the host.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Build hosting-inventory.md from the owner's files (project settings, vercel.json, database config, invoices). Record host, plan, region, database, stored files and owner per site. Answer Q-083 and Q-085 with source: agent_from_owner_files and cite the file. Leave Q-049 and Q-086 for the owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Set the default function region in vercel.json to the EU region nearest the database, if the owner agrees. Verify: the owner deploys a preview and reads the function region in the host's deployment details. Do not sign in for them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a scheduled backup job (for example a CI workflow) that runs pg_dump --format=custom, then restic backup, restic forget --prune and restic check. Read every secret from the CI secret store. Verify: the workflow file contains no connection string or password, and a manual run produces a new entry in restic snapshots.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a separate copy step for stored files if the project uses file storage. Verify: the restored snapshot contains the files.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a failure alert to the job. Verify: force one failure on a branch and confirm the alert arrives.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Write docs/restore.md with the exact restore commands into a scratch database. Run it once with the owner. Verify: a dated entry in docs/restore-log.md with snapshot date, size, time, row counts and result.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Draft the privacy notice lines for host, database, backup storage and backup runner (recipient, location, safeguard, retention). Ask the owner to confirm each line (Q-077, Q-106, Q-108).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] List for the owner: each DPA to accept, the spend-control choice, and any commercial site on a free plan. Do not decide these.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Leave anything marked \"needs a specialist\" for the owner.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If a site with forms or signups ran on a plan that the vendor's public DPA does not cover, what processor terms covered it, and what is the right fix?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For client sites in my account, am I the client's processor? What must my contract with the client say about sub-processors, backups and exit (Q-083, Q-087)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does any support or remote access by my host, database vendor or backup runner count as a transfer for my setup, and is each exact entity covered (Q-106 to Q-108)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How should erasure requests apply to records that remain in backup rotation, and what backup retention period can I justify (Q-077)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"What should a restore test record look like to support Article 32 for my risk level?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"If a backup is lost or exposed, is AZOP the competent authority for my processing?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do I hold a VAT ID for cross-border services, and am I in full domestic VAT registration (Q-144)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How are invoices from an EU host and from a US host treated for me? Do I self-assess VAT under reverse charge, and can I deduct it?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Are hosting fees billed in USD handled differently in my books, and at which exchange rate?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Version or date","u":""},{"t":"Claim ids","u":""}],[{"t":"GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 3(1), 4(7) to (8), 5(1)(e) to (f), 5(2), 13, 14, 17, 28(1) to (4), 28(3)(f) to (g), 28(9) to (10), 32(1), 33, 34","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-05, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-11, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M03, N-HR-AUTH-M04. Article 32 has no claim record.","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, controller and processor","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-10/EDPB_guidelines_202007_controllerprocessor_final_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 94 to 99, 110 to 114, 125 to 127, 128 and footnote 54, 130 to 145","u":""},{"t":"Final version","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-10, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M02","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Opinion 22/2024, processors and sub-processors","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2024-10/edpb_opinion_202422_relianceonprocessors-sub-processors_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 22 to 29, 34 to 41, 69 to 71","u":""},{"t":"October 2024","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-12","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, Article 3 and Chapter V","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/edpb_guidelines_05-2021_interplay_between_the_application_of_art3-chapter_v_of_the_gdpr_v2_en_0.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 9 to 13, section 2.2, Examples 7, 8.1 and 12","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0, February 2023","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20. Section 2.2 and Example 12 have no claim record.","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Recommendations 01/2020, supplementary measures","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2021-06/edpb_recommendations_202001vo.2.0_supplementarymeasurestransferstools_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Sections 2.1 to 2.6, paragraphs 8 to 14 and 69 to 73","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.0","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-16, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-20","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 3/2018, territorial scope","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/files/file1/edpb_guidelines_3_2018_territorial_scope_after_public_consultation_en_1.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Section 1(a) and 1(b)","u":""},{"t":"Version 2.1","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-SCOPE-02","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2023/1795, EU-US DPF","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/1795/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Article 1, Article 3, Annex I Section I.3","u":""},{"t":"Adopted 10 July 2023, OJ L 231, 20.9.2023","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB DPF FAQ for European businesses","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-04/edpb_dpf_faq-for-businesses_v2_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Questions 3, 3.1, 3.3","u":""},{"t":"Version 2, 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-09, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-13","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB information note on US transfers","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2023-07/edpb_informationnoteadequacydecisionus_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Question 1","u":""},{"t":"July 2023","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-11","u":""}],[{"t":"Latombe v Commission, T-553/23","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=CELEX:62023TJ0553"},{"t":"General Court","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 15, 22, 58, 204, operative part point 1","u":""},{"t":"Judgment 3 September 2025","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-06","u":""}],[{"t":"C-703/25 P case register","u":"https://juris.curia.europa.eu/juris/liste.jsf?num=C-703/25&language=en"},{"t":"Court of Justice","u":""},{"t":"Displayed status, order of 4 June 2026","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-07, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08","u":""}],[{"t":"First DPF periodic review, COM(2024) 451 final","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52024DC0451"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Section 5","u":""},{"t":"9 October 2024","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB letter on Trump v. Slaughter","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/2026-08/edpb_letter_20260731_us_supremecourt_judgment_trump_v_slaughter_en.pdf"},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Page 1, page 2 final paragraph","u":""},{"t":"31 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-M02","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission adequacy decisions directory","u":"https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/international-dimension-data-protection/adequacy-decisions_en"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"DPF entries","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-08","u":""}],[{"t":"Decision (EU) 2021/914, SCCs","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Article 1(1) to (2), recitals 7 and 9, Annex Clauses 14 to 16, Modules 2 and 3","u":""},{"t":"4 June 2021","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-13, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission SCC questions and answers","u":"https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/international-dimension-data-protection/new-standard-contractual-clauses-questions-and-answers-overview_en"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Questions 6 to 7, 29, 35, 39","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-TRANSFER-14, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-14","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Guidelines on transparency, WP260 rev.01","u":"https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-09/wp260rev01_en.pdf"},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party, endorsed by EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Annex, storage-period row","u":""},{"t":"Endorsed 25 May 2018","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-04","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018-805","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2018_05_42_805.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 4","u":""},{"t":"In force 25 May 2018","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-AUTH-01","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP breach reporting page","u":"https://azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Heading and first paragraph","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-AUTH-06","u":""}],[{"t":"NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2022/2555/oj/eng"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 2 to 3 (including 2(2)(a) and 2(4)), 6(30), 21(2)(d), 41(1), recital 33, Annexes I and II","u":""},{"t":"In force, transposition date 17 October 2024","u":""},{"t":"F-NIS2-01, F-NIS2-02, F-NIS2-04, F-NIS2-05, F-NIS2-07, F-NIS2-11, F-NIS2-12","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reco/2003/361/oj/eng"},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Annex Articles 2 to 6","u":""},{"t":"6 May 2003","u":""},{"t":"F-NIS2-02","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02006L0112-20250414"},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Articles 196, 219a, 220, 226","u":""},{"t":"Consolidated 14 April 2025","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-05","u":""}],[{"t":"ZPDV amendments, NN 152/2024","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_12_152_2508.html"},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 16 (new Article 89.b(2)(b)), Article 17 (Article 90(1)), Articles 18 and 28","u":""},{"t":"Checked 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-11, F-TAX-12","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o porezu na dodanu vrijednost, NN 73/13 and amendments","u":""},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Article 38, standard rate","u":""},{"t":"Not reopened for this module","u":""},{"t":"None. Accountant question.","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel terms","u":"https://vercel.com/legal/terms"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Section 4","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor terms, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel fair-use guidelines","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/limits/fair-use-guidelines"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"\"Commercial usage\", \"Additional resources\"","u":""},{"t":"Last updated 2026-09-14","u":""},{"t":"Vendor terms, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel DPA","u":"https://vercel.com/legal/dpa"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Sections 1, 4.1, 13.1, 13.3, Schedule 3","u":""},{"t":"Effective 2026-03-31","u":""},{"t":"Vendor terms, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel Hobby plan and pricing","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/plans/hobby"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"\"Hobby billing cycle\", \"Upgrading to Pro\", included credit","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel Spend Management and 2024 changelog","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/spend-management"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Alerts, \"Pausing projects\", exclusions","u":""},{"t":"Docs updated 2026-09-18, changelog 27 June 2024","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Vercel function region","u":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/configuring-functions/region"},{"t":"Vercel (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"\"Setting your default region\", \"Limits\"","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Hetzner Storage Box and docs","u":"https://www.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/"},{"t":"Hetzner (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Plan table, protocols, location, DPA \"Optional\", RAID and \"single host server\"","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Hetzner storage comparison","u":"https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/general/which-storage-is-right-for-me/"},{"t":"Hetzner (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Comparison table","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Hetzner Cloud cost-optimized plans","u":"https://www.hetzner.com/cloud/cost-optimized/"},{"t":"Hetzner (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Smallest plan, backup price, availability notice","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Coolify installation, database backups and pricing","u":"https://coolify.io/docs/get-started/installation"},{"t":"Coolify (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Minimum requirements, admin warning, backup destinations","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}],[{"t":"Supabase database backups","u":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/platform/backups"},{"t":"Supabase (vendor)","u":""},{"t":"Backups by plan, free-tier export advice, Storage objects excluded, PITR","u":""},{"t":"Retrieved 2026-11-07","u":""},{"t":"Vendor claim, not law","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"Gaps.","t":"No claim record in the pack covers GDPR Article 32, so the restore section cites the article text directly. That wording is quoted from the official text and was not reopened for this module. EDPB 05/2021 section 2.2 and Example 12 have no claim record. Claim F-TAX-11 covers ZPDV Articles 89a to 89b and 90 and says the exemption is not an exemption from reverse-charge duties, but the quoted Croatian wording of Article 89.b(2)(b) is not in any claim record. Read it in NN 152/2024 before relying on it. How erasure applies to backup copies is left to counsel. Croatia's NIS2 implementation and the ZPDV Article 38 rate were not reopened. Vendor pages change often, and none of them shows what your own account accepted. The DPF list could not be read directly for any vendor. The storage box setup fee was not shown. The USD figures use an assumed 1.10 to 1.20 USD per EUR range, not a dated rate. No live account, backup or restore was tested for this module.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-11","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Invoicing and VAT questions for a Croatian obrt","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A Croatian obrt or other small business that sells software, subscriptions or web services to Croatian companies, private people and perhaps foreign buyers, and that pays for foreign online tools","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-139, Q-140, Q-142, Q-143, Q-144, Q-145, Q-148, Q-149, Q-150, Q-153]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-TAX-01, F-TAX-02, F-TAX-03, F-TAX-04, F-TAX-05, F-TAX-06, F-TAX-08, F-TAX-09, F-TAX-10, F-TAX-11, F-TAX-12, F-TAX-14, F-TAX-15, F-TAX-16, F-TAX-17, F-TAX-18, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-02]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"tax":{"title":"Invoicing and VAT questions for a Croatian obrt","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Fact","u":""},{"t":"Why it matters","u":""},{"t":"Question","u":""}],[{"t":"What does each sale contain: a hosted subscription, software access, hand-built work, consulting, or a mix?","u":""},{"t":"An automated online service is an electronically supplied service for VAT. Work built by hand for each customer may not be. That decides the place of supply for consumer sales abroad.","u":""},{"t":"Q-139","u":""}],[{"t":"Is each buyer acting as a taxable business or as a consumer, and what evidence shows it?","u":""},{"t":"Business and consumer sales follow different place-of-supply rules, invoice rules and fiscalisation routes.","u":""},{"t":"Q-140","u":""}],[{"t":"Is each sale a domestic B2B transaction, a domestic consumer sale or a cross-border supply, and how does the buyer pay?","u":""},{"t":"eRačun covers defined domestic transactions only. Consumer fiscalisation depends on the payment method, and bank transfer is now included.","u":""},{"t":"Q-149","u":""}],[{"t":"Are you in the VAT register? Separately, do you hold a PDV ID number? How much domestic turnover counts toward EUR 60,000?","u":""},{"t":"Register status sets your eRačun phase and invoice wording. A PDV ID can be needed for foreign services even when you are exempt. Turnover decides whether the exemption ends.","u":""},{"t":"Q-148","u":""}],[{"t":"Are you taxed as a lump-sum (paušal) obrt or on real income, and is this your first part-year?","u":""},{"t":"The lump-sum regime, contributions, VAT and fiscalisation each have their own rules, and each can change when turnover or activity changes.","u":""},{"t":"Q-153","u":""}],[{"t":"What do your cross-border sales of qualifying digital services to EU consumers total, this year and last year?","u":""},{"t":"Above EUR 10,000, the place of supply moves to each customer's state from the time the threshold is crossed.","u":""},{"t":"Q-142","u":""}],[{"t":"Would you use OSS, register in other states, or use the EU cross-border SME exemption?","u":""},{"t":"These are separate routes with separate conditions. OSS is reporting, not an exemption.","u":""},{"t":"Q-143","u":""}],[{"t":"Which foreign online tools do you pay for, which legal entity bills you, and is that entity in the EU or outside it?","u":""},{"t":"Some foreign B2B services make you liable for Croatian VAT by reverse charge, even if your own sales are exempt.","u":""},{"t":"Q-144","u":""}],[{"t":"Is your eRačun receiving set up for 2026, and is your issuing set up for 1 January 2027?","u":""},{"t":"Non-VAT businesses already receive and fiscalise incoming eRačun in 2026.","u":""},{"t":"Q-150","u":""}],[{"t":"Which invoice rules, exemption wording, numbering and retention apply to each invoice you issue?","u":""},{"t":"One template does not fit every buyer and route.","u":""},{"t":"Q-145","u":""}]]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"1. Classify before you tax","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Establish the supplier's establishments, the customer's status and location, and the type of supply before you assign any VAT treatment. The general rules tax a B2B service where the customer is, and a B2C service where the supplier is, with exceptions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Applies to every sale. Do the analysis per sale type, not per business.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not infer a customer's country from website language, hosting location or domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC, consolidated 14 April 2025, Arts. 43 to 45. European Commission, Place of taxation, supply of services section.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"2. An obrt label does not answer the tax questions","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"The obrt form does not establish VAT status or the fiscalisation phase. Legal form, income or profit-tax treatment, any lump-sum regime, VAT identification and domestic VAT registration are separate facts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"An obrtnik is a natural person carrying on a craft activity. A legal person can also carry on craft activity.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Lump-sum income-tax eligibility and contributions were not researched here. The lump-sum limit sits in the Zakon o porezu na dohodak and the Pravilnik o paušalnom oporezivanju samostalnih djelatnosti, which this research did not read. Practitioner commentary says the lump-sum limit follows the VAT threshold. Treat that as a question, not a rule.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o obrtu, NN 143/2013, Arts. 2 and 4. Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, Arts. 2(1)(21) and (24), 38(1), 80. VAT Act amendments, NN 152/2024, Art. 17 (VAT Act Art. 90).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-12.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"3. The EUR 60,000 small-taxpayer exemption","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Croatia exempts a taxpayer whose annual domestic turnover was not more than EUR 60,000. The rule is in force from 1 January 2025.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Turnover is not profit and not money received. The accountant calculates which supplies count. A taxpayer established in another EU state faces a EUR 100,000 Union turnover ceiling and notification conditions as well.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"When it ends.","t":"The exemption ends from the time the threshold is exceeded. Exceeding it in the preceding calendar year blocks the exemption for the following year. An exempt taxpayer may not show VAT on invoices and may not deduct input VAT. A voluntary election into ordinary taxation binds for the current and the following calendar year.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"The exemption is not a general release from registration, invoicing or reverse-charge duties. New VAT Act Art. 89.b(2)(b) excludes \"prijenosa porezne obveze na male porezne obveznike u smislu članka 75. stavka 1. točaka 6. i 7.\" This research reads that as keeping reverse-charge liability under Art. 75(1) points 6 and 7 outside the exemption. Confirm that reading with your accountant. Practitioner commentary says a P-PDV form is due within 8 days after crossing the threshold. That form and deadline are commentary only, so confirm them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Later amendments.","t":"NN 52/2025, NN 151/2025, NN 32/2026 and NN 48/2026 were checked and do not change Art. 90. NN 48/2026 adds Art. 38.a on energy rates. Do not call any consolidation current unless it includes NN 48/2026 and any later act.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"VAT Act amendments, NN 152/2024, Arts. 16 to 18 and 28 (VAT Act Arts. 89.a, 89.b, 90, 90f to 90h). NN 52/2025 Art. 1. NN 151/2025 Arts. 1 to 12. NN 32/2026 Art. 1. NN 48/2026 Art. 1.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-TAX-11, F-TAX-15.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"4. Foreign services you buy: PDV ID and reverse charge","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"The 2014 rulebook text says every taxpayer, including a small taxpayer, that receives services under VAT Act Art. 17(1) from a supplier in another EU state must apply for a PDV ID number under VAT Act Art. 77(5)(d).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"It depends on each supplier's contracting entity, its invoice and any place-of-supply exception. Services from an EU supplier and from a third-country supplier follow different routes. A PDV ID for cross-border services is not the same as full domestic VAT registration. An exempt small trader can owe self-assessed VAT and still have no input deduction.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not apply 25 percent mechanically to every listed tool or payment-processor fee. A payment processor is not automatically the supplier of the service you buy.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Pravilnik o PDV-u, Art. 150(2), as replaced by NN 157/2014 Art. 28. This is the 2014 text, and the current consolidated rulebook was not read. VAT Act Art. 89.b(2)(b), inserted by NN 152/2024 Art. 16. VAT Directive Art. 196.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-TAX-05, F-TAX-11. The rulebook duty itself has no claim id yet.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"5. Return deadlines moved in 2026","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"From 1 January 2026, the filing deadlines in VAT Act Arts. 44(3), 85(6), 86(2) and 88(2) moved to \"do zadnjeg dana u tekućem mjesecu\" (by the last day of the current month). Ask your accountant which reporting period each deadline covers. That covers the PDV and PDV-S returns under Arts. 85(6) and 86(2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Applies if you file those returns. NN 151/2025 Art. 10 keeps the old rules for the last 2025 reporting period.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Also in this act.","t":"NN 151/2025 Art. 3 adds VAT Act Art. 80(2): the buyer's consent is not needed for a mandatory eRačun.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Do not move every other deadline to month-end. Only the listed articles changed.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"VAT Act amendments, NN 151/2025 (published 15 December 2025), Arts. 3 to 6, 10 and 12.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"No claim id yet. F-TAX-11 records that this act does not change Art. 90.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"6. Is it an electronically supplied service?","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"An electronically supplied service is essentially automated, involves minimal human intervention and cannot be provided without information technology.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Look at what the customer receives and how much human work each sale needs. A self-serve hosted subscription points one way. A deliverable built by hand for each customer points the other. Mixed packages need separate classification.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Email contact alone does not make a service electronic. Individually supplied professional advice and teacher-led online teaching are excluded. Do not treat all online sales as digital services.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Implementing Regulation (EU) 282/2011, consolidated 14 April 2025, Art. 7(1) and (3)(i) and (j), Annex I. VAT Directive Art. 58(1), final sentence.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"7. B2C digital services to other EU states: the EUR 10,000 rule","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"B2C telecommunications, broadcasting and electronic services are generally taxed where the customer is. Art. 59c keeps them in the supplier's state while the VAT-exclusive total of these qualifying cross-border services plus intra-EU distance sales of goods stays at or below EUR 10,000 in both the current and the preceding calendar year.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The supplier must be established, or otherwise permanently addressed or usually resident, in only one Member State. Destination treatment applies from the time the threshold is exceeded. An option for destination treatment binds for at least two calendar years.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What Porezna uprava says.","t":"Below EUR 10,000 in the prior and current calendar year, these supplies are taxed in Croatia. Above it, the place of supply moves to the customer's state, and the supplier reports within 8 days and registers for OSS or in each state. An annual report is due by 20 January when below the threshold. This page is undated and still uses kuna wording in places, so check it against the current rulebook.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"EUR 10,000 is not a worldwide VAT-free allowance. It is not available by default to a non-EU supplier.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"VAT Directive Arts. 58(1), 59c(1) to (3). Porezna uprava, PDV OSS page 4693, section 2.2.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-03. The Porezna page has no claim id yet.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"8. OSS and the cross-border SME exemption are different things","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"OSS is optional reporting of foreign VAT through one Member State. The Union scheme covers eligible intra-EU distance sales of goods and certain B2C services. The non-Union scheme covers suppliers with no EU establishment. OSS does not remove domestic returns.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"SME exemption.","t":"An EU-established business with Union turnover of at most EUR 100,000 may use another state's small-enterprise exemption, within that state's threshold. It needs prior notification to the home state and an individual EX identification number. It starts on notification of the number or confirmation of an update. Art. 288a also tests the preceding year, and the exemption ends when the Union ceiling is exceeded. Quarterly reports apply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Phases.","t":"ViDA OSS changes start on 1 January 2027. Implementing Regulation 2026/1869 Art. 2 applies from 1 January 2027 to 30 June 2028, and its Arts. 1 and 3 from 1 July 2028.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"OSS is not a tax exemption. Whether a business outside the Croatian VAT register can use OSS, or must register first, was not confirmed in this research.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"European Commission, The One Stop Shop and Register to OSS pages. VAT Directive Arts. 284(2) to (5), 284a, 284b, 288a, 358a to 359, 369a, 369b. Council Directive (EU) 2025/516, Arts. 1 to 3, 6(1) to (3), 7. Implementing Regulation (EU) 2026/1869, Arts. 1 to 4.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-TAX-04, F-TAX-14, F-TAX-06, F-TAX-17.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"9. Proof of customer location","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"For B2C electronic services, the residual location presumption normally needs two non-contradictory items of evidence listed in Art. 24f.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"A supplier whose qualifying supplies from an EU establishment stay at or below EUR 100,000 excluding VAT in the current and preceding year may rely on one item supplied by an independent party to the supply. Specific presumptions for landlines, mobile networks and decoders apply first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"This EUR 100,000 evidence simplification is not a VAT exemption, and it is separate from the EUR 10,000 threshold. The presumption can be rebutted.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Implementing Regulation (EU) 282/2011, Arts. 24b, 24d, 24f.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-18.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"10. Selling to EU businesses: reverse charge and invoice rules","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"A B2B service is generally taxed in the customer's state, and Art. 196 can shift the VAT liability to the business customer. Art. 219a decides which country's invoice rules apply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Check the customer's VAT status (a VIES check of the VAT ID is common evidence), the invoice issuer and any OSS use. Ask whether you need a PDV ID and a recapitulative statement (zbirna prijava, ZP) for these sales.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"There is no universal invoice template and no blanket reverse charge.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"VAT Directive Arts. 44, 196, 219a, 220 and 226.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-TAX-05, F-TAX-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"11. Fiscalisation Act: which transactions enter eRačun","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"eRačun covers defined domestic transactions between specified issuers and recipients. Both parties must have a Croatian seat or residence, and the supply must fall within Croatian VAT scope, including exempt supplies. A PDF alone is not a structured eRačun.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The act is NN 89/2025, item 1233, published 13 June 2025, in general force from 1 September 2025. The same issue carries the accessibility act as item 1231, so keep the item numbers apart.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Invoices to buyers in other EU states or third countries go outside the eRačun exchange, on paper or another acceptable form. No later amending Fiscalisation Act was found in bounded official searches. A practitioner tracker showed no amendments as of 28 March 2026, and an amendment bill sent to the Sabor on 30 January 2026 received a Government opinion with no enactment found.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, Arts. 2(1)(24) and (34), 38(1) and (2). Porezna uprava, eRačun page, opening definition. Porezna uprava, FAQ 8047 on issuing, receiving and fiscalising eRačun (updated 30 January 2026).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"12. eRačun phases for 2026 and 2027","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"From 1 January 2026, covered VAT-registered taxpayers issue and receive eRačun. Covered taxpayers outside the VAT register receive and fiscalise incoming eRačun in 2026. Their issuing duty under Art. 38(1) points 2 and 3 starts on 1 January 2027.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who is in point 2.","t":"Income-tax payers from independent activity and profit-tax payers who are not in the VAT register and have a seat, residence or habitual residence in Croatia.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Timing of fiscalisation.","t":"An issuer fiscalises an issued eRačun at the time of issue. A recipient fiscalises a received eRačun within five working days of receipt. The five-day period also applies to self-billing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"MIKROeRAČUN.","t":"Art. 80 delays Arts. 54 to 56, the MIKROeRAČUN issuing part, to 1 January 2027. MIKROeRAČUN does not issue or fiscalise B2C receipts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Not every non-VAT individual is a covered recipient. How a private room renter taxed on property income is treated as a recipient rests on commentary only. The unread second half of FAQ 8047 may answer it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, Arts. 2(1)(24), 38(1), 41, 47, 54 to 56, 80. Porezna uprava, Vodič kroz Fiskalizaciju 2.0, phase sections. Porezna uprava, FAQ 8047, opening questions on timing and Q21.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-09. The timing and MIKROeRAČUN points have no claim id yet.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"13. Consumer receipts: payment method matters","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"Consumer fiscalisation now includes payments to a transaction account, from 1 January 2026. Art. 3 covers payment \"gotovinom, karticama, transakcijskim računom i na ostale načine\" (cash, card, bank transfer and other methods). Porezna uprava confirms the bank-transfer extension for a lump-sum obrt too.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Statutory activity exclusions apply. Cash or card transactions already invoiced and fiscalised under Art. 15 may use the Art. 39 exception, so you do not fiscalise twice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rulebook change.","t":"NN 97/2026 (2 September 2026) amends the consumer fiscalisation rulebook, NN 153/2025. Its Art. 13 puts it in force on 1 January 2027. It is not in force yet, and it does not postpone the bank-transfer rule. Its technical content was not read in full.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Bank transfer is not a way out of fiscalisation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, Arts. 2(1)(21) and (26), 3, 4, 15, 39, 80. Porezna uprava, FAQ 8047, Q21. NN 97/2026, Art. 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-10. NN 97/2026 has no claim id yet.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"14. Advance payments and missing e-invoice addresses","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"The domestic-transaction definition includes advance payments. A yearly subscription paid in advance can therefore fall in scope. If an eRačun cannot be issued because the recipient's identifier is not in the AMS directory, Art. 40 allows a paper invoice and requires the Art. 51 e-reporting route.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"This is a narrow fallback for a missing identifier. It is not a general exemption for a failed delivery.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, Arts. 2(1)(34), 40(1) and (2), 51.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-TAX-16.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"15. What your website says about tax","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule.","t":"An online provider shows its tax number where it is a VAT payer. Displayed prices must say whether tax and other price-affecting costs are included.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The VAT-number field is conditional. The identification rule in Art. 6(1) is not limited to consumer sales. Separate consumer-law price rules can apply on top of Art. 6(2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Website disclosures do not replace invoice rules. An exempt small taxpayer may not show VAT on invoices. Your accountant confirms the exact exemption note.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, Art. 6(1) and (2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-02.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Write down your four status facts.","t":"Legal form, income-tax regime, VAT register status and PDV ID status, each as a separate line with the date your accountant confirmed it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each line names its source, such as a Porezna uprava decision or your accountant's email.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-148 and Q-153 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"List what you sell and to whom.","t":"One row per product. Mark it automated, hand-built or mixed, and list the buyer types: domestic companies and obrt, domestic private people, EU businesses, EU consumers, buyers outside the EU.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: every product on your website appears in the list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: cannot classify a supply. Answer Q-139 and Q-149 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"List the foreign tools you pay for.","t":"For each, record the billing entity, its country and whether your PDV ID is on the billing profile.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: match each row to a real invoice from that supplier.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: logs third-party scripts on your public pages. That shows some vendors, not who bills you. Answer Q-144 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Check your eRačun receiving setup for 2026.","t":"Confirm with your accountant the access point (pristupna točka), the authorised person, and who fiscalises each received eRačun within five working days.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test or real incoming eRačun shows as received and fiscalised.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-150 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Plan issuing from 1 January 2027, if you are outside the VAT register.","t":"Pick the tool that will issue eRačun to domestic business buyers. Ask whether it is MIKROeRAČUN or another solution.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: your accountant names the tool and the start date in writing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-150 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Confirm how consumer payments are fiscalised.","t":"Include bank-transfer payments. Ask which tool does it, since MIKROeRAČUN does not.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: one consumer payment of each type has a fiscalised receipt.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: logs third-party scripts, which may include a card processor, and form destinations on public pages. It cannot see receipts. Answer Q-149 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Track the two thresholds.","t":"Keep a running total of domestic turnover toward EUR 60,000, and of cross-border B2C digital sales toward EUR 10,000, for this year and last year.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: totals match your invoice records for the same dates.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-148 and Q-142 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Fill the transaction matrix with your accountant.","t":"Use the table under \"Ask a specialist\". Each cell needs the document type, the fiscalisation route, the VAT treatment and the start date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no cell is empty for a buyer type you actually sell to.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-145 yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Fix the tax line on your website.","t":"Show the VAT number only if your accountant says you must. State whether prices include VAT, or that VAT is not charged, in the words your accountant gives you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the trader page and each price carry the same wording as your invoices.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: observes whether a trader-information page exists and its language. It does not read the tax line, so check it yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Keep the records together.","t":"Orders, invoices, payment proofs, eRačun and buyer-status evidence go in one place, whatever inbox receives the order.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: pick three past orders and find every record for each in under a minute.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: not visible. Answer Q-145 yourself.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating \"under EUR 60,000\" as \"no VAT anywhere\".","t":"The exemption covers your domestic supplies. It is not a general release from reverse-charge duties on foreign services you buy. Ask your accountant which ones apply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating VAT register status and a PDV ID as one question.","t":"They are separate. You can be outside the register and still need a PDV ID.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Thinking eRačun starts only in 2027.","t":"Businesses outside the VAT register already receive and fiscalise incoming eRačun in 2026. Only issuing waits for 1 January 2027.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Reading \"five working days\" as the rule for everything.","t":"That period is for received eRačun and self-billing. An issued eRačun is fiscalised at issue.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Assuming bank transfer avoids fiscalisation.","t":"Consumer fiscalisation includes transaction-account payments from 2026.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Expecting MIKROeRAČUN to cover consumer receipts.","t":"It does not issue or fiscalise B2C receipts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sending a PDF and calling it an eRačun.","t":"A structured format is required.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sending foreign buyers an eRačun through the domestic exchange.","t":"The exchange covers domestic transactions only.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Calling every online sale a digital service.","t":"Hand-built work and individual advice may not be electronically supplied services.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating OSS as an exemption.","t":"It is a way to report foreign VAT. It does not remove domestic returns.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Moving every deadline to month-end.","t":"NN 151/2025 moved only the listed VAT Act deadlines.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Applying 25 percent to every foreign invoice.","t":"The answer depends on each supplier entity, its country and the service.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Using one buyer label for everything.","t":"The same buyer can be a business for VAT, a different category for eRačun, and a consumer under consumer law. See UC-02.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Work through these in order. Stop and ask the owner where a step needs a fact you do not have. Do not decide any tax treatment in code.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add buyerCapacity (business or private), buyerCountry, buyerTaxId and paymentMethod fields to the order form and the order record.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: create a test order and read the stored record.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] If buyerTaxId is an EU VAT number, store the VIES check result and the check date with the order. Do not block the order on a failed check without the owner's rule.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run one valid and one invalid test number and compare the stored results.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Store two items of location evidence for each EU consumer order, such as billing country and IP country.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: query recent consumer orders for any record with fewer than two items.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Read the VAT note, the VAT-number line and the invoice exemption wording from one owner-supplied config value. Do not hard-code them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: change the config in a test build and confirm the site and the invoice template both change.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Number invoices in one unbroken sequence per the owner's numbering rule. Never reuse a number.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: generate ten test invoices and check the sequence has no gaps or repeats.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a report that totals domestic turnover and cross-border B2C digital sales per calendar year, from invoice records.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: compare the report with a manual sum for one month.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Export orders, invoices, payment proofs and buyer evidence to one archive location.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: export one past order and confirm every linked record is present.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] If the site adds a checkout or a card processor, tell the owner before launch. That changes the consumer fiscalisation and consumer-law questions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run the outside check and note which payment scripts load.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Do not write tax conclusions into the site. Leave every accountant question below open.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Am I taxed as a lump-sum obrt or on real income? Am I in the VAT register? Do I hold a PDV ID number? Please answer each separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"If this is my first part-year, how do the first-year limits apply, for VAT and for the lump-sum regime?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"Which revenue counts toward the EUR 60,000 test: subscriptions, one-off projects, consulting, foreign sales?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Is the lump-sum limit the same amount, and what happens to my regime if I cross EUR 60,000 mid-year? Is a P-PDV form due, and by when?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"Would voluntary VAT registration ever pay off, given who my buyers are?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"Which of the foreign tools I pay for require a PDV ID and self-assessed Croatian VAT? Which return applies, and by which day? Does Art. 89.b(2)(b) mean my exemption does not cover reverse charge under Art. 75(1) points 6 and 7?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"","t":"Should my PDV ID be on each foreign vendor's billing profile?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"","t":"For EU business buyers, is the place of supply the customer's state with reverse charge? Do I need a zbirna prijava?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"","t":"Is each product an electronically supplied service, given how much is built by hand?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"","t":"Can a business outside the VAT register use OSS, or must it register first? Does the EU cross-border SME exemption help me?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"11","b":"","t":"Is a private host or renter in another EU state a business or a consumer for VAT?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"12","b":"","t":"Who sets up my eRačun access point and authorised person, and who fiscalises received eRačun within five working days?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"13","b":"","t":"Which tool fiscalises consumer payments by bank transfer? Will NN 97/2026 change its setup from 1 January 2027?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"14","b":"","t":"Which document does each buyer get: eRačun, consumer receipt or other invoice? How is a domestic private renter treated as an eRačun recipient?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"15","b":"","t":"How should I record each buyer's status at the point of sale? Is an OIB or AMS directory check enough?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"16","b":"","t":"What must my invoice state as a non-VAT obrt? Which exemption note is required? Which numbering, operator mark and business-premises rules apply?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"17","b":"","t":"How long must I keep invoices, fiscal records and eRačun? Does storage in MIKROeRAČUN satisfy that?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"18","b":"","t":"For a yearly subscription, when do I invoice: at signup, at renewal, or prorated? Does an advance payment change it?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Transaction matrix to fill with your accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"The cells are empty on purpose. Each needs the document type, the fiscalisation route, the VAT treatment and the start date.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Buyer","u":""},{"t":"Bank transfer","u":""},{"t":"Card or processor","u":""},{"t":"Cash","u":""}],[{"t":"Domestic company or obrt","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""}],[{"t":"Domestic private renter","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""}],[{"t":"Domestic consumer","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""}],[{"t":"EU business","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""}],[{"t":"EU private renter or consumer","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""}],[{"t":"Buyer outside the EU","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""},{"t":"","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"Counsel","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Is a private renter who buys from me a consumer under ZZP Art. 4 point 21? This is a consumer-law question, separate from the VAT answer. See UC-02.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Checked","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, item 1233","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_06_89_1233.html"},{"t":"Arts. 2(1)(21), (24), (26) and (34), 3, 4, 15, 38 to 41, 47, 51, 54 to 56, 80","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Porezna uprava, eRačun","u":"https://porezna.gov.hr/fiskalizacija/bezgotovinski-racuni/eracun"},{"t":"Opening definition and phase paragraphs, \"Kako se pripremiti\" sections 1 and 2","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Porezna uprava, Vodič kroz Fiskalizaciju 2.0","u":"https://porezna-uprava.gov.hr/hr/vodic-kroz-fiskalizaciju-2-0/8149"},{"t":"Phases for VAT and non-VAT taxpayers, MIKROeRAČUN section","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Porezna uprava, FAQ 8047, updated 30 January 2026","u":"https://porezna-uprava.gov.hr/hr/izdavanje-i-primanje-eracuna-i-fiskalizacija-eracuna-azurirano-30-01-2026/8047"},{"t":"Opening questions on fiscalisation timing, Q21, Q22, \"Slijednost računa\" Q1. First half read.","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"NN 97/2026, item 1181","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_09_97_1181.html"},{"t":"Amends rulebook NN 153/2025, Art. 13 commencement","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Act amendments, NN 152/2024","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2024_12_152_2508.html"},{"t":"Arts. 16 to 18 and 28 (VAT Act Arts. 89.a, 89.b, 90, 90f to 90h)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Act amendment, NN 52/2025","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_03_52_673.html"},{"t":"Art. 1","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Act amendments, NN 151/2025","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2025_12_151_2262.html"},{"t":"Arts. 3 to 6, 10, 12","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Act amendment, NN 32/2026","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2026_03_32_377.html"},{"t":"Art. 1","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Act supplement, NN 48/2026","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/full/2026_05_48_578.html"},{"t":"Art. 1 (new Art. 38.a)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT rulebook amendment, NN 157/2014","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2014_12_157_2978.html"},{"t":"Art. 28, replacing rulebook Art. 150","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Porezna uprava, PDV OSS page 4693","u":"https://porezna-uprava.gov.hr/hr/pdvoss/4693"},{"t":"Section 2.2, EUR 10,000 rule, annual report by 20 January. Undated.","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o obrtu, NN 143/2013","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2013_12_143_3065.html"},{"t":"Arts. 2 and 4","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, item 2504","u":"https://narodne-novine.nn.hr/clanci/sluzbeni/2003_10_173_2504.html"},{"t":"Art. 6(1) and (2)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC, consolidated 14 April 2025","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02006L0112-20250414"},{"t":"Arts. 43 to 45, 58, 59c, 196, 219a, 220, 226, 284 to 284b, 288a, 358a to 359, 369a, 369b","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Implementing Regulation (EU) 282/2011, consolidated 14 April 2025","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:02011R0282-20250414"},{"t":"Arts. 7, 24b, 24d, 24f, Annex I","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"European Commission, Place of taxation","u":"https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/taxation/vat/vat-directive/place-taxation_en"},{"t":"Supply of services section","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"European Commission, The One Stop Shop and Register to OSS","u":"https://vat-one-stop-shop.ec.europa.eu/one-stop-shop_en"},{"t":"Background, who can register, scheme tables","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Council Directive (EU) 2025/516","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2025/516/oj/eng"},{"t":"Arts. 1 to 3, 6(1) to (3), 7","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2026/1869","u":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2026/1869/oj"},{"t":"Arts. 1 to 4","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Practitioner commentary (TEB, RRIF, fiskai.hr)","u":""},{"t":"P-PDV after crossing the threshold, renters as eRačun recipients, Fiscalisation Act amendment tracker","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07, commentary only","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Gaps: no current consolidated VAT Act or VAT rulebook was read, and the rulebook Art. 150 text is the 2014 version. The lump-sum limit and its legal basis were not read. Whether a business outside the VAT register can use OSS is not confirmed. The second half of FAQ 8047 is unread. NN 97/2026 was read only for its base act and commencement. Retention periods for invoices and eRačun were not checked. The Porezna OSS page is undated and keeps kuna wording.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-12","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Quizzes, leaderboards and waitlists that store names or emails","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small business in Croatia that runs a browser quiz, a game with a leaderboard, or a launch waitlist, and keeps names, scores or email addresses in the visitor's browser or in a hosted database.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-027, Q-028, Q-029, Q-031, Q-035, Q-075, Q-077, Q-213, Q-214, Q-129]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-02, F-DEVICE-03, F-DEVICE-06, F-DEVICE-07, F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-12, F-DEVICE-13, F-DEVICE-14, F-DEVICE-M01, F-DEVICE-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-07, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-01, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-08, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-10, F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-05, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-NOTICE-M03, F-GDPR-BASIS-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-03, F-GDPR-BASIS-05, F-GDPR-BASIS-06, F-GDPR-BASIS-08, F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-04, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-07, F-EMAIL-08, F-EMAIL-10, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-M04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04, F-DSA-02, F-DSA-04, F-DSA-08, F-SECTOR-01, F-SECTOR-02, F-SECTOR-05, N-HR-AUTH-01]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"storage":{"title":"Quizzes, leaderboards and waitlists that store names or emails","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Does any code write to or read from the browser's storage, including short-lived memory?","t":"(Q-027). localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB and cookies all count. Storage duration and medium set no minimum threshold.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What does each stored key actually hold and do?","t":"(Q-028). List every key, what it holds, who reads it, and when it is cleared. \"Quiz progress\" and \"a copy of the typed email\" get different answers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Does a result computed in the browser leave the device?","t":"(Q-029). A score or quiz result that stays on the device is local use. The same result sent to an analytics tag or to your database can be access, and needs its own assessment.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Which function did the visitor ask for, and does each key serve only that function?","t":"(Q-031). A key that keeps the current question number serves the quiz. A key that counts plays for your dashboard serves you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Is the leaderboard only on this device, or shared and public?","t":"(Q-035). A local-only scoreboard publishes nothing. A shared leaderboard shows names to everyone, which brings in publication, notice and takedown questions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Who receives the data, and from which countries can they access it?","t":"(Q-075). This includes the hosted database, its sub-processors and backups, the email sending tool and any analytics vendor.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How long do you keep each data set, and what starts the clock?","t":"(Q-077). Leaderboard entries, waitlist addresses, browser keys and the suppression record each need their own period. localStorage never expires by itself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Is each email a requested service message, promotion, or a mix?","t":"(Q-213). \"Here is your result\" can be a service message. \"We have launched, here is the offer\" is promotion.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Do you have valid consent before the first promotional email?","t":"(Q-214). For a free quiz or waitlist, the default answer is usually consent, because there is usually no sale.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Is the quiz offered directly to children, and is consent your basis?","t":"(Q-129). If both are true, GDPR Art. 8 age rules apply.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"1. Browser storage is device storage","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"Storing information on a user's device, or reading information already stored there, needs consent after clear and complete information, especially about purposes. In Croatia this is ZEK Art. 43(4). At EU level it is ePrivacy Directive Art. 5(3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"The rule covers any information, personal or not. Storage and access are separate operations, and either one is enough. Storage duration and medium set no minimum threshold.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How it applies to localStorage [Inference, from guidance].","t":"Assess a localStorage write under the same storage and access test as a cookie. EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 para. 44 says use wholly inside the device is not \"gaining access\" while the data stays there. That paragraph concerns access only. It does not remove the storage operation. Assess the write, the local use and any later disclosure separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Current text.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022 took effect on 12 July 2022. NN 14/2024 (in force 15 February 2024) repealed Art. 41. NN 45/2026 took effect on 7 May 2026. The checked chain leaves Art. 43(4) unchanged.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Art. 43(4), first sentence. Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 5(3), first sentence. CJEU C-673/17 Planet49, paras. 68-71 and operative part point 2. EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 v2.0, adopted 7 October 2024, paras. 6, 35-39, 44 and 52-53. NN 14/2024, Arts. 115(1) and 116. NN 45/2026, Art. 38.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-01, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-03, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-04, F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-03, F-DEVICE-06, F-DEVICE-07, F-DEVICE-M01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"2. The strictly necessary exemption, key by key","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"No consent is needed for storage or access that is strictly necessary to provide a service the user expressly requested. A second exemption covers access used only to transmit a communication.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions [Guidance].","t":"Necessity is judged from the function the user asked for, not from the value the operator places on the data. WP29 gives conditional examples, including user input and user-selected interface settings. Each example has purpose and duration limits.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions [Guidance].","t":"First-party analytics are not strictly necessary merely because operators value them. No general Croatian analytics exemption was found in the checked sources.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Applied to quizzes [Inference].","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Likely to fit: the current answers and question number while a quiz is in progress, and a setting the player chose, such as sound off.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Unlikely to fit: counters, flags or history that only feed your totals and statistics, and a copy of an email address after the server already holds it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Depends on design: remembering the player's display name. An explicit \"remember my name on this device\" toggle can make prefilling a function the player asked for. Storing a typed name without asking is weaker.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Duration matters. A key that lives forever is harder to justify than state cleared at the end of the session. Storing a timestamp and purging old keys is one way to set a limit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK Art. 43(4), second sentence. Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 5(3), second sentence. WP29 Opinion 04/2012 (WP194), sections 2, 3.1-3.7, 4.2-4.3 and 5. EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paras. 44 and 52-56. AZOP, \"Obrada osobnih podataka putem kolačića\", published 14.8.2026, paragraph beginning \"Ako se, međutim\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-02, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-07, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M03, F-DEVICE-02, F-DEVICE-12, F-DEVICE-13, F-DEVICE-10.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"3. Necessary keys still need information, other keys stay off until consent","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Guidance].","t":"AZOP's 2026 guidance says a site that uses only technically necessary storage does not need a banner asking visitors to accept. It still needs clear information about that storage. Non-essential items must stay inactive until valid consent. Preselected choices, continued browsing and silence are not consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Explain the controller, purposes, data, recipients, storage duration and the withdrawal route before you switch on anything that needs consent. Keep separate purposes as separate choices. Your policy must match what the code really does.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Withdrawal [Law and Guidance].","t":"Withdrawal must be as easy as giving consent. After withdrawal, stop future non-essential reads, writes and requests, and test that they stop. Rejecting must not block the basic quiz.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"AZOP, published 14.8.2026, paragraphs beginning \"Ako internetska stranica koristi isključivo tehnički nužne kolačiće\", \"Ako se, međutim\", \"Nužni kolačići\", \"Ističemo da činjenica\" and \"Sama tvrdnja\". GDPR Art. 7(3). EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent, paras. 43-45, 64-65, 114 and 117.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M02, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-01, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-09, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-10.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"4. Quiz results sent to analytics or a database","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Guidance].","t":"When a result computed on the device is made available outside it, the access rule applies to that disclosure (EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paras. 52-53). \"Cookieless\" is not a legal conclusion.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"GDPR is a separate test [Inference].","t":"If the result or event is personal data, it also needs a GDPR Art. 6 basis. A device-access exemption does not settle that, and a legitimate-interest assessment does not replace a device consent that is required.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Applied to quizzes [Inference].","t":"Sending a quiz result with a waitlist signup or an analytics event links that result to the person. Ask whether you need it. If not, drop it. For analytics tags in general, see UC-06.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paras. 4, 40, 44 and 52-55. GDPR Arts. 2, 4(1), 5, 6(1) and 95. EDPB Guidelines 2/2019, paras. 48-49, printed p. 14.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-DEVICE-M01, F-DEVICE-10, F-DEVICE-M03, F-GDPR-BASIS-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"5. Notice where the name or email is typed","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"When you collect data directly, give the GDPR Art. 13 information at that moment. That covers who you are and how to reach you, each purpose and basis, recipients or categories, any third-country transfer and its safeguard, retention or the criteria for it, and the rights, including withdrawal and the right to complain. Say which fields are required and what happens if the person leaves them out.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"GDPR applies to your processing. In Croatia the supervisory authority for complaints is AZOP.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How to present it [Guidance].","t":"Put a short layer next to the field, with a direct link to the full notice. For a leaderboard, the short layer says the name is shown publicly and how to remove it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Art. 13(4) removes the duty only where and insofar as the person already has the information.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 13(1)(a)-(f), 13(2)(a)-(e), 13(3), 13(4). WP260 rev.01, paras. 35-36, printed p. 19, and its Annex, storage-period row, printed pp. 38-39, endorsed by EDPB Endorsement 1/2018, Item 2. Croatian GDPR implementing act, NN 42/2018, Art. 4.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-02, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-05, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, N-HR-AUTH-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"6. Basis for the quiz and the leaderboard entry","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law and Guidance].","t":"Each purpose needs its own basis. Art. 6(1)(b) can cover data objectively needed to perform a contract with the person, or to take steps they ask for before one. Where that does not fit, Art. 6(1)(f) may fit, but only with a recorded legitimate purpose, necessity and balancing result.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions [Inference].","t":"Showing a chosen nickname on a public leaderboard is part of the feature the player asked for, if they enter it to join the board. Adding the same person to a mailing list is a different purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Making the quiz or the result depend on a consent that is not needed for it weighs against free consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 4(11), 6(1)(b), 6(1)(f), 7(4), Recital 32. EDPB Guidelines 2/2019, paras. 22-30 and 45-47, printed pp. 8-9 and 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-BASIS-02, F-GDPR-BASIS-03, F-GDPR-BASIS-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"7. The waitlist email is usually marketing","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"ZEK Art. 50(1) requires prior consent for email direct promotion and sales. The EU starting rule for natural persons is the same.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Art. 50(2) lets a trader market its own similar products to consumers whose addresses it obtained in a sale. A free quiz or a waitlist is not a sale on its face. The Inteligo case treated one specific free account, tied to paid content, as a sale context. That does not make every free registration qualify. The Croatian text speaks of consumers, so it does not automatically cover professional individuals.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Art. 50(4) removes paragraphs 1 and 2 for legal persons. Quiz players and waitlist signups are usually individuals.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Consent conditions [Law].","t":"Consent must be freely given, specific, informed, unambiguous and demonstrable. Withdrawal must be as easy as giving it. Record who chose what, when, and the wording shown. Do not collect extra identifying data only to prove consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Every message [Law].","t":"Show the sender's identity and a valid, free stop address. By the first message, state the right to object to marketing clearly and separately from other information. An objection ends marketing use, with no override test.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Evidence and suppression [Inference].","t":"Double opt-in can support consent evidence. It is not a universal legal requirement. A minimal suppression record can stop a refused address from coming back. Give it a purpose, access limits and a review period, and never reuse it for marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Current text.","t":"NN 14/2024 and NN 45/2026 leave Art. 50 unchanged.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK NN 76/2022, Art. 50(1)-(4). Directive 2002/58/EC, Art. 13(1), (2), (4) and (5). CJEU C-654/23 Inteligo Media, paras. 38-39, 43-48 and 53-63. GDPR Arts. 4(11), 5(1), 7(1)-(4), 21(2)-(4). EDPB Guidelines 05/2020, paras. 104-108.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-03, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-02, F-EMAIL-01, F-EMAIL-04, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, F-EMAIL-07, F-EMAIL-08, F-EMAIL-10, F-GDPR-NOTICE-M03, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-M01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"8. The hosted database is your processor","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"You decide the purposes and means, so you are the controller. A hosted database that stores entries for you is usually your processor. Processing must rest on a written contract or other binding legal act with the Art. 28(3) content.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Transfers [Law and Guidance].","t":"A transfer exists when data you control are made available to a separate entity in a third country. The EU-US Data Privacy Framework covers only organisations on the DPF list, not every US recipient.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"How to check [Guidance].","t":"Review each service on its own. Match the DPA, security annex, sub-processor list, transfer terms and exit process to your actual data flows.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 4(7), 4(8), 28(1)-(4), 28(9), 28(10). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, Part II, paras. 112-114 and 143-145. EDPB Guidelines 05/2021, paras. 9-13. Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795, Art. 1 and Annex I, Section I.3.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-01, F-GDPR-TRANSFER-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"9. Public leaderboards","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Erasure [Law].","t":"Erase without undue delay when an Art. 17(1) ground applies, subject to the Art. 17(3) exceptions. Grounds include data that are no longer needed, consent withdrawn with no other basis, and a valid objection. If you made the data public and must erase them, take reasonable steps to tell other controllers who copied them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Retention [Law].","t":"Set a period, or clear criteria, for leaderboard entries. \"Forever\" needs a reason.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Platform rules may apply [Law, conditions unresolved].","t":"Hosting under the Digital Services Act means storing information supplied by and at the request of a user. A hosting service that also shows that information to the public can be an online platform, unless the public feature is minor and purely ancillary under strict conditions. A nickname box on a leaderboard may or may not be hosting in this sense. Hosting providers have baseline duties such as contact points and clear terms. Treat this as a question, not a conclusion.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 5(1)(e), 13(2)(a), 17(1)-(3). Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 (DSA), Arts. 3(g)(iii), 3(i), 3(k), 11-14, recital 13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-M04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-DSA-02, F-DSA-04, F-DSA-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"10. Children","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Law].","t":"GDPR Art. 8 applies where an information society service is offered directly to a child and processing relies on consent. The EU default age is 16, and national law may lower it to no less than 13. Below that age, a holder of parental responsibility gives or authorises consent, and you must make reasonable efforts to verify it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Conditions.","t":"Both conditions must hold. A cross-border service cannot always rely on one country's age rule.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Exceptions.","t":"Art. 8 does not ban processing under-16 data on other bases. Children still get particular protection, and swapping consent for an invalid contract or legitimate-interest claim is not a workaround.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Gap.","t":"The checked sources do not establish the Croatian Art. 8 age. Ask counsel.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Arts. 5, 6, 8(1)-(3), 12(1), recital 38. EDPB Guidelines 05/2020, paras. 125-127 and 131.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-SECTOR-01, F-SECTOR-02, F-SECTOR-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"11. Withdrawal and deletion","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rule [Guidance].","t":"When consent is withdrawn, stop the processing that relied on it. If no other basis justifies keeping the data, delete it. Earlier lawful processing stays lawful. Do not switch to another basis afterwards to rescue invalid consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2020, paras. 117-123. GDPR Arts. 7(3), 17(1)(b), 17(3).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW-08, F-GDPR-BASIS-06.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"List every browser key and every network call the quiz makes.","t":"Play the quiz, join the leaderboard and sign up for the waitlist in a fresh browser profile. Write down each storage key, what it holds, when it is written, and every request that leaves the page. For each item, record the requested function, retention, recipients and the reason for any exemption, then test again before and after each consent choice (F-DEVICE-14).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: open developer tools, Application tab, and compare the key list with your notes. Then repeat in a new profile and check nothing is missing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: cookies, localStorage and sessionStorage at first load, after Reject and after Accept, then after withdrawal and reload, plus third-party requests in the network log. It never submits forms or plays the quiz, so it cannot see keys written after a click or a submit. A signup sent through an SDK call may show no form destination in the page. Those items show as \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Stop writing the email address to the browser.","t":"If the server already stores the signup, the local copy is unlikely to be needed for the requested service.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: submit a test signup, then search localStorage for @. No key should contain an address.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: an email-shaped value in storage only if it was written at page load. A write on submit is invisible to it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Delete keys that only feed your statistics.","t":"Remove counters, flags and history kept only for your numbers, unless they are part of a feature the player chose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: finish a quiz in a fresh profile, then list keys. Only game state and player-chosen settings remain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: keys present at first load in each consent state.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Give the remaining keys a limit.","t":"Keep in-progress state in sessionStorage, or store a timestamp and purge old keys. Put \"remember my name on this device\" behind an explicit toggle.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: close and reopen the browser and check that session keys are gone. Set the clock forward past your limit and check that old keys are purged.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: which storage area holds each key. It cannot see expiry logic.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Add the notice where people type.","t":"One line next to the name field: what is shown publicly, for how long, and how to remove it. One line next to the waitlist field: what you will send, who sends it, and a link to the full notice. Add one line to the notice about the necessary browser keys.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: read the form on a phone screen without scrolling away from the field.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: under \"Forms\", whether notice text sits next to each form, and under \"Pages\", whether a privacy link exists. It cannot judge whether the text is accurate.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Make the waitlist opt-in separate and specific.","t":"One unticked box, one purpose, for example \"Email me when the product launches. Nothing else. Unsubscribe any time.\" Never make the quiz result depend on giving an email for marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: complete the quiz without ticking anything and confirm you still see the result.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: whether marketing consent is a separate unticked box. It cannot see what happens after submit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Record consent and honour stops.","t":"Store the choice, the time and the wording version. Put the sender name and a working unsubscribe in every email, and state the right to object in the first one. Keep a minimal suppression record with a review date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: subscribe and unsubscribe with a test address and check the database row and the suppression record.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing here. This is \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Drop quiz results from analytics and signup payloads","t":"unless you have assessed why you need them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: in the network tab, inspect the signup and analytics requests for result values.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: analytics requests and their timing. It cannot see a request fired only after interaction.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Sign the processor terms and record the region.","t":"Accept the hosted database's DPA for your plan. Note where data and backups sit and which transfer route applies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: keep a copy of the accepted DPA version and the region setting.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: the database host in the network log, if it is called at page load. The vendor register marks role, DPA and region as unknown until you answer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Set retention and a takedown route for the leaderboard.","t":"Decide how long entries stay, add a removal contact, and test a removal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: remove a test entry and confirm it is gone from the public board and the database.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check shows: nothing here. This is \"needs your answer\".","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"\"No cookies\" is not \"no consent needed\".","t":"localStorage is storage too. The rule covers any information on the device, not only cookies.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Para. 44 does not clear a write.","t":"Local-only use is not access while it stays local, but writing the key is still storage.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Keeping a second copy \"just in case\".","t":"A local copy of an email that the server already holds is unlikely to be needed for the service.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Necessary keys left out of the notice.","t":"No banner is needed for them, but the notice must still explain them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Result gating.","t":"\"Enter your email to see your result\" ties the quiz to marketing. Show the result first, then ask separately.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"One box for two purposes.","t":"\"Updates and news\" bundles purposes. Each purpose gets its own choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating a waitlist as a customer list.","t":"A free signup is usually not a sale, so the customer exception usually does not apply.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Real names on a public board by default.","t":"Ask for a nickname, say it is public, and let people remove it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Missing that the result travels.","t":"A quiz result attached to an analytics event or a signup links the result to the person.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Trusting the outside check alone.","t":"It does not play the quiz or submit forms. What happens after a click needs your own test.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Grep the codebase for localStorage, sessionStorage, indexedDB and document.cookie. List each key with its purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the list matches what developer tools show after a full play-through in a fresh profile.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove any write of an email address to browser storage.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: after a test signup, no storage value matches /@/.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Remove or gate keys used only for counts or stats. Gate means: do not write until consent is given, and stop writing after withdrawal.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: in a fresh profile with no choice made, those keys are absent. After Reject, still absent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Move in-progress quiz state to sessionStorage, or add a timestamp and a purge on load.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a key older than the limit is deleted on the next page load.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a \"remember my name on this device\" toggle, off by default, before storing a display name.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: with the toggle off, no name key exists after play.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add notice text next to the leaderboard name field and the waitlist field, with a link to the privacy page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the text is in the DOM inside or directly beside each form element.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Make the waitlist checkbox unticked, single-purpose and not required to see the result.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the result renders with the box unticked. The input has no checked attribute.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Store consent records: choice, timestamp, wording version. Do not add extra IP or device fields only for proof.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a test signup creates one row with those three fields.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Strip quiz results from analytics events and signup payloads unless the owner confirms a reason.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: inspect request bodies in the network log.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Add a delete path for leaderboard entries and waitlist addresses.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: delete a test entry and confirm it is gone from the public view and the table.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Repeat the outside check and attach your notes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no unexplained storage keys at first load in any consent state.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel or a privacy professional:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"Which of our browser keys fit the ZEK Art. 43(4) \"strictly necessary\" exemption, given the player's requested function and how long each key lives?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"","t":"Does remembering a display name behind an opt-in toggle count as a function the user expressly requested?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"","t":"What is the Croatian age for a child's own consent under GDPR Art. 8, and does our quiz count as offered directly to children?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"","t":"Does a public leaderboard where users type their own nickname make us a hosting service under the DSA, and does the ancillary-feature exclusion apply?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"","t":"Can a launch announcement to a waitlist ever fall under ZEK Art. 50(2), or is prior consent under Art. 50(1) always needed for a free signup?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"","t":"Is our hosted database's transfer route valid for our plan and region, and is the accepted DPA binding for our account?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant:","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"","t":"If the quiz or waitlist promotes a paid product, does that change how the activity is classified for our business form and invoicing? (This module does not cover tax. See the tax family.)","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Issuer","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Checked","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama (ZEK), NN 76/2022","u":""},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 43(4), Art. 50(1)-(4), Art. 187","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Cybersecurity Act, NN 14/2024","u":""},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 115(1), third indent, Art. 116","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"ZEK amendment, NN 45/2026","u":""},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 1-38, especially 10-11 and 38","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o provedbi Opće uredbe o zaštiti podataka, NN 42/2018","u":""},{"t":"Narodne novine","u":""},{"t":"Art. 4(1)-(3)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy), consolidated 19 December 2009","u":""},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Art. 5(3), Art. 13(1), (2), (4), (5)","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)","u":""},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 4(11), 5, 6, 7, 8, 12, 13, 17, 21, 28","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 (DSA)","u":""},{"t":"EU","u":""},{"t":"Arts. 3(g), 3(i), 3(k), 11-14, recital 13","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/1795","u":""},{"t":"European Commission","u":""},{"t":"Art. 1, Annex I, Section I.3","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU C-673/17 Planet49","u":""},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 52-71, operative part points 1-3","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU C-654/23 Inteligo Media","u":""},{"t":"CJEU","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 38-69, operative points 1-2","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 on the technical scope of Art. 5(3), v2.0, adopted 7 October 2024","u":""},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 4, 6, 35-40, 44, 52-56","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2020 on consent","u":""},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 43-45, 64-65, 104-108, 114-123, 125-131","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2019 on Art. 6(1)(b)","u":""},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 22-30, 45-49","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":""},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Part II, paras. 112-114, 143-145","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 05/2021 on transfers","u":""},{"t":"EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 9-13","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Opinion 04/2012 (WP194) on cookie consent exemption","u":""},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party","u":""},{"t":"Sections 2, 3.1-3.7, 4.2-4.3, 5","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Guidelines on transparency (WP260 rev.01)","u":""},{"t":"Article 29 Working Party, endorsed by EDPB","u":""},{"t":"Paras. 35-36, Annex storage-period row","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP, \"Obrada osobnih podataka putem kolačića i usklađivanje s Općom uredbom o zaštiti podataka\", azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/","u":"https://azop.hr/kolacici-gdpr/"},{"t":"AZOP","u":""},{"t":"Published 14.8.2026, paragraphs cited in rule 3","u":""},{"t":"2026-11-07","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Claim records: research/families/F-DEVICE.json, F-GDPR-NOTICE.json, F-GDPR-BASIS.json, F-EMAIL.json, F-GDPR-RIGHTS.json, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR.json, F-GDPR-TRANSFER.json, and research/national/HR/N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT.json, N-HR-COOKIE-WITHDRAW.json, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL.json, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER.json, N-HR-AUTH.json. The F-DSA and F-SECTOR claims come from the wider EU research set and are not yet copied into the kit. Every claim is draft and not legally reviewed.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-13","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Too many sites and products, sorted into keep, merge, park or shut down","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A solo studio or small business in Croatia with more websites, domains and side products than one person can maintain. Some earn money, some are free, and some are half-forgotten.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-008, Q-014, Q-016, Q-058, Q-059, Q-060, Q-062, Q-070, Q-071, Q-073, Q-074, Q-075, Q-077, Q-080, Q-083, Q-086, Q-087, Q-091, Q-092, Q-094, Q-103, Q-145, Q-153, Q-161, Q-178, Q-181, Q-189, Q-216, Q-222]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-BASIS-M02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-08, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-08, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, F-CONSUMER-07, F-CONSUMER-11, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-04, F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-13, F-DEVICE-14, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, F-ECOMMERCE-02, F-TAX-05]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"sort":{"title":"Too many sites and products, sorted into keep, merge, park or shut down","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"#","u":""},{"t":"Fact","u":""},{"t":"Why it changes the answer","u":""},{"t":"Question id","u":""}],[{"t":"1","u":""},{"t":"Money in from each site or product over the last 12 months","u":""},{"t":"Separates keep from park or shut down","u":""},{"t":"Business fact, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"2","u":""},{"t":"Hours per month you spend keeping it running","u":""},{"t":"A site that earns little but costs hours is a merge or shut-down candidate","u":""},{"t":"Business fact, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"3","u":""},{"t":"Active users, and paying customers with time left on a plan","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether shutting down needs notice, an export window and a refund plan","u":""},{"t":"Q-014, Q-016","u":""}],[{"t":"4","u":""},{"t":"Whether those customers are consumers or businesses","u":""},{"t":"Consumer law protects consumers. Business contracts follow their terms","u":""},{"t":"Q-008, Q-161","u":""}],[{"t":"5","u":""},{"t":"What data each site holds, from whom, through which tools","u":""},{"t":"Decides what to delete, return or keep","u":""},{"t":"Q-073, Q-091","u":""}],[{"t":"6","u":""},{"t":"Why you use each data set and on which basis","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether the merged site may reuse it","u":""},{"t":"Q-074","u":""}],[{"t":"7","u":""},{"t":"How long you keep each data set, and which law makes you keep some of it","u":""},{"t":"Decides what survives a shutdown","u":""},{"t":"Q-077, Q-070","u":""}],[{"t":"8","u":""},{"t":"Which vendors process data for each site, from which countries, and whether you can leave them in practice","u":""},{"t":"Decides who must return or delete data, and how many contracts you keep","u":""},{"t":"Q-083, Q-103, Q-075, Q-086, Q-087","u":""}],[{"t":"9","u":""},{"t":"Whether all sites run under the same legal entity","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether a merge changes the controller","u":""},{"t":"Q-216, Q-071","u":""}],[{"t":"10","u":""},{"t":"How each address on each email list joined, and for which sender","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether lists can be combined","u":""},{"t":"Q-059, Q-060","u":""}],[{"t":"11","u":""},{"t":"Which trackers run before a choice on each site, and whether the notice matches","u":""},{"t":"Decides what to strip before you park a site","u":""},{"t":"Q-178, Q-181","u":""}],[{"t":"12","u":""},{"t":"Whether a domain is used for account logins, password resets or customer replies","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether you renew it or let it expire","u":""},{"t":"Technical, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"13","u":""},{"t":"Whether invoices or tax records live inside the product","u":""},{"t":"Decides what you keep after shutdown and for how long","u":""},{"t":"Q-145","u":""}]]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[],"children":[{"h":"Keep data only as long as you need it","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Personal data must be kept no longer than needed for its purpose. Your notice must say how long you keep it, or the criteria that decide the period. You must know the period for each purpose and data set.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"A shut-down product has no purpose left for most of its data. A parked site that still stores form entries keeps a purpose you no longer have.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 5(1)(e), 13(2)(a) and 14(2)(a).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-04.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Erasure, and what you may still keep","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Erase personal data without undue delay when an Article 17(1) ground applies. One ground is that the data are no longer needed for the purpose you collected them for. Article 17(3) lets you keep what is necessary for a legal duty or for legal claims. Keep only what that exception actually needs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Limits.","t":"\"We might be sued one day\" is not enough on its own. Invoices and tax records usually fall under a legal duty, which your accountant confirms (Q-145).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 17(1)(a) to (f), 17(3)(a) to (e), 5(1)(c) and (e), and 12(4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"A small suppression record can outlive the list","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"When someone objected to marketing, you must stop. A narrow suppression record can stop a re-import of that address later. It needs its own documented basis, minimal data and a retention limit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"If you delete a whole list at shutdown, you also delete the record of who said no. If you later merge another list that holds the same people, they get mail again.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 21(2) to (5), 12(4) to (5), 5(1)(b) to (e) and 6(1). Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 13(2) and (4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-EMAIL-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Your vendors must return or delete the data when the service ends","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"A vendor that handles personal data for you is usually your processor, and that needs a written contract. At the end of the service, you choose return or deletion. The vendor deletes existing copies unless law requires it to keep them.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"What to check.","t":"The DPA covers the exit. Backups are inside the deletion. You get a confirmation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 4(7), 4(8), 28(3) opening sentence, 28(3)(g), 28(9) and 28(10).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Fewer vendors means fewer contracts to check","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Each processor needs Article 28 terms. Sub-processor changes need your authorisation, with notice and a chance to object. Your duty to check a processor's guarantees continues after you sign. Review service by service against your real data flows.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"Every vendor you drop when you park or shut a site is one less DPA, one less sub-processor list and one less exit plan to keep current.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 28(1) to (4) and 28(9). EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, paragraphs 94 to 99, 112 to 114 and 143 to 145.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Merging can change who the controller is and what people are told","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Your notice names the controller and its contact details, each purpose and its basis, the recipients and any third-country transfer. When a merge changes any of these, the notice on the site you keep must change too.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"If the entity changes.","t":"If the merged site runs under a different legal entity (for example an obrt moving work into a new d.o.o.), the new controller receives data it did not collect. Article 14 information is then due within a reasonable time and no later than one month, or at the first communication if that comes sooner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"If only the site changes.","t":"If the same obrt runs both sites, the controller stays the same. You still update purposes, recipients and retention on the notice you keep (Q-080).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 13(1)(a) to (f), 14(1)(a) to (f), 14(3) to (4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Reusing data on the merged site needs a compatibility check","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"If the merged site uses old data for a new purpose, and you do not rely on consent or a law for that, assess whether the new purpose is compatible with the original one. Look at the link between purposes, the collection context, the kind of data, the consequences and your safeguards. A new notice alone does not make a new purpose compatible. You tell people before the new use.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Example.","t":"Accounts from the tool at yourproduct.com used to send course offers from yourdomain.com. That is a new purpose. It needs its own check, and for email it also needs send permission (next section).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 5(1)(b), 6(4)(a) to (e), 13(3) and 14(4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"F-GDPR-BASIS-M02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Email permission does not move with the list","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Consent to marketing was given to one sender for what that sender described. The customer exception lets a trader email its own consumers about its own similar products, with a free objection at collection and in every message. Merging two lists does not extend either permission to the other brand's offers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Evidence.","t":"You must be able to show consent. If you close a newsletter tool, export how each contact joined before you cancel the account. New copy cannot recreate old consent.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 13(1) and (2). CJEU, Inteligo Media, C-654/23, paragraphs 38, 47 to 48 and 63. ZEK, NN 76/2022, Article 50(2). GDPR Articles 4(11) and 7(1) to (4).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-EMAIL-02, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01, F-EMAIL-05.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Paid customers: what you promised still counts","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"For consumer subscriptions you had to disclose cost per billing period, duration, renewal and termination conditions and any minimum commitment. Croatian Article 60 covers the same ground. Those terms are your starting point when you end a product.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Remedies stay separate.","t":"EU digital-content rules give remedies when digital supply fails or does not conform. These are separate from the 14-day withdrawal right. A customer who paid for a year and gets four months may have a remedy for the rest.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Gap.","t":"The kit has no claim yet on what refund is owed when you, the trader, end a prepaid consumer plan early. A pro-rata refund or running the service to the end of the paid term is the cautious practical choice. Ask counsel before you announce dates. No claim id yet.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Directive 2011/83/EU (consolidation of 27 September 2026), Article 6(1)(e), (o) and (p), and Article 8(2). Directive (EU) 2019/770, Articles 1, 13 to 14 and 22. Zakon o izmjenama i dopunama Zakona o zaštiti potrošača, NN 59/2026, Article 24 (new Article 60).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-CONSUMER-07, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-04, F-CONSUMER-11.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"A parked page still needs consent for any tracker on it","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Storing or reading information on a visitor's device needs informed consent, unless a narrow exemption applies. First-party analytics are not strictly necessary just because you value them. AZOP says non-essential analytics and marketing cookies stay off until valid consent. Your policy must match what the site actually loads.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"The good news.","t":"A site that uses only technically necessary cookies does not need a banner asking people to accept cookies. It still needs clear information about the cookies it uses. Strip the trackers and the banner can go.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 5(3). WP29 Opinion 04/2012, sections 4.2 to 4.3. EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paragraphs 6, 30 to 40 and 46 to 55. AZOP cookie guidance (2026) and recommendation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-DEVICE-01, F-DEVICE-13, F-DEVICE-14, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Trader information on every site you keep","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Croatian law requires provider identity, obrt or company seat, an effective contact including email, and any registration, supervisory, professional and VAT details, directly and permanently accessible. The EU rule is the same in outline.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"When you merge, the imprint on the surviving site must cover the business behind everything it now sells. A shared imprint page linked from every live site is the simplest way to keep one version true (Q-222).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, Article 6(1). Directive 2000/31/EC, Article 5(1)(a) to (g) and 5(2).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, F-ECOMMERCE-02.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Technical standards, not law","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Null MX","t":"(RFC 7505, section 3). MX 0 . says a domain takes no mail. It does not stop anyone spoofing the domain in a From address.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"SPF","t":"(RFC 7208). v=spf1 -all says no server may send for the domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"DMARC","t":"(RFC 9989). p=reject asks receivers to reject mail that fails. Final handling is left to the receiver. When sp is absent, p applies to subdomains.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Together.","t":"Null MX, -all and p=reject reduce misuse of the exact domain. They do nothing about lookalike domains or display-name abuse. UC-04 step 7 has the full setup and the wildcard caveat.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each step says how you verify it, and what an outside check can show. An outside check reads public DNS and loads public pages. It sees mail DNS, third-party requests, device storage in three consent states, forms and where they post, notice and imprint links, and hosting headers. It cannot see revenue, users, your hours, what sits in your databases, or your contracts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Run the outside check on every domain.","t":"One pass gives you notes across the whole portfolio.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For each domain: nslookup for MX, SPF and _dmarc, then a fresh private window with DevTools open. The README has the steps.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: your notes have a section for every domain you own. Compare the list with your registrar's domain list, so nothing is missing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: trackers, storage, forms, mail DNS and hosting per site. List every vendor you see.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Fill the one-page inventory.","t":"One row per site or product. Use the template below. Copy the observed columns from the report. Fill money, users and hours yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Why: a factual inventory of forms, scripts, suppliers, purposes and retention comes before any notice you write (F-GDPR-NOTICE-09).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: every domain in the report has a row, and every row has all five decision facts.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: fills the observed columns. The Questions page shows which questions are still open.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Label each row.","t":"Use the decision rule below. Write the date next to the label.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: no row is unlabelled. Any row you could not decide is labelled park.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: nothing. This is your call.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Park first.","t":"It is the fastest win. For each parked site, remove analytics, pixels, embeds and forms. Leave a short static page with a link to your main site, its notice and its imprint. Cancel the vendor accounts the page no longer uses.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: repeat the outside check on that domain. Zero third-party requests before a choice, and no form posting anywhere. If you keep any optional tool, test that it stops after reject and after withdrawal (Q-189).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: third parties, device storage and forms per site.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Plan each shutdown.","t":"Use the shutdown checklist below. Paid customers come first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: each shutdown row has a dated notice, an export window, a refund decision and a deletion date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: nothing until the site goes offline. Then it confirms the domain serves only a redirect or a parked page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Merge last.","t":"Merging touches notices, lists and sometimes the controller. Do it after the simpler moves have cut the noise.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the surviving site's notice names every purpose, recipient and retention period it now has. Old URLs return a permanent redirect to the right page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: notice and imprint links present on the surviving site, and the old domain shows a redirect.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Retire domains and mail.","t":"Use \"Retiring a domain\" below.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: from an outside account, send to an old address and check the result matches the path you chose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: MX, null MX, SPF, DMARC p and sp, and wildcard behaviour.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Close vendor accounts and collect deletion confirmations.","t":"Export what you must keep first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: a dated confirmation of deletion, or of return, for each vendor you dropped, stored with your records.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: fewer vendors load when you repeat it. It cannot see contracts or confirmations.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Repeat the whole outside check and compare.","t":"Keep the before and after reports side by side.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: fewer sites, fewer vendors, fewer findings. No new findings on parked domains.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: the full set again.","lk":[]}],"children":[{"h":"Decision rule","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Start at the top. Take the first label that fits.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Label","u":""},{"t":"When it fits","u":""},{"t":"What happens next","u":""}],[{"t":"Keep","u":""},{"t":"It earns money or has active users, and you can maintain it within your monthly time budget","u":""},{"t":"Fix its findings. See UC-14 for an order","u":""}],[{"t":"Merge","u":""},{"t":"It serves the same audience as a site you keep, and its content or users would fit there","u":""},{"t":"Move content and users, redirect, update the notice, then shut the old one","u":""}],[{"t":"Park","u":""},{"t":"No money and no active users, but you want the domain or the idea for later","u":""},{"t":"Static page, no trackers, no forms, no data collection","u":""}],[{"t":"Shut down","u":""},{"t":"No money, few or no users, and it costs you time, holds data or carries vendors","u":""},{"t":"Shutdown checklist below","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Two tie-breakers. If you cannot decide, park. If a site holds data you cannot explain, it moves up the list, because it carries risk without paying for it.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"One-page inventory","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Copy this into a file next to your report. No passwords, no customer data, only counts.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Field","u":""},{"t":"Example row","u":""}],[{"t":"Site or product","u":""},{"t":"Subscription tool","u":""}],[{"t":"Domains","u":""},{"t":"yourproduct.com, app.yourproduct.com","u":""}],[{"t":"What it does, in one line","u":""},{"t":"Yearly plan for a small online tool","u":""}],[{"t":"Money in, last 12 months","u":""},{"t":"EUR amount from your books","u":""}],[{"t":"Active users","u":""},{"t":"Count of logins in the last 90 days","u":""}],[{"t":"Paying customers with time left","u":""},{"t":"Count, and the latest end date","u":""}],[{"t":"Consumers, businesses or both","u":""},{"t":"Both","u":""}],[{"t":"Hours per month","u":""},{"t":"Your honest estimate","u":""}],[{"t":"Data held","u":""},{"t":"Accounts, emails, payment references","u":""}],[{"t":"Where the data lives","u":""},{"t":"Hosting, database, mail tool, payment provider (from the Vendors register)","u":""}],[{"t":"Forms","u":""},{"t":"2 (from the report)","u":""}],[{"t":"Trackers before a choice","u":""},{"t":"1 (from the report)","u":""}],[{"t":"Sends email as","u":""},{"t":"yourproduct.com","u":""}],[{"t":"Used for logins or password resets","u":""},{"t":"Yes, two vendor accounts","u":""}],[{"t":"Legal surface count","u":""},{"t":"Number of forms, trackers, vendors, paid customers and sending domains","u":""}],[{"t":"Label and date","u":""},{"t":"Merge, 2026-11-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Next step","u":""},{"t":"Move users to yourdomain.com, notice update, redirect","u":""}]]}]},{"h":"Shutdown checklist","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Do these in order. Stop and ask a specialist if a step does not fit.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Stop new sign-ups and renewals.","t":"Turn off automatic renewal in your payment provider so no one is charged for time you will not deliver.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Decide what paid customers get.","t":"Read what you promised on duration and termination (F-CONSUMER-07, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-04). Choose a refund for unused paid time or run the service to the end of the term. Ask counsel first (no claim id yet).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Tell users, with a date.","t":"Say when the service stops, how to export their data, what happens to unused paid time and how to reach you. Keep it a service message. Do not add an offer for another product unless you hold send permission for it (Q-058).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Give an export window.","t":"Long enough that a busy person can act. Test the export yourself.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Sort the data into three piles.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Delete: data with no purpose left (F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Keep under a legal duty: invoices and tax records, for the period your accountant confirms (F-GDPR-RIGHTS-08, F-TAX-05, Q-145).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Keep minimal: a suppression record of people who objected to marketing (F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Export what you keep, then ask each vendor for deletion.","t":"Under Article 28(3)(g) you choose return or deletion (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07). Include backups. Save each confirmation.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Remove the product from your notice.","t":"Update the notice on every site that mentioned it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Take the site down.","t":"Point the domain at a short page or a redirect to your main site.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"Retire the domain.","t":"See the next section.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Tell your accountant.","t":"A product that ends changes your revenue lines and may change your obrt's activity (Q-153).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Retiring a domain","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Pick one of two paths for each domain. Write the choice in the inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Path A, transition.","t":"Keep the MX records and one alias, such as hello@yourproduct.com, that delivers into your main mailbox. Reply from your main address so people learn it. Keep this for a period you choose, then move to path B.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Path B, non-mail domain.","t":"When you confirm no tool sends as the domain and no one still writes to it: null MX 0 ., SPF v=spf1 -all and DMARC p=reject. Remove old SPF includes and DKIM keys for tools you dropped. Check for a wildcard first, as UC-04 step 7 explains.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Then decide renew or expire.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Renew","t":"any domain that ever carried customer mail, account logins or password resets. Renew for several years and enable auto-renew. It is cheap insurance.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Let expire","t":"only a domain that never sent or received mail and was never used for a login. Before that, move every account (registrar, hosting, payment provider, app stores, social profiles) off addresses at the domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why.","t":"When a domain expires, anyone can register it. The new owner then receives mail sent to the old addresses, including password reset links and customer replies.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Deleting the list and the suppression record together.","t":"People who said no come back on the next import.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Merging two newsletters into one.","t":"Each list joined for one sender and one topic. Ask for permission again, or keep them apart (F-EMAIL-02, N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A shutdown email that sells.","t":"\"We are closing, try our other product\" can turn a service message into marketing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Parking a site but leaving the analytics tag.","t":"The tag still sets cookies and still needs consent. The banner then has to stay too.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Leaving forms live on a parked page.","t":"People keep submitting, and you keep collecting data with no purpose.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Forgetting the vendor after the site is gone.","t":"The form tool or mail tool still holds the data, and the DPA still runs.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Asking for deletion before exporting what you must keep.","t":"Invoices go with it. Export first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Letting a domain expire with logins still on it.","t":"A new owner can reset your passwords.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Believing null MX and p=reject stop all spoofing.","t":"They protect the exact domain only.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"A stale SPF include on the main domain.","t":"A tool you dropped stays authorised to send as you.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Merging into the site with the weakest notice.","t":"Pick the surviving site's notice on purpose and rewrite it for the merged purposes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Assuming the controller is the same after a merge.","t":"It is the same only if the same legal entity runs both sites.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating \"free\" as \"no obligations\".","t":"A free product with accounts still holds personal data and still needs a clean exit.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Read-only by default. Propose changes as a diff for the owner to approve. Never delete production data, cancel a vendor or send a customer email. Drafts only, a human sends.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Run one multi-site check and keep the report.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For each domain: nslookup for MX, SPF and _dmarc, then a fresh private window with DevTools open. The README has the steps.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"From the outside check, build the observed inventory columns per domain: trackers before a choice, device storage, forms and their destinations, sending domains, Vendors register entries.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] List open questions for the owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Open the Questions page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Fill only what the owner's own files show (DNS exports, hosting project settings, form code, invoices). Mark each as agent_from_owner_files. Leave money, users and hours to the owner.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each site labelled park, search the code for analytics snippets, pixels, embeds and form endpoints. Propose one diff that removes them and leaves a static page with links to the main notice and imprint.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each site labelled merge, build a redirect map from old URLs to new ones. Flag any old URL with no good target.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each site labelled shut down, list every place data lives: database tables, storage buckets, mail tool lists, form tool entries, logs and backups. Mark each delete, keep under legal duty, or keep minimal. Do not delete anything.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Draft the customer notice as a service message. Include the stop date, export steps, the paid-time decision the owner made and a contact address. No offers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each retiring domain, record current MX, SPF, DMARC and DKIM values and TTLs before any change.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +noall +answer MX spare-domain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +short TXT spare-domain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"dig +short TXT _dmarc.spare-domain.com","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Probe for a wildcard with a random label: dig +short A zq7-check.spare-domain.com. If it resolves, flag \"wildcard likely\" and stop before proposing a null MX.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Flag any SPF include on a kept domain for a tool that only a retired product used.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] After the owner applies changes, re-run the same check and diff it against the first report.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"When I end a prepaid consumer subscription early, what must I refund, and how much notice must I give (Q-014, Q-016)? Does the answer change for business customers (Q-008, Q-161)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does a merge that moves users to a different legal entity need anything beyond the Article 14 notice (Q-216, Q-071)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"May the merged site use old accounts for a new purpose, given the compatibility factors in Article 6(4) (Q-074)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Can I combine two email lists, or must I ask for permission again (Q-059, Q-060, Q-062)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"What basis and retention period suit a suppression record kept after a list is deleted (Q-094)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which data from a shut-down product must I keep for a legal duty, and which can I delete now (Q-070, Q-092)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does a parked holding page that names my business still need a full imprint (Q-222)?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How long must I keep invoices, payment records and contracts from a product I close (Q-145)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does closing a product change my obrt's activity, VAT position or fiscalisation duties (Q-153)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How are refunds for unused paid time booked and invoiced?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"How do I book the end of annual vendor subscriptions I cancel early?","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Law, case law and official guidance (with claim ids)","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Claim ids","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)","u":""},{"t":"Articles 4(7), 4(8), 4(11), 5(1)(b) to (e), 6(1), 6(4), 7, 12(4) to (5), 13, 14, 17(1) and (3), 21(2) to (5), 28(1) to (4), 28(3)(g), 28(9), 28(10)","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-01, F-GDPR-NOTICE-03, F-GDPR-NOTICE-04, F-GDPR-NOTICE-07, F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-BASIS-M02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-07, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-08, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-14, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-01, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-04, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-07, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01, F-EMAIL-05","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 94 to 99, 112 to 114, 143 to 145","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-M01","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC, consolidated 19 December 2009","u":""},{"t":"Articles 5(3), 13(1), (2) and (4)","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-01, F-EMAIL-02, F-EMAIL-08","u":""}],[{"t":"CJEU, Inteligo Media, C-654/23, 13 November 2025","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 38, 47 to 48, 63","u":""},{"t":"F-EMAIL-02","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama, NN 76/2022","u":""},{"t":"Article 50(2)","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-CUSTOMER-01","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2011/83/EU, consolidation of 27 September 2026","u":""},{"t":"Article 6(1)(e), (o), (p), Article 8(2)","u":""},{"t":"F-CONSUMER-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive (EU) 2019/770 (digital content)","u":""},{"t":"Articles 1, 13 to 14, 22","u":""},{"t":"F-CONSUMER-11","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o izmjenama i dopunama Zakona o zaštiti potrošača, NN 59/2026, item 728","u":""},{"t":"Article 24, new Article 60(1)(15), (18), (21) to (25), 60(3) to (5), Article 66","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-04","u":""}],[{"t":"WP29 Opinion 04/2012 on cookie consent exemption","u":""},{"t":"Sections 4.2 to 4.3","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-13","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 on Article 5(3)","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 6, 30 to 40, 46 to 55","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-14","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP cookie guidance (2026) and recommendation","u":""},{"t":"As cited in N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-06, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, item 2504","u":""},{"t":"Article 6(1)","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2000/31/EC","u":""},{"t":"Article 5(1)(a) to (g), 5(2)","u":""},{"t":"F-ECOMMERCE-02","u":""}],[{"t":"VAT Directive 2006/112/EC","u":""},{"t":"Articles 196, 219a","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-05","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"All claims above are draft research with legal review not requested, checked 2026-11-07. Croatian texts are researcher translations. The refund owed when a trader ends a prepaid consumer plan early has no claim id yet.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Technical standards (no claim ids)","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Status","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 7505 (null MX), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7505","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7505"},{"t":"Section 3","u":""},{"t":"Read, 2026-11-07, as cited in UC-04","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 9989 (DMARC), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9989","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9989"},{"t":"Sections 4.7, 4.10.1, 5.4","u":""},{"t":"Read in part, 2026-11-07, as cited in UC-04","u":""}],[{"t":"RFC 7208 (SPF), rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7208","u":"https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7208"},{"t":"-all mechanism","u":""},{"t":"Cited from knowledge, not fetched","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"id: UC-14","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"title: Where to start when it all feels wrong, your first hour, week and month","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"who: A small business owner in Croatia or elsewhere in the EU who runs a few sites, mailboxes and products, has never sorted privacy, email or consumer rules, and wants one calm place to begin.","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"countries: [HR, EU]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"questions: [Q-041, Q-043, Q-049, Q-051, Q-052, Q-058, Q-059, Q-060, Q-062, Q-073, Q-083, Q-085, Q-086, Q-089, Q-093, Q-095, Q-150, Q-161, Q-165, Q-178, Q-181, Q-216]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"claims: [F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-DEVICE-14, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-10, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-02, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04, F-CONSUMER-09, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, N-HR-AUTH-06, F-AI-07, F-TAX-06, F-TAX-09, N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-04]","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"status: draft, not legally reviewed","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"---","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]},"start":{"title":"Where to start when it all feels wrong, your first hour, week and month","sections":[{"h":"Facts that change the answer","lead":[{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"#","u":""},{"t":"Fact","u":""},{"t":"Why it changes the answer","u":""},{"t":"Question id","u":""}],[{"t":"1","u":""},{"t":"Which sites and tools collect data about people, and what they collect","u":""},{"t":"Decides where your first fixes go","u":""},{"t":"Q-073","u":""}],[{"t":"2","u":""},{"t":"What runs before a visitor makes a choice","u":""},{"t":"The most common finding, and the fastest to fix","u":""},{"t":"Q-178","u":""}],[{"t":"3","u":""},{"t":"Whether your notice matches what the site actually loads","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether you rewrite the notice or just trim the site","u":""},{"t":"Q-181","u":""}],[{"t":"4","u":""},{"t":"Which offer brings in the money","u":""},{"t":"That offer's checkout, form, mail and domain get protected first","u":""},{"t":"Business fact, no kit question yet","u":""}],[{"t":"5","u":""},{"t":"Whether you sell to consumers, businesses or both","u":""},{"t":"Consumer rules apply only to consumers","u":""},{"t":"Q-051, Q-161","u":""}],[{"t":"6","u":""},{"t":"Whether the site concludes contracts or only informs","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether checkout and withdrawal rules come into play","u":""},{"t":"Q-052, Q-165","u":""}],[{"t":"7","u":""},{"t":"Whether you act commercially, including through ads","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether trader information is needed","u":""},{"t":"Q-049","u":""}],[{"t":"8","u":""},{"t":"Your legal form (obrt, d.o.o., other)","u":""},{"t":"Decides imprint fields and tax questions","u":""},{"t":"Q-216","u":""}],[{"t":"9","u":""},{"t":"Whether your marketing list has permission you can show","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether you may keep mailing it","u":""},{"t":"Q-059, Q-060","u":""}],[{"t":"10","u":""},{"t":"Whether an unsubscribe in one tool reaches every tool","u":""},{"t":"Decides whether an objection is really honoured","u":""},{"t":"Q-062","u":""}],[{"t":"11","u":""},{"t":"Which vendors can reach your data, and whether their terms bind your account","u":""},{"t":"Decides your first vendor paperwork","u":""},{"t":"Q-083, Q-085, Q-086","u":""}],[{"t":"12","u":""},{"t":"Whether anyone has asked about their data or objected to marketing","u":""},{"t":"These have a clock, so they jump the queue","u":""},{"t":"Q-089, Q-093, Q-095","u":""}],[{"t":"13","u":""},{"t":"Whether you have fewer than 10 staff and stay under the financial thresholds","u":""},{"t":"May take one whole regime off your list","u":""},{"t":"Q-041, Q-043","u":""}],[{"t":"14","u":""},{"t":"Whether you must issue eRačuni from 1 January 2027","u":""},{"t":"A near date for your accountant","u":""},{"t":"Q-150","u":""}]]}],"children":[]},{"h":"What may apply","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Only the rules that set the order are here. Each module has the detail.","lk":[]}],"children":[{"h":"A few things have a clock","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Answer a request about personal data without undue delay and within one month. Explain any extension within that first month. When someone objects to direct marketing, stop that marketing. There is no balancing test. Report a personal-data breach to the competent authority without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours, unless it is unlikely to put people at risk. In Croatia that authority is usually AZOP, but check that first.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"These are the only items in this module that cannot go on a \"later\" list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 12(3) to (4), 21(2) to (5) and 33(1). AZOP breach-reporting page.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, N-HR-AUTH-06.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Trackers before a choice come first","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"AZOP says non-essential analytics and marketing cookies stay off until valid consent. It recommends a technical inventory of cookies and tracking tools, and your policy must match what the site does. Ask what each tool reads, writes and sends, and test before and after a choice.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"An outside check sees this directly, the fix is usually small, and every visitor benefits right away.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"AZOP cookie guidance (2026) and recommendation. EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, paragraphs 6, 30 to 40 and 46 to 55.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08, F-DEVICE-14.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"An inventory comes before a notice","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Build a factual list of forms, scripts, suppliers, purposes and retention first. Then write a short, clear notice from it. Review vendors service by service against those real data flows.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"Rewriting a notice before you know what the site does wastes an afternoon. The outside check is most of your inventory.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"GDPR Articles 5(2), 12(1), 13, 14 and 28. EDPB Guidelines 07/2020, paragraphs 112 to 114 and 143 to 145.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Marketing email needs permission you can show","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"In Croatia, email promotion to individuals needs prior consent, with separate exceptions for your own customers and for legal persons. Every marketing message needs a clear sender and a free way to stop. Where you rely on consent, you must be able to show it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"Before you send the next campaign, check you can show how each person joined. UC-05 has the full routes.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"ZEK, NN 76/2022, Article 50(1), (3) and (4). Directive 2002/58/EC, Article 13(4). GDPR Articles 4(11) and 7.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05, F-EMAIL-05, F-EMAIL-06.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Trader information on every site you keep","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Show who you are, your obrt or company seat, a working email and any registration, supervisory, professional and VAT details, directly and permanently accessible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, Article 6(1).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Checkout rules already in force for consumer sales","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"Since 19 June 2026, a covered online consumer contract needs a prominent withdrawal function during the withdrawal period, a confirmation step and a prompt acknowledgement on a durable medium with the submission date and time.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"If your money offer sells to consumers online, this belongs in your first month. UC-02 walks through a subscription checkout.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o izmjenama i dopunama Zakona o zaštiti potrošača, NN 59/2026, item 728, Article 28 (new Article 81a) and Article 66. Directive (EU) 2023/2673, Article 1(2) to (3), inserting CRD Article 11a.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claims.","t":"N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04, F-CONSUMER-09.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Dates in the next two months","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"These come from claim records with an effective date. The Stay aligned page in the guide shows them filtered by your answers.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Date","u":""},{"t":"What happens","u":""},{"t":"Who it affects","u":""},{"t":"Claim id","u":""},{"t":"Module","u":""}],[{"t":"17 November 2026","u":""},{"t":"New Croatian duty to publish current product price lists on your website. The publication method is left to a ministerial rule that is not verified yet","u":""},{"t":"Traders selling to Croatian consumers","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-10, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-02","u":""},{"t":"UC-02, UC-11","u":""}],[{"t":"2 December 2026","u":""},{"t":"End of the transition for marking AI-generated content, for providers whose system was on the market before 2 August 2026. Chatbot identification was not postponed","u":""},{"t":"Providers of AI systems that generate text, images, audio or video","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-07","u":""},{"t":"UC-07","u":""}],[{"t":"1 January 2027","u":""},{"t":"Covered taxpayers outside the VAT register start issuing eRačuni","u":""},{"t":"Many obrti and small businesses outside the VAT register","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-09","u":""},{"t":"UC-11","u":""}],[{"t":"1 January 2027","u":""},{"t":"EU OSS changes under ViDA start","u":""},{"t":"Sellers using or considering OSS","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-06","u":""},{"t":"UC-11","u":""}]]}]},{"h":"Some regimes may not apply to you at all","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Plain statement.","t":"The Croatian accessibility act exempts microenterprises that provide services. A microenterprise has average annual employment below 10 and stays within the prior-year revenue or asset threshold of up to EUR 2 million.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Why it matters here.","t":"If the exemption fits, you can move accessibility findings for your services from \"now\" to \"nice to have\". Confirm the facts first (Q-041, Q-043). Accessibility still helps your customers.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Source.","t":"Zakon o zahtjevima za pristupačnost proizvoda i usluga, NN 89/2025, item 1231, Article 4(2) and original Article 5 point 18 (current point 22 after NN 114/2026, item 1371).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Claim.","t":"N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-04.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"What to do, smallest first","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Each step says how you verify it, and what an outside check can show. Each result carries one of three labels: observed, needs your answer or needs a specialist. The first hour uses all three.","lk":[]}],"children":[{"h":"The first hour","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Minutes 0 to 10. Run the outside check on every domain.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For each domain: nslookup for MX, SPF and _dmarc, then a fresh private window with DevTools open. The README has the steps.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"While it runs, list every domain you pay for from your registrar. Add any you forgot and run again.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: your notes have a section for each domain you own.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: mail DNS, pages, third parties, device storage in three consent states, consent order, forms and hosting.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Next: if the list of domains surprises you, read UC-13. If you build sites for clients, run this on your own sites first, then see UC-01.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Minutes 10 to 20. List your mailboxes and aliases.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"One line per address: the address, mailbox or alias, which domain, who reads it and which tools send as it. No passwords.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: the list matches your mail host's admin console.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: MX, SPF, DMARC and known DKIM selectors per domain. It cannot see mailboxes or aliases.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Next: UC-04 turns this list into one inbox. UC-08 is for later, once the basics hold.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Minutes 20 to 30. Pick the one offer that pays you.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Name it. Write down its domain, its checkout or signup form, its confirmation email and the vendors it uses. This offer gets protected first. Everything else waits its turn.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: you can point to each of those four things in the report.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: shows the forms, trackers and vendors on that domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Next: UC-02 for a subscription, UC-03 for a free workshop that leads to a sale, UC-07 for an AI product, UC-11 for invoicing.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Minutes 30 to 40. Fix the top three findings.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Take the three observed findings on the money domain, in this order, and fix only those:","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":"1","b":"","t":"A tracker or cookie that fires before a choice. See UC-06. For referral scripts see UC-09. For quizzes and waitlists see UC-12.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":"2","b":"","t":"A form with no notice next to it, or a marketing box that is ticked by default. See UC-06, UC-03 and UC-12.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":2,"n":"3","b":"","t":"A mail DNS gap on the sending domain, such as no DMARC record. See UC-04 and UC-05.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Each step has a fix and a way to verify it. Hand them to your coding agent if you like.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: run the re-check command for each fix.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: repeat it to confirm each fix.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Minutes 40 to 50. Answer the open questions.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"The Questions page lists the open items.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Answer what you know. \"I don't know\" is a valid answer. It keeps the related checks visible, which is what you want.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: answers.json holds your answers, with the date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: fill in what you observed yourself and note where you saw it.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Minutes 50 to 60. Book your specialist questions.","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Copy every needs a specialist item into two lists, one for counsel and one for your accountant. Add the questions from the \"Ask a specialist\" section of each module you opened.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Book one call with each. Send the list ahead, so the call is short.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Verify: both calls are in your calendar with the list attached.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Outside check: nothing more. You have done the hour.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"The first week","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"One task a day. Each is small.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Repeat the outside check","t":"and compare with the first report. Enjoy the shorter list.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Label every site","t":"keep, merge, park or shut down. Park anything you are unsure about. See UC-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Park what you will not keep.","t":"Strip trackers and forms from parked sites. That removes findings without fixing them. See UC-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"One notice per kept site","t":", written from the inventory, plus trader information on every kept site (F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01). See UC-06.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"One real inbox.","t":"Turn role addresses into aliases and add DMARC at p=none with rua pointed at a reports alias. See UC-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Export your list evidence.","t":"For each marketing list, export how each person joined, and the unsubscribe list. Check that an unsubscribe in one tool reaches every tool (Q-062). See UC-05.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Set up the two clocks.","t":"Decide where a data request or objection lands, and write the one-month deadline on your calendar each time one arrives (F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02). Save the AZOP breach page in your bookmarks (N-HR-AUTH-06).","lk":[]}]},{"h":"The first month","blocks":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"1","b":"Week 2. Merge and shut down","t":"the sites you labelled. Paid customers first. See UC-13.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"2","b":"Week 2. Check the money offer's checkout","t":"if it sells to consumers online: the withdrawal function, its confirmation and the acknowledgement (N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04). See UC-02.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"3","b":"Before 17 November 2026.","t":"Ask counsel whether the new price-list duty covers your offer and how to publish it (N-HR-TRADER-INFO-10).","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"4","b":"Before 2 December 2026.","t":"If you provide an AI system that generates content, check content marking (F-AI-07). See UC-07.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"5","b":"Week 3. Vendor paperwork for the money offer.","t":"For each vendor it uses, save the DPA that binds your account, the sub-processor list and where data sits (F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15). See UC-10.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"6","b":"Week 3. Test one restore","t":"of your main database or site backup. See UC-10.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"7","b":"Week 4. Accountant call","t":"about eRačun from 1 January 2027 and OSS (F-TAX-09, F-TAX-06, Q-150). See UC-11.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"8","b":"Week 4. Tighten DMARC slowly","t":", only if reports show only your own senders. See UC-04.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"9","b":"End of month. Re-run everything.","t":"Compare with the hour-one report. Open the Stay aligned page and note the next three dated actions.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":"10","b":"Only then, the AI inbox helper.","t":"Once mail, notices and vendors are in order, see UC-08.","lk":[]}]},{"h":"Choosing what to ignore for now, safely","blocks":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Ignoring safely means writing it down with a date, not forgetting it. Put each finding in one of three boxes.","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Box","u":""},{"t":"What goes in it","u":""},{"t":"Examples","u":""}],[{"t":"Now","u":""},{"t":"Anything with a clock, anything that runs on visitors' devices before they choose, and anything on the money offer","u":""},{"t":"A data request, a marketing objection, a breach, a tracker before a choice, a form with no notice","u":""}],[{"t":"This month","u":""},{"t":"Fixes on kept sites that touch people's data or money, and dated items in the next two months","u":""},{"t":"Notice rewrite, imprint, list evidence, vendor DPAs, checkout withdrawal function","u":""}],[{"t":"Later, with a date","u":""},{"t":"Technical hardening that affects no person yet, findings on sites you will park or shut down, and regimes that may not apply to you","u":""},{"t":"DMARC p=quarantine, DKIM key length, findings on spare-domain.com, accessibility if the microenterprise exemption fits (N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-04)","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Three quick tests decide the box.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Is a real person affected today?","t":"If yes, it is not \"later\".","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Is there a date or a clock?","t":"If yes, put the date in your calendar now.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Will this site still exist next month?","t":"If no, park it instead of fixing it.","lk":[]}]}]},{"h":"Common traps","lead":[{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Trying to fix everything in the first hour.","t":"Three fixes is the plan. The rest has a box and a date.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Rewriting the privacy notice first.","t":"Trim the site, then write the notice from what is left.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Fixing findings on a site you are about to park.","t":"Park it, and the findings go away.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Treating \"I don't know\" as a failure.","t":"It is a valid answer, and it keeps the check visible.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Sending one more campaign while you sort permissions.","t":"Pause the campaign for a week. It costs less than mailing people who did not agree.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Ignoring a data request because it does not say \"GDPR\".","t":"It still counts. The month starts when it arrives.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Assuming every EU regime applies.","t":"Check scope first. Some, like accessibility for microenterprise services, may not.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Booking a specialist with no list.","t":"Send the questions ahead. The call gets shorter and cheaper.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"Adding an AI helper before the basics.","t":"It reads whatever your inbox holds. Get the inbox in order first.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"For your coding agent","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"","t":"Read-only by default. Propose changes as a diff for the owner to approve. Never submit forms, log in, send mail or claim a site is compliant.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Run the outside check on every domain the owner names.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":1,"n":null,"b":"","t":"For each domain: nslookup for MX, SPF and _dmarc, then a fresh private window with DevTools open. The README has the steps.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] From the outside check, list the three top observed findings on the owner's money domain, in this order: trackers before a choice, forms without notice or with a pre-ticked marketing box, mail DNS gaps on the sending domain.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] For each of the three, propose one diff and how to verify it. Stop after three.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Open the Questions page. Answer only from the owner's own files, and ask the owner to confirm each answer.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Collect every needs a specialist item into two Markdown lists, counsel and accountant, with the question ids.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] Draft a \"later\" list with a date on each item. Do not drop any finding.","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"[ ] After the owner applies the fixes, repeat the outside check and compare it with the first one.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Ask a specialist","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Counsel","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which of my findings carry the most risk, given that I sell to consumers, businesses or both (Q-051, Q-161)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does my site conclude contracts or only inform, and what follows from that (Q-052, Q-165)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do I act commercially in a way that needs a full imprint on every site (Q-049, Q-216)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Can I keep mailing my current list, or must I ask for permission again (Q-058, Q-059, Q-060)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does the price-list duty from 17 November 2026 cover my offer, and how must I publish it?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Does the microenterprise accessibility exemption fit my business (Q-041, Q-043)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Is AZOP my competent authority for a breach, or is another authority in charge?","lk":[]},{"k":"p","b":"Accountant","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Must I issue eRačuni from 1 January 2027, and what do I need to set up (Q-150)?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Do the OSS changes from 1 January 2027 affect me?","lk":[]},{"k":"li","l":0,"n":null,"b":"","t":"Which records must I keep from the products I sell, and for how long? See UC-11.","lk":[]}],"children":[]},{"h":"Sources","lead":[{"k":"p","b":"Law, case law and official guidance (with claim ids)","t":"","lk":[]},{"k":"tbl","rows":[[{"t":"Source","u":""},{"t":"Locator","u":""},{"t":"Claim ids","u":""}],[{"t":"Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)","u":""},{"t":"Articles 4(11), 5(2), 7, 12(1), 12(3) to (4), 13, 14, 21(2) to (5), 28(1) to (4), 28(9), 33(1)","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-NOTICE-09, F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-02, F-GDPR-RIGHTS-11, F-EMAIL-05, N-HR-AUTH-06","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 07/2020 on controller and processor","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 112 to 114, 143 to 145","u":""},{"t":"F-GDPR-PROCESSOR-15","u":""}],[{"t":"EDPB Guidelines 2/2023 on Article 5(3)","u":""},{"t":"Paragraphs 6, 30 to 40, 46 to 55","u":""},{"t":"F-DEVICE-14","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP cookie guidance (2026) and recommendation","u":""},{"t":"As cited in N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-05, N-HR-COOKIE-CONSENT-08","u":""}],[{"t":"AZOP breach-reporting page, azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/","u":"https://azop.hr/izvjescivanje-o-povredi-osobnih-podataka/"},{"t":"Heading and first substantive paragraph","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-AUTH-06","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkim komunikacijama, NN 76/2022","u":""},{"t":"Article 50(1), (3) and (4)","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-01, N-HR-EMAIL-NATURAL-05","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive 2002/58/EC, consolidated 19 December 2009","u":""},{"t":"Article 13(4)","u":""},{"t":"F-EMAIL-06","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o elektroničkoj trgovini, NN 173/2003, item 2504","u":""},{"t":"Article 6(1)","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-01","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o izmjenama i dopunama Zakona o zaštiti potrošača, NN 59/2026, item 728","u":""},{"t":"Article 4 (new Article 7(9) and (12)), Article 28 (new Article 81a), Article 66","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-TRADER-INFO-10, N-HR-CONSUMER-INFO-02, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04","u":""}],[{"t":"Directive (EU) 2023/2673","u":""},{"t":"Article 1(2) to (3), inserting CRD Article 11a, Article 2(1)","u":""},{"t":"F-CONSUMER-09, N-HR-CONSUMER-WITHDRAW-04","u":""}],[{"t":"AI Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, consolidated 27 July 2026","u":""},{"t":"Article 111(4), Article 50(1) to (4), Article 113","u":""},{"t":"F-AI-07","u":""}],[{"t":"Council Directive (EU) 2025/516 (ViDA)","u":""},{"t":"Articles 1 to 3, 6(1) to (3), 7","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-06","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o fiskalizaciji, NN 89/2025, item 1233","u":""},{"t":"Articles 2(1)(24), 38(1), 41, 47, 80","u":""},{"t":"F-TAX-09","u":""}],[{"t":"Zakon o zahtjevima za pristupačnost proizvoda i usluga, NN 89/2025, item 1231, amended by NN 114/2026, item 1371","u":""},{"t":"Article 4(2), original Article 5 point 18, current point 22","u":""},{"t":"N-HR-EAA-SCOPE-04","u":""}]]},{"k":"p","b":"","t":"All claims above are draft research with legal review not requested, checked 2026-11-07. Croatian texts are researcher translations. The ministerial rule on how to publish price lists is not verified.","lk":[]}],"children":[]}]}};
